(Phnom Penh): In order to take care of the precious arts left by Khmer ancestors, especially in the field of drama and drama to survive, the famous drama "Sad Family" will be performed at Chaktomuk Theater on the 23rd On March 24, for the Cambodian people to visit as well as dedicate to Professor Vireak Selpak, who left these works for the next generation of artists.
The play "The Story of a Sad Family" is written by the famous poet Hang Thorn Hak. This story became very popular throughout the country in the 1960s. But later, because some Cambodian children did not know or had watched, this unique drama "Sad Family Story" was re-organized by the Arts Action Organization in collaboration with the High School of Fine Arts for Cambodians, especially young people. Visit.
This story has an educational content, that is, it wants to show the differences that make this family life unhappy. But virtue and reconciliation put an end to this lineage and built a bright future.
Therefore, let the Cambodian people, especially the youth, visit to show their support for the work of our early heroes in the drama "Sad Family" which will be performed from March 23 to 24, 2019. This is at the Chaktomuk Theater.
