(Preah Sihanouk): Mr. Yon Min, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province, urged Anco Company to supply enough water to Sihanoukville Water Supply Authority to be able to distribute enough to the people in Preah Sihanouk Province.
The push was made on the evening of Sunday, March 10, 2019, when Mr. Yon Min inspected the condition of the clean water pool in Kbal Chhay area of Anco Company and inspected the water storage location in some places, including Plumbing at various locations in Sihanoukville to find out the specific causes of water shortages in some areas in Sihanoukville at present.
While urging Anco, the governor of Sihanoukville, he sought the intervention of the Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts to help solve this problem.
Please be informed that today, the water situation in Sihanoukville, some places have enough water, some places lack water. In this water-scarce area, some people have turned to digging wells to help with the clean water provided by the water utility, which is weak.
Opinions from some residents that in Sihanoukville there are two types of water supply: the state network and the Anco network. In both of these networks, people say that Anco's network has enough water, while the state's water network in some places does not have enough water.
Mr. Phorn Rattanak, Head of Sihanoukville Water Supply Authority, stated that at present, the Water Supply Authority accepts wholesale from Anco to distribute to the people.
He said that Sihanoukville needs about 40,000 cubic meters of water per day. Anco provides between 28,000 and 30,000 cubic meters of water. Insufficient supply is the reason for the shortage of water in some areas today.
Mr. Phorn Rattanak asked Anco to speed up the delivery of water to meet the actual needs of the people.
Sun Ngy, a representative of Anco, said that the company currently supplies about 30,000 cubic meters of water per day to the Sihanoukville Water Supply Authority. He said that there is no shortage of water in Kbal Chhay, but the reason for the insufficient supply of water may be due to the connection of the main pipe to the distribution station is not complete.
Mr. Sun Ngy confirmed that this problem today, the main network is working to solve this problem. He did not specify when the pipeline would be completed.
The purpose of this meeting is to review and discuss the progress of the implementation of cooperation under the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle (CLV DTA) after the 10th CLV DTA Summit in Hanoi, Vietnam. Aims to develop specific action plans and projects for the implementation of existing agreements and master plans.
At the meeting, the ministers of the three countries noted the amount of Vietnamese investment in Cambodia in 49 CLV DTA projects worth US $ 1.63 billion and the efforts of Cambodia and Vietnam to attract Invest more by signing the agreement on double taxation and the elimination of income-related taxes on March 31, 2018, while Laos is exchanging views on this issue.
In addition, to promote trade facilitation with other ASEAN countries, Cambodia has delegated the issuance of Certificate of Origin (CO) Form D (D) to the Department of Commerce in nine border provinces such as Pailin, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey. Oddor Meanchey, Ratanakiri, Mondulkiri, Tbong Khmum, Kratie and Stung Treng.
At the same time, the Ministers of the three countries also reviewed and approved the report prepared by the Prime Ministers of Cambodia, Laos and Vietnam with the following results:
* Appreciate the CLV Trade Fair held on March 7-10, 2019 with a total of 215 booths, of which 5 booths were provided to the provinces of Laos and Vietnam to showcase services and sell products Agriculture, handicrafts, food and beverage, souvenirs and construction materials, etc.
Assign the three countries to collect and update tourism data in the CLV DTA for scheduling meetings to finalize the master plan as soon as possible.
Exchange views on the feasibility of concluding a study report on the rubber industry development plan in the CLV DTA and an agreement to update data and information through key officials of the three countries.
Assign Vietnam the task of leading, storing and updating information on the CLV DTA website, and authorize the three institutions to co-host information that is unified, transparent and accurate.
* Recognize the importance of updating the CLV DTA 2010-2020 Master Plan for Economic Development to give a full picture, reflecting the real challenges and opportunities as well as the needs of the three countries in the context of new development. .
* Thank you Laos for hosting the Special Senior Officials Meeting to host the 11th CLV DTA Summit later this year and the 13th CLV DTA Joint Coordinating Committee Meeting in conjunction with the Summit. Officials and meetings of the four sub-committees in 2021.
