Too symphonic! A 9-year-old bricklayer enters a brick mill with her right arm amputated in Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province
(Central): A 9-year-old girl whose parents are bricklayers and she also works as a parent has an unfortunate incident in the hands of a brick grinder, causing a broken right arm to the armpit. Unimaginable. This horrible incident happened on March 9, 2019 at the brick kiln at Preah Prosop village, Preah Prosop commune, Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province.
According to the report of the local police officer, the victim girl named Chheng Srey Pheak, 9 years old, resided in Thmey Village, Krala Commune, Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province (injured right arm to armpit) with her father named Chheng Bunhom, 37 years old. Brick worker and mother Khim Channa, 33 years old, occupation: Brick worker, living in the same commune.
Moments later, when the brick cart was full, Chheng Bunhom dragged the cart to dry the sun, but when Chheng Bunhom was drying the bricks, he saw his daughter Chheng Srey Pheak put his right hand into the brick grinder. Chheng Bunhom and a nearby brick kiln worker took the victim to the District Referral Hospital, then the District Referral Hospital sent the victim to a hospital in Phnom Penh.
Please be informed that this kind of incident is not new, it is observed that getting involved in the brick mill is frequent, so it is hoped that the relevant authorities will strengthen this work to avoid this case again and again. The victim became paralyzed and had lifelong remorse.
