Foreign Business Investment Law Protects China's New High-Level Open Opinion (Video Inside) A new one that China is implementing to achieve high-quality development has not stopped at all.
More than 2,900 Chinese representatives are currently discussing a draft law on foreign investors' investment in Beijing. Both create a business environment with the rule of law, internationalization and facilitation.
In drafting the law on investment by foreign traders, China adheres to the principles of openness and transparency, based on the realities of the national situation and in line with international law on domestic and foreign investment.
The draft law on investment by foreign traders consists of six chapters: generalization, investment promotion, investment protection, investment management, legal responsibility and additional provisions, etc., which respond to the focus of the external environment. It also shows China's openness and self-confidence.
Analysts say the introduction of the Foreign Trade Investment Law aims to set the basic framework and rules for allowing foreign traders to invest, as well as to promote, support and control the investment of foreign traders in the future. If foreign traders face any related issues, they can be resolved with justice, equality and transparency in accordance with relevant Chinese laws.
