Battambang University and Battambang Pedagogical Institute sign a memorandum of understanding to share management experience and educational techniques
Mrs. Sieng Em Totim, Rector of the University of Battambang, Mr. Chum Sophal, Director of the Battambang Pedagogical Institute and many other government officials witnessed the ceremony.
The MoU signing ceremony was held on March 9, 2019 at the Battambang Pedagogical Institute.
This Memorandum of Understanding was prepared on the initiative and guidance of the leaders of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports in order to share the experience of management and technical work in higher education between the two higher education institutions in Battambang province.
The Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) also aims to provide cooperation and support for the development process of the Battambang Pedagogical Institute to be suitable as a higher education institution to provide training for 12 + 2 teachers and 12 + 4 student teachers to become qualified teachers. Biology and high national consciousness.
The two units agreed to cooperate on seven key activities, including:
1. Organizing joint research programs related to social sciences and applied sciences
2. Cooperation program on staff development related to educational evaluation and internal quality assurance
3. Providing technical support for agricultural education in agronomy and horticulture
4. Providing technical support on information technology and telecommunications and information technology
5. Provide technical support on administrative and financial management
6. Strengthen staff capacity building and professional development on STEM education, including physics, chemistry, biology, geology and mathematics
7. Staff transfer (pedagogical, student, exam supervisor, administrative staff and academic staff)
Please note that this Memorandum of Understanding is valid for 5 years from the date of signing.
The leaders of the two higher education institutions are committed to implementing this agreement to improve the quality of education and training of human resources in the northwestern region of Cambodia in accordance with the policy of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Strategy. Rectangle, the fourth phase in the sixth mandate of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
