(Pursat): Mr. Var Kimhong, Senior Minister in charge of Border Affairs, led a delegation from the Joint Committee on Border Affairs to inspect and determine the construction site of administrative infrastructure at the Thmor Da International Border Crossing in Pursat Province, opposite the Tha Sen checkpoint in Trat Province (Thailand). Located in Sangkum Thmey Village, Thmor Da Commune, Veal Veng District, Pursat Province.
The border inspection was held on March 08, 2019 with the participation of Mr. Mao Thunin, Governor of Pursat Province, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism, Working Group of the Joint Boundary Committee, Provincial and District Authorities, 3 Land Border Protection Corps, Communication Working Group. Boundaries and also representatives of the Special Economic Zone Development Company (MDS).
After verifying the map of the proposed construction of administrative infrastructure at the Thmar Da International Border Crossing, Mr. Var Kimhong authorized the Special Task Force to inspect the checkpoint of the 825th Border Guard Corps and continue to inspect the geographical situation. By defining the demarcation point for the construction of the border gate in an area of 14 hectares (fourteen hectares), which will be implemented in the near future.
Heng Sopheana, the governor of Veal Veng district, said that the area was originally a Khmer Rouge stronghold, fighting almost daily and no roads, so not many people came to live there.
He said that under the policy of turning the former battlefield into a development area, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has also started to put forward a plan for the development of Veal Veng district. Initially, demining forces were deployed to provide land for people to grow crops and avoid danger to their livelihoods.
In addition, the Royal Government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen also built an additional road, National Road 55, connecting National Road No. 5 in Pursat to the battlefield until the border crossing with Thailand. . The construction of this road is very difficult, having to cross the mountain range to be able to connect to the rocky border area.
More than 600 tricycle and tuk-tuk drivers rush to attend free road traffic training to prepare for driver's license exam
(Phnom Penh): 631 drivers of tricycles and motorcycle trailers in the morning of March 9, 2019 rushed to participate in free road traffic training to prepare for the driving test.
Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, confirmed that for the morning of March 9, 2019, 631 drivers of tricycles and trailers attended the free road traffic training. To prepare for the driving test, while last Saturday, there were only 215 people.
He added that the training course on road traffic law will take place every Saturday for two months from March 2 to May 4, 2019 at two locations, such as the driving license unit of the Department of Public Works and Transport. Phnom Penh, Street 598, Sangkat Chrang Chamres II, Khan Russey Keo and another location at the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh on National Road 6, Sangkat Prek Leap, Khan Chroy Changva.
It should be noted that the rush to participate in the free road traffic training course by the drivers of the above tricycles and motorcycle trailers was organized after the Phnom Penh Capital Administration issued a notification on the opening of the road traffic law training course. For free tricycle, motorcycle and tuk tuk drivers on March 1.
This announcement of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration confirms that in the past, most of the passengers in the business of transporting passengers in Phnom Penh have been driving on the road without a valid driver's license.
After completing the training, you can apply for the theory and steering test to get a "A" driver's license.
