Senior Minister Osman Hassan: We will strive to make Cambodia a large halal industrial economic zone in the coming years
(Phnom Penh): On behalf of the Cambodian Halal Product Inspection Committee and the Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia will strive to become a large halal industrial economic zone in the coming years. This face. This was stated by Mr. Osman Hassan, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions and Vice Chairman of the Cambodian Halal Product Inspection Committee.
Mr. Osman Hassan made the remarks at the closing ceremony of the third training course on the basics of halal standards in Cambodia on March 9, 2019 at the Modern 5 Center in Phnom Penh, which consists of participants from the leadership. Senior members of Cambodian Islam in all capitals and provinces, and leaders of the Cambodian Muslim Youth League in all capitals and provinces, as well as a total of 200 representatives of local enterprises.
Senior Minister Osman Hassan informed the importance of companies, factories, enterprises, products that meet the Cambodian halal standard, that although the number of Muslims in Cambodia is less than 1 million, the local consumer market may be limited, but Cambodia has a lot of Muslim tourists.
He said that the global Muslim customers are about 2 billion, a huge market target that they need to consume halal products. In addition, customers who need to use halal are the general population around the world, not just Muslims, because they understand the hygienic standards and quality of halal-certified products.
However, in order for the above expectations to be successful, good cooperation between the relevant ministries and institutions, especially the Cambodian Secretariat for Halal Specialization, as well as the Cambodian Committee for the Control of Halal Products, must accelerate and expand the dissemination of Cambodian halal. To factories, enterprises and local manufacturers more widely, in collaboration with relevant ministries.
On that occasion, Senior Minister Osman Hassan stressed that in addition to the Ministry and the Department of Commerce, the Department of Industry and Handicraft of Phnom Penh is also an important party to play a leading role in other provinces in providing cooperation on this case to promote Develop the halal industrial economy in Cambodia to grow further. Check out a collection of photos from international events on March 9, 2019! (Photo inside)
