(Phnom Penh): The Office of the Spokesperson of the Royal Government of Cambodia will hold a press conference on the outcome of the workshop on "Active Spokesperson Towards Effective Prestige, Honor of Provinces and Cities, Together with the Preservation of Sovereignty, Unity and Proud of the National Revival ”which took place in Sihanoukville and the new discoveries of development in this province.
1. Mr. Phay Siphan, Spokesman of the Royal Government. 2. Dr. Ros Chantraboth, Personal Adviser to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The purpose of this closed-door meeting is to discuss the Partnership Strategy for Cambodia's Development for the next five years (2019-2023) based on: First: The Rectangular Strategy Phase 4, which is the policy agenda. Socio-economics of the political program of the Royal Government, 6th legislature of the National Assembly, 2nd: Update and assessment of development situation and sectoral challenges, and 3rd: ADB 2030 Strategic Development Framework.
The meeting lasted throughout the day, with in-depth and frank discussions on honest partnerships in the areas of transportation, education and skills training, urban planning and management, natural resource and agriculture management, and public sector management. As well as the financial sector.
Mr. Vongsy Visoth stated that this meeting is really an important forum for discussion in the mechanism of the partnership between Cambodia and ADB, which is a real and credible development partner. He said that Cambodia wants to prioritize the use of ADB financing more clearly and directionally based on the Royal Government's strategic framework, policy framework and vision, especially the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 and Vision 2030.
In addition to considering the efficiency of use, Cambodia also wants to focus on the sustainability of the project to ensure that the resources that Cambodia receives ADB, are used properly and smartly to meet the needs of the country and can Meet its main priorities to achieve sustainable development.
Mr. Vongsey Visoth also asked the partners to change the way they used to work in investing. He also highlighted the integration of policies into formal development assistance (ODA) by linking policy frameworks and strategies from the sectoral level upwards with the investment framework to improve resource allocation efficiency.
Financing related to urban development requires an urban development master plan, strategic framework and investment plan. At the same time, all investment projects must be feasible and sustainable, especially the cost recovery plan must be considered to ensure justice between city dwellers and residents. Rural areas can benefit the general population, not just one group.
Similarly, from now on, all investments in the transport sector also need to have a master plan for the transport sector, and if we manage, allocate and use resources efficiently and correctly, and have good governance. Cambodia will have a better future.
The meeting also discussed the Development and Technical Assistance Program 2020-2022. It should be noted that from 1992 to January 2019, ADB provided co-financing to Cambodia for 160 development projects totaling approximately US $ 3.194 million, of which approximately 2,704 concessional loans. Million dollars and about 490 million dollars in grant financing.
