(Kratie): The Provincial Coordinating Committee of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle held a meeting in Kratie province on March 08, 2019, agreeing on 12 points for the development of the triangle. The meeting was attended by relevant officials from the three countries, led by Mr. Luramin, Undersecretary of State, Ministry of Interior of Cambodia.
The 12-point agreement for the 10th meeting of the Provincial Coordinating Sub-Committee for the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle includes:
1. The Provincial Coordinating Sub-Committee of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle (hereinafter referred to as the “Sub-Committee) convened the 10th Meeting of the Provincial Coordinating Sub-Committee for the Development Triangle Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam in the territory of Kratie Province, Cambodia.
3. The Commission welcomes and congratulates the outcome of the 10th Summit of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle and the official adoption of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Economic Linkage Master Plan to 2030. Held on March 31, 2018 in Hanoi, Socialist Republic of Vietnam.
4. The Sub-Committee is committed to continuing the cooperation so that the 13 provinces of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle can develop and contribute to the sustainable development of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle.
5. The Sub-Committee requested the governments of the three countries and development partners to continue to invest in and support joint development projects on physical and physical infrastructure in order to establish a consistent link between the provinces of the CLV-DTA, in particular; All three countries in general.
6. The Sub-Committee is committed to implementing the Action Plan for Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Economic Connectivity by 2030 "in accordance with the agreements agreed by the governments of the three countries and the legal documents of each country.
7. The Sub-Committee emphasized the importance of forging alliances between provinces in the CLV-DTA, which contributes to strengthening and supporting the implementation of the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle Socio-Economic Development Plan to 2020. And action plans for Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam economic connectivity by 2030.
Sub-Committee encourages local administrations, CLV-DTA and relevant authorities to cooperate and exchange necessary information on a regular basis to resolve issues and incidents affecting people, traders and investors in the border areas and to cooperate in The fight against all kinds of transnational crime within the jurisdiction in accordance with the laws and regulations of each country and the agreements of the governments of the three countries.
9. The Sub-Committee requested the governments of the three countries to continue to promote cooperation in the implementation of the Agreement on Trade Facilitation and Promotion in the Cambodia-Laos-Vietnam Development Triangle.
10. The Sub-Committee reviewed and decided that the Chairman of the Cambodian Provincial Coordinating Sub-Committee would report the results to the Senior Officials Meeting.
11. The Sub-Committee thanked and commended the Government of the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Kratie Provincial Administration for the warm hospitality and excellent arrangements for this meeting.
Sub-Committee welcomes the 11th Meeting of the Provincial Coordinating Sub-Committee to be held in Laos at an appropriate time.
