Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, March 8: 755 illegal vehicles found and 507 fined
(Phnom Penh): Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign For March 8, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 5,512 vehicles, found 755 vehicles violated the law (72% motorcycles), educated 248 vehicles and fined 507 units, according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
For the results of the 8-day inspection from March 1 to 8, 2019, the police inspected 29,937 vehicles and found 5,208 offending vehicles (78% motorcycles), including education 1,701 units and fines of 3,501 units. Thmda Special Economic Zone Development Company and Tycoon Try Pheap Donate $ 120,000 to Support Cyclo Fund
(Phnom Penh): The Thmda Special Economic Zone Development Company in Veal Veng District, Pursat Province, and Tycoon Try Pheap, General Director of Try Pheap Group, have donated 120,000 USD to the Cyclo Fund of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. Difficult and improve the lives of cyclo drivers.
This support was made during a get-together and a refreshing meal between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and about 320 people in the Royal Government's cyclo-taxi operators at the Koh Pich Exhibition and Convention Center on Friday, March 8, 2019.
Tycoon Try Pheap told Fresh News that this support is a contribution to Samdech Techo Hun Sen to alleviate the difficulties of cyclo drivers. Tycoon Try Pheap added that his company, as well as himself, has always supported and contributed to the Royal Government to solve social problems through humanitarian activities.
After maintaining commitment to buy S-400, Turkey participates in more military exercises with Russia in the Black Sea
The Russian Navy in the Black Sea region, along with the Turkish navy, has led a joint naval exercise aimed at developing interoperability capabilities to respond to risks in the Black Sea. This is according to a statement from the Russian Navy quoted by Sputnik on Friday, March 8, 2019.
According to Rulyov, the two countries' navies will also conduct drills through the danger zone with landmines. It was an operation that came after Russia reaffirmed its commitment to defend its contract to buy S-400 missile defense systems from Russia in the face of growing warnings from the United States and NATO. .
