(Phnom Penh): In response to the concerns of cyclo drivers in Cambodia, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, reiterated his position that as long as Samdech remains the Prime Minister, the Cyclo Fund should not be lost.
The announcement of Samdech Techo Hun Sen was made on March 08, 2019, when Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with more than 300 cyclo drivers at Koh Pich Center.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that in the past, some people have accused Samdech of holding a referendum on the cyclo regime. Samdech also asked how to conduct a referendum if after the day of national liberation, Samdech has been doing humanitarian work forever, not snatching, but regularly by creating a fund for long-term insurance.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated: "It can also be seen that if Hun Sen is no longer the Prime Minister, it can be said that it will also disappear, because if you all no longer need me. "Do I need to continue to do it? Let the next prime minister do the work. If I remain the prime minister of the CPP, I understand that this fund should not be lost."
Please note that the Cycro Foundation has been announced to be implemented by Samdech Techo Hun Sen from January 13, 2018 onwards. The announcement to establish and implement the Cyclo Fund was made at the Plenary Meeting of the Council of Ministers on Friday, January 12, 2018. This is according to the results of the Cabinet meeting on the afternoon of January 12, 2018.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that the establishment of this fund not only helps the livelihood of the cyclo people, but also contributes to the preservation of the cyclo, which is the vehicle of Khmer identity since the French era.
Both the cyclo driver and the informal economy association have expressed support for Samdech Techo Hun Sen's initiative. The cyclo riders expressed their happiness and called for all these actions to help his livelihood and also to help keep the cyclo present in Cambodia.
