This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen invited to have a chat with the cyclo drivers
(Phnom Penh): On Friday, March 8, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, will hold a get-together with more than 300 cyclo riders. At Koh Pich Center.
This morning's social gathering and refreshments is a gesture of high regard for the well-being of cyclo riders from the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia.
The cyclo business, which dates back to the French colonial era, has made it difficult for riders to find riders, as is the case today due to the abundance of means of transportation. The lack of riders makes it difficult for most of the elderly cyclo riders to earn enough money to support themselves.
Seeing the challenges of cyclo riders as well as maintaining the identity of the cyclo, one of Cambodia's vehicles, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to establish the "Tricycle Fund" or "Cyclo Fund" in January 2018. Samdech Techo Hun Sen dropped about $ 140,000 into the fund and continued to deposit about $ 20,000 a month.
Through the fund, it has contributed to solving some of the difficulties of cyclo drivers and helping to raise the hard-earned money from cyclo cycling left to support livelihoods. However, cyclo riders in Phnom Penh continue to face difficulties because there is no suitable place to sleep, continuing to sleep on the porch of their homes.
