(Phnom Penh): The Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC) has issued a statement thanking Kong Vibol, the Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, for his efforts in facilitating tax issues. In the garment industry to maintain the growth and competitiveness of the industry.
In a statement obtained by Fresh News on the morning of March 8, it was stated that during the meeting between the association's representative with Mr. Kong Vibol and his officials at the General Department of Taxation, the association requested a solution to four issues: Below:
1: Tax audit once a year 2: Make tax holiday a reality for qualified projects 3: Tax exemption for seniority payments under the Labor Law Recent Amendments 4: Complete elimination of 1% income tax exemption or payment of income tax exemption.
The General Department of Taxation has carefully considered and responded positively to the following requests of the Association:
1. For the Association's request on tax audit once a year is approved. The General Department of Taxation will send the draft Prakas on the audit guidelines to the Minister of Economy and Finance for final review and signing. There will be a number of audits only once a year, which can be a letter audit or a transitional audit or a full audit.
A full audit can be retrospective for a maximum of three years. In case of serious irregularities, the General Department of Taxation can review 5 years. There will also be special incentives for companies with a gold tax compliance certificate. A committee for issuing the certificate will be set up soon.
2: For the request to make the tax holiday come true for qualified projects. The General Department of Taxation is in the process of amending the tax law, especially Article 23.
3. Payment of seniority allowance will also be exempt from payroll tax or surcharge tax. This exemption is only for the garment sector.
4: 1% Income Tax Deduction or Income Tax Deduction is currently suspended for our sector, but under the conditions of holding proper accounting records and having financial statements audited as required by General Department of Taxation.
However, there will be an exemption period for the strict implementation of those conditions in order for the factory to strengthen its capacity in relation to tax compliance techniques.
These are the positive results of GMAC's meeting with the General Department of Taxation, and GMAC would like to thank Kong Vibol for his consideration in facilitating the private sector to bring about a better business environment in line with the Royal Government's goals. Under the leadership of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, who always considers the private sector for economic growth and development of the country.
