(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon and Ms. Mak Sitha, together with Ms. Sivan Botum, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, as well as a large number of leaders and officials of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, celebrated the International Women's Day on March 8. 108th 2019 under the theme "Promoting Gender Equality and Social Protection for Human Resource Development".
He said that now, as Cambodia moves forward, the Royal Government has put in place a number of national laws, policies and mechanisms to continue to improve the status, rights, status and role of women in a more equitable and equitable manner. Gender equality with men emphasizes the value of women as an indispensable force in contributing to the development of the country to achieve the vision of the Royal Government in 2030 and 2050.
To celebrate the 108th International Women's Day on March 08, 2019 and to promote the merits of women, rights and gender equality, the Minister instructed the leaders of the relevant ministries and institutions under the Ministry to pay attention to the implementation. The following are the main points:
1. To continue to implement the policy of the Royal Government and the strategic framework for gender mainstreaming in the agricultural sector, especially the 11 recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, which were presented to the National Council of Cambodia for Women on February 18, 2019.
2: Gender and children working groups should study and understand the obstacles in fulfilling the roles and responsibilities of women at both the national and sub-national levels, continue to study and understand the important principles for strengthening the capacity of women.
3. Continue to pay attention to increase the number of female civil servants and assign positions to women in all structures, both at the central and sub-national levels, as well as provide support in terms of spirit, means, budget and provide opportunities. Women's voices participate in the decision-making process.
4: Improve the capacity, knowledge, skills, experience and courage of women farmers in agricultural development, community development and family economy. Promote the participation of women at all levels to benefit from the provision of technical training services, the supply of agricultural inputs and finance.
5: Continue to increase human resources, financial resources and include gender and child action plans to promote gender equality and children in the organization, and should organize monitoring, monitoring and evaluation that is consistent, equitable, transparent and accountable to women and children. Women in agriculture.
Stung Treng Provincial Armed Forces Launch Operation to Crack Down on Lao Drug Trafficker, Confiscate Nearly 8,000 Drugs
(Stung Treng): The Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie Force under the leadership of Brigadier General Ieng Vandy, Provincial Gendarmerie Commander, on March 7, 2019, launched an operation to crack down on a Lao drug trafficker and confiscate drugs. Nearly 8,000.
The Stung Treng Provincial Gendarmerie Commander told Fresh News that the operation took place at the second bridge in Kham Phan village, Samaki commune, Stung Treng city, after the suspects smuggled drugs into Cambodia in Stung Treng province.
Brigadier General Ieng Vandy confirmed that the operation was carried out in accordance with the orders of General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Armed Forces, and in accordance with the instructions of Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor of Stung Treng Province and Chairman. Provincial Unity Command.
Currently, the suspects and exhibits are being detained and kept in the unit so that the case file office can be sent to the Stung Treng Provincial Court to proceed with the procedure.
