Ministry of Labor sets out 24 work directions for officials to continue their efforts in 2019
(Phnom Penh): In the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results in 2018 and work direction in 2019, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, set out 24 work directions for civil servants to continue to work together. Implemented in 2019.
Minister Ith Sam Heng recommended that in 2019, the leaders and civil servants of the Ministry of Labor must implement 24 important tasks, including:
1: Continue to strive to effectively implement the 10 recommendations of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to support and facilitate costs as well as solve problems of workers.
2. Continue to study the possibility of amending the law and preparing legal documents related to rights and working conditions in accordance with the socio-economic needs.
3. Strengthen the quality and efficiency of labor inspection by launching a joint labor inspection report on an automated database system that can automatically synthesize and evaluate working conditions.
4: Adjust the method of labor inspection based on the risk level of the enterprise and set the labor inspection on the export enterprise once / year.
5: Prakas defining 31 core working conditions and 41 general working conditions that enterprises and establishments must implement.
6: Continue to strengthen the capacity of labor inspectors by establishing at least 50 trainers in the field of labor and at least 450 labor inspectors with the competency examination after the training.
7. Disseminate and disseminate knowledge about laws and regulations related to the labor sector, especially about labor rights to at least 1,200 delegates, union representatives, union leaders and at least 750 administrative staff of enterprises and establishments.
9. Continue to prevent the use of the most serious forms of child labor and forced labor.
10: Continue to strive to resolve labor disputes to all parties involved in a timely and effective manner by studying with the Arbitration Council to include the resolution of some individual disputes to the Arbitration Council and strive to prevent illegal strikes and demonstrations. On the principles of law and the rule of law.
11. Promote the transformation of an enterprise into a peaceful community of workers with full capacity, productivity, work attitude and high professional conscience.
14. Establish mechanisms and programs for skills training (Reskilling) and mechanisms with relevant partners to provide credit to trainees, students who complete the training course to establish their own business.
15. Revise the standard document that provides equality between apprenticeship and apprenticeship obligations, and strengthen apprenticeships and internships, and increase awareness of technical and vocational education and training.
16. Strengthen the implementation of the National Employment Policy and integrate appropriate employment programs for Cambodia 2019-2023 and development partner programs.
17: Continue to improve the provision of quality and effective employment services and labor market information by expanding the "Job Forum" mechanism as well as promoting cooperation on the use of labor with partner countries, especially the establishment of support services for migrant workers. Khmer aims to ensure the protection of Cambodian migrant workers and their families.
19: Increase education, production of sports education and promotion of traffic safety to prevent accidents at work and fainting.
20: Continue the implementation of the roadmap for the implementation of the ILO Recommendations regarding the freedom of professional organizations to promote the implementation of freedom of association in Cambodia.
21. Strengthen the capacity of officials and units to provide public services with gentleness, professional ethics and timely to the people, especially workers in accordance with the principles of decentralization and deconcentration.
22: Establish a transparent and accountable administrative and financial system for accurate and regular evaluation to form the basis for implementing the five approaches: "mirror, bath, scrub, treat and operate" and the reform motto. Internal of Samdech Techo Prime Minister.
24. Establish a mechanism to monitor and evaluate the performance of all units under the Ministry by establishing a working group to monitor and evaluate the implementation of the Strategic Plan for Labor Development and Vocational Training 2019-2023. Russian telecoms giant MTS agrees to pay $ 850 million to end US court case
