Lt. Gen. Chum Savuth filed a complaint with the Department of Technology Crimes against the owner of a Facebook page that posted false information affecting his reputation
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Chum Savuth, Director of the Defense Police Department of the General Commission of the National Police, has filed a complaint with the Department of Technology Crimes against an online website that posted false information affecting the honor of his position as a brigade. A police force.
In a complaint received by Fresh News this morning, March 7, 2019, Lt. Gen. Chum Savuth claimed that he was not the owner of the disputed land in Po Thoeun village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district, Sihanoukville province. . That is, he is only responsible for relying on renting machinery to clear the border.
The director of the Defense Police Department also claimed that on the day of the incident, February 15, 2019, the day the court executed the order to demolish the slums on the 88-hectare disputed land, he was not there. Attend the meeting of the Ministry of Interior in Phnom Penh.
He later saw several Facebook accounts posting false information that he had used his power to seize land from 31 families, a charge that had seriously damaged his own reputation and that of the Ministry of Interior. Request the authorities to help research to take legal action. Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration Will Continue to Take Action Against Invasion of Illegal State Land and Call on Citizens Not to Believe the Incitement of Corrupt People
