Stopping the use of telephone systems in correctional centers and prisons in accordance with the high order of the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen on March 4, 2019 at the groundbreaking ceremony for various construction projects in the water protection project. Flooding and improvement of canal system in Phnom Penh.
In this letter, the General Department of Prisons introduced the following:
1: Stop using the telephone system provided to detainees from March 4, 2019 until there is a new regulation.
2. Increase the prevention of all smuggling of mobile phones into correctional centers and prisons, and strengthen inspections and confiscation of mobile phones in correctional centers and prisons.
3. To find a phone that is intended to be imported or to find a phone in prison, make a record of the confiscation and keep it. For those who commit crimes, legal measures shall be taken as stated in Articles 571 and 572 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia and disciplinary action shall be taken in accordance with the prison regulations.
4. To report on the situation and the results of the implementation of this instruction through the daily report to the General Department of Prisons.
