Samdech Techo Hun Sen Asks His Majesty the King to Send a Message to Bless His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia on the Occasion of International Women's Day, March 8
Seeing the challenges of cyclo riders as well as maintaining the identity of the cyclo, one of Cambodia's vehicles, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, decided to establish the "Tricycle Fund" or "Cyclo Fund" last month. January 2018. Samdech Techo Hun Sen dropped about $ 140,000 into the fund and continued to deposit about $ 20,000 a month.
Through the fund, it has contributed to solving some of the difficulties of cyclo drivers and helping to raise the hard-earned money from cyclo cycling left to support livelihoods.
Kem Ken, 76, has been driving a cyclo in Phnom Penh for about 36 years, since Cambodia was liberated from the genocidal regime of Pol Pot. Mr. Kem Ken said that the cyclo taxi business is not as lucrative as before, so the establishment of the Cyclo Fund has contributed to solving some of the challenges in his life.
Mr. Bun Sorn, a resident of Takeo province, has been riding a cyclo since Sangkum Reastr Niyum. Mr. Bun Sorn is now 75 years old and still runs a cyclo to support his livelihood despite his advanced age.
Mr. Bunsorn said that now the cyclo taxi business is not as lucrative as before, the most lucrative day is only 30,000 riel. Therefore, Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Cyclo Foundation has contributed to solving most of his difficulties.
In addition to the financial support, the team of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Cyclo Foundation also provided the National Social Security Fund to the members of the fund to receive free medical examination and treatment.
Cyclo riders are very happy and satisfied with the consideration and attention of the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen. However, the cyclo riders still face some problems, such as the lack of a place to stay at night and a place to take a shower.
Met Meas Pheakdey, spokesman for the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration, said that the Cyclo Foundation currently has a total of 320 members. Ratanakkiri Provincial Commissioner Calls for the Advancement of Women Towards Progress, Equal Rights and Together to Build a National Society of Security and Order to Become a Prosperous and Rule of Law
(Rattanakiri): "Promoting Gender Equality and Social Protection for Human Resource Development" is a topic raised on the occasion of the International Women's Day on March 8, the 108th Anniversary of 2019, which was celebrated by the Ratanakkiri Police Commissioner. On the morning of March 7, 2019 in the presence of Major General Yin Chamnan, Ratanakkiri Provincial Commissioner.
This day was attended by Mr., Mrs. Deputy Commissioner, Chief of Office, Municipal, District Inspector, Commander of the two Border Protection Battalions. On this day, Brigadier General Keo Davy, Deputy Commissioner for Gender Planning, pointed out that the Commission always celebrates the International Day of Women's Rights on March 8 every year, and there are 63 female police officers in the unit, with 23 positions.
Addressing the entire ceremony, Major General Yin Chamnan expressed his full support for the theme of Promoting Gender Equality and Social Protection for Human Resource Development, which was launched by the Ministry of Women's Affairs in 2019 in order to highlight the value of peace. And the promotion of gender equality, which the Royal Government has been supporting, encouraging the participation of all institutions, including men and women, to develop quality and capable human resources.
In addition, the Royal Government has been supporting the National Council of Cambodia for Women, the National Committee for the Promotion of Social Morality, the Values of Women and the Khmer Family in implementing policies to improve the living conditions, status and role of women, as well as to promote social morality, women's values and Khmer family. He believes that Cambodian women really have the support of legal protection, the promotion of status, status, role, authority better.
Minister of Women's Affairs urges detainees to change by doing good for family and society
(Phnom Penh): Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs, urged all women in detention in the Correctional Center (M2) to strive for change by doing good deeds in the family and society after applying the law. .
The announcement of the Minister of Women's Affairs was made this morning, March 7, 2019, on the occasion that she, along with Mr. Keo Remy, Deputy Prime Minister and Chairman of the Cambodian Human Rights Committee and Mr. Ky Tech, Group Leader Lawyer of the Royal Government, Deputy Chairman of the Council of Jurists and Chairman of the Volunteer Lawyer, Samdech Techo Sen, met with women detained at the Correctional Center (M2) in Phnom Penh.
She said that even Thailand, which is close to Cambodia, highly appreciates the Royal Government of Cambodia for taking care of the protection of women. So at this point, let the women who are being held in this correctional center, before doing anything, have to think carefully, if we as mothers commit any wrongdoing, it will make us convicted, it will give Significant impact on family and society.
In particular, Mr. Keo Remy said that every woman has an important role in the development of the family and society, which is the backbone of the family economy. Therefore, every woman should not do anything that is not appropriate, committing other crimes leads to punishment, it is also part of bringing remorse to the family, parents, husbands, children and society as a whole.
Meanwhile, lawyer Ky Tech also said that recently, seeing the hardships of women, Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to set up a group of Samdech Techo Sen volunteer lawyers to provide free defense to poor women across the country. The service is to provide and provide legal advice to women when the court lacks protection for women victims or poor women.
The President of the Volunteer Lawyer, Samdech Techo Sen, continued that, therefore, all women in the Correctional Center (M2) and other centers, please correct themselves, respect the sector and try to apply their sentences properly according to the law to get out as soon as possible. Instead, be a good mother, a good wife, a good child for the Cambodian society, which has progressed in all areas as well.
The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in Battambang Province is planning to celebrate Krong Pali Sankranta New Year which will take place on April 12-16.
(Battambang): The Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Battambang Province (UYFC) this morning, March 6, 2019, held a Krong Pali ceremony to pray for happiness on the occasion of the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the Great Hall of the Year. New Khmer tradition at Nep Yang University and Chea Sim Primary School in front of the statue of Grandpa Dambang Kronhong.
The ceremony was presided over by Mr. Chan Sophal, Member of Parliament of Battambang Province, and Mr. Soeum Bunrith, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, and Mr. Sar Ratha, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, Battambang Province, along with many other members.
According to the organizers of this event, this is the second time that the Battambang Provincial People's Party has organized this festival for the people living in Battambang province to enjoy the festival. The organizers have confirmed that this year's festival is bigger than last year and that all kinds of popular games will be held in different places.
The organizers of the event said, "The Battambang Sanctuary 2019 will start from April 12 to 16, 2019, with nearly 10 national and international guests and people will participate."
The purpose of this event is to provide traditional Khmer fun through religious ceremonies, exhibitions of Khmer products, traditional art shows, traditional games and ancestral traditions to the people of Battambang province throughout the Khmer generation. Later, as well as national and international guests became more familiar with the glorious culture and civilization of Cambodia since ancient times.
(Phnom Penh): The President of the Constitutional Council, Mr. Im Chhun Lim, revealed that throughout 2018, the Constitutional Council has made a significant contribution to ensuring peace, security and social stability, especially strengthening the legal security that is the foundation. Of the rule of law.
According to Mr. Im Chhun Lim, the work shown above is a great contribution to ensuring peace, security and social stability, especially to strengthen the legal security, which is the foundation of the rule of law.
Along with the opening of the meeting this morning, the Constitutional Council also celebrated the 108th anniversary of International Women's Day. During the ceremony, Mr. M. Chhun Lim, President of the Constitutional Council, fully supported the contents of the Royal Message of His Majesty the Queen Mother of Cambodia, the highest reverence and full support for the theme "Promoting "Gender equality and social protection for human resource development."
In this morning's ceremony, Mr. M. Chhun Lim also presented the medals and medals to the members of the Constitutional Council and the civil servants of the General Secretariat of the Constitutional Council. Ministry of Tourism urges Sihanoukville operators to strengthen their capacity to improve the quality of tourism services
(Sihanoukville): In line with the growth of the tourism industry and the growth of tourism support in tourist destinations, especially the coastal areas, the Ministry of Tourism has been paying close attention to training and developing human resources to respond. To the demand for skilled labor in tourism, both in quantity and quality.
In response to this issue, on March 7, 2019, a meeting was held to discuss the needs and supply of training and skilled labor in the tourism sector under the chairmanship of Mrs. Hiek Himley, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province at Preah Sihanouk Provincial Hall. From the specialized department of the Ministry of Tourism, the Department of Tourism, representatives of tourism and hospitality training schools, tour operators and stakeholders, a total of 85 people.
The meeting noted the importance of the role and participation of stakeholders, especially tourism operators and businesses in the tourism sector, in promoting training and capacity building for their staff, both existing and new, and new skills. And the ability to provide better customer service.
For new tourism businesses, at least 30% of the total number of employees must be trained in tourism and hospitality skills.
It should be noted that in connection with the promotion of training and development of human resources in the tourism sector, the Ministry of Tourism has set out its vision of "one employee, one skill" and its strategic goals, including:
* 2020: Encourage the creation of about 1 million direct workers and encourage at least 50% of professionals to have a certificate or certification in line with national and ASEAN standards through training and competency assessment.
* 2025: Co-create 1.2 million direct jobs and achieve the "One Person, One Skill" campaign, which encourages all tourism professionals (100%) to have a certificate or certification. In accordance with national and ASEAN standards.
