(Phnom Penh): The Football Federation of Cambodia (FFC) will prepare a national club license in 2020 to further strengthen development and competition. This was stated by Mr. Chhang Piseth, Executive Secretary of the National Football Commission of Cambodia (CNCC) in a press conference on the opening of the new 2019 season yesterday.
Mr. Chhang Piseth stated that "the license of the National Club of the Football Federation of Cambodia will be implemented from 2020 to strengthen the football club to grow and become a real professional club." He revealed that the federation is currently preparing and documenting the national club license, and there will be some changes to ensure the high level of competition of football clubs in Cambodia.
Answering questions from journalists, how many teams can be eliminated in the 2019 Cambodian Premier League? Mr. Chhang Piseth stated, "After applying for the national club license, no matter if the 13th or 14th team, even the 9th or 10th place team, is not sure to continue playing in the league next year." "So everything is waiting for the issuance of licenses for all clubs to implement and comply with by 2020."
This is good news for the Football Club of Cambodia to develop into a professional club and easy to license from the International Federation of AFC and FIFA. However, the licensing conditions of the national club have not been disclosed, only representatives of the FFC-affiliated entities have confirmed that the federation will take effect in 2020.
