(Kampong Cham): The Governor of Kampong Cham Province, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, urged the police officers of Kampong Cham Provincial Police to work harder to serve the people better.
The Provincial Governor presided over the meeting with Lieutenant General Sek Phum, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police, during the 2018 Annual Meeting of Kampong Cham Provincial Police and disseminated the work direction of the National Police Commissioner General 2019 in the afternoon. March 06, 2019 at Kampong Cham Provincial Police.
After reading the report by Major General Em Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Cham, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Provincial Governor, asked all police officers at all levels and in all fields to concentrate their intelligence on the use of force to the best of their ability. Maintain better local security.
At the same time, Lt. Gen. Sek Phum said that the implementation of the policy of safe villages, communes, Kampong Cham province ranked No. 1 throughout the country for 4 consecutive years. However, there are still challenges, such as the general criminal situation, which has increased by 8%, of which the most notable cases are misdemeanors, an increase of 8%, cases of intentional and domestic violence.
The number of traffic accidents decreased by two cases, but there were still more deaths than last year, 108 out of 90 people, speeding and drunk driving. There is also a significant increase in fire problems, mostly caused by negligence and electric shock.
The number of suicides has also risen, killing 49 people, and authorities are still investigating the cause, but Lt. Gen. Sek Phum also praised the results. 2018 of Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner.
