(Kampong Cham): Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, called on the people of Kampong Cham Province to cooperate and take the time to provide interviews according to the appointments of the census officials. Each interviewer must be able to coordinate the work according to the actual situation by being able to adjust the time, regardless of administrative hours, so that the work of the 2019 census in the province to get better results.
The provincial governor made the call while census officials interviewed him at his home in Ta Neng village, Sambour Meas commune, Kampong Cham city, on the morning of March 6, 2019.
The provincial governor confirmed that the implementation of the 2019 census in Kampong Cham province so far, some cities and districts have performed well and achieved about 21%.
In addition, some cities and districts received only 12% of the results, and this, according to the interviewer, that the delay is due to the factors of conducting interviews in some local areas, our people have not. Responded to what the interviewer wanted, that is, some of them were busy with their daily routine.
There are many potential attractions in the area, including: Ancient temples from the reign of King Suryavarman I (1025 AD) and a Buddhist pagoda together, a mysterious natural spring and flowing ancient canals that can be visited. Acquired agro-tourism area, zoo, flower garden, hydropower system, irrigation system for agricultural land in Prey Chhor district, Kampong Cham province and part of Baray district, Kampong Thom province.
Mr. Sean Sokun, Director of Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Tourism, said that in this Teuk Cha area, there are many interesting places to visit, such as: Teuk Cha natural resort, Kbal Teuk, zoo and flower garden, agro-tourism area, Thmar Da Teuk Cha, pagoda and Preah Theat Teuk Cha temple. Built during the reign of Suryavarman I. In both Kbal Teuk and Teuk Cha resort areas, there are also vendors serving food and beverage services.
After the flames of war have disappeared and Cambodia has regained full peace, the Kampong Cham provincial authorities as well as the provincial tourism department have made efforts to transform the existing natural springs into attractive tourist attractions. Currently, this natural resort has also been handed over to the investment company to increase the development to be more attractive.
Mr. Som Thoeun, the manager of Teuk Cha resort and the vendors at Kbal Teuk resort, called on tourists from all over to visit Teuk Cha resort as well as the waterfront in large numbers.
Ms. Sok Kheang, the owner of Sok Kheang Restaurant in Shanghai, claims that her shop is well-organized for tourists to relax and serve food and beverages with high attention to hygiene and price confirmation.
Mr. Chin Va, the owner of Mlup Po Kbal Spean Restaurant, said that the snails he rented to the tourists cost only 20,000 Riel per plate, and the tourists could also order food for lunch. Great attention is paid to hygiene, food, garbage, waste and the environment around the area.
At the same time, the Director of the Department of Tourism of Kampong Cham Province also urged all tourists who visit the above two tourist resorts to be highly responsible for their garbage and waste, that is, please pack and store. In the bin properly, avoid falling into the water, which leads to damage to the beauty of the water there.
