(Kandal): After Fresh News published an article entitled “Ariyaksat commune residents erupted in protest as the authorities issued land titles to them, conspiring to falsify their land transfer documents to Duke Phen Phalla Then the representatives of Phen Phalla and the authorities came out and denied that in fact the people's accusations against the authorities and the company were just misleading.
The company representative claimed that before the authorities decided to request the issuance of land titles to the people living on the mouth of the stream, the company had received approval from the Ministry of Interior, the approval of Kandal Provincial Hall, and the company with officials at all levels. And the people themselves held three public forums to mediate and find a solution together until there was agreement without any coercion.
As for the 15-meter cut of National Road 380, it is only a legal procedure to issue a title deed. In fact, the 15-meter cut in front of the house is still the land of the people.
The official added that the outcry was due to rumors that the company would cut 10 meters of land in the back, contrary to the agreement, so they protested. The idea is that the company will do whatever it takes to get the people to get the land title.
