Cambodia has been considered a country with a glorious cultural civilization since ancient times. But this civilization and culture was completely lost during the 3 years, 8 months and 20 days of the Democratic Kampuchea regime of Pol Pot. Cambodian civilization and culture were rebuilt and revived after January 7, 1979, when the genocidal regime of Pol Pot was overthrown.
The Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid close attention to the revitalization of Cambodian culture until it decided to establish the "National Culture Day on March 3" in 1998. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have always been invited to celebrate the "National Culture Day on March 3" to encourage and inspire the Cambodian people, especially the youth to love the nation's culture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has dedicated the 21st National Cultural Day, March 3, as a day to commemorate the merits of Khmer ancestors and ancestors and wish this day to be immortal in the hearts of all Cambodians throughout the country with a willing conscience and spirit. Responsible as a whole to maintain, protect and promote the national culture for progress and stability forever.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, stated that the organization of the National Cultural Day, along with the annual gathering of artists across the country, is very important to commemorate the merits and outstanding works of the Khmer ancestors left behind. Leave invaluable cultural heritage to future generations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen added that this cultural day is also to promote and disseminate knowledge, technical skills and cultural talents to inspire young Cambodians, who are the successors of bamboo to love the national culture, have a patriotic conscience and have the duty to preserve Preservation of national cultural heritage aims to make Cambodia a center for the dissemination of national culture, which is one of the priority goals of the Royal Government's national policy on culture.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the deaths of Prach Chhuon and Phlong Moek were the loss of Cambodia's precious heroes. Samdech Techo invited all participants to celebrate the National Cultural Day on March 3 to stand up and pay homage to the spirits of the two artists.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen provided seven suggestions to improve the organization of the National Cultural Day.
The recommendations include:
1. Jointly organize the National Cultural Day every year to increase awareness and love of national culture, cultivate awareness, will and responsible spirit in the transfer of knowledge, technical skills, arts and culture to promote the preservation and development of national cultural heritage. As well as multiculturalism in Cambodia, which is the foundation of the harmonization of society to be stable.
4: The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts must have a mechanism to create the conditions for Cambodian children to be able to create works that are their new cultural products through training courses for young people in high schools, universities and general arts organizations / associations to strengthen the quality of creators. All new in the form of national culture, dignity and human virtues, avoid completely copying foreign works of art.
5: Samdech supports the theme "Youth for National Culture" which has been selected for the National Cultural Day on March 3, now in the years to come, this is a meaningful topic for all young Cambodians who are the right turn. There is an obligation to preserve, protect and create more positive new works in all areas of all forms of cultural art: Cambodia: the Kingdom of Culture, based on the ancient philosophy, not slow, modern, not foreign.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen decides to facilitate and favor tax for another 5 years until the end of 2023 to encourage and promote the arts and production of Khmer films.
The next five years of tax concessions and concessions include:
1. Permission to suspend the implementation of the 15% withholding tax on intangible assets (granting the right to screen locally produced films). 2. Permission to suspend income tax for Cambodian film production companies. Special practice on leisure services (10%) for circus art of Phare Ponleu Selpak, Siem Reap.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his congratulations and pride for the progress of the film industry in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the progress in the film industry came from hard work, not from any humiliation.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued to call for more efforts in film production. Samdech Techo said that if there is good writing and directing, the performance of Khmer stars will also be good. Samdech Techo also expressed his delight at the growing number of Cambodian film fans.
* However, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also criticized the writing of a story in which a 40-year-old woman had a child up to 25 years old. Samdech Techo stated that the writing lacks the fact that if the mother is 40 years old and has a child up to 25 years old, it means that this woman must be married at the age of 14, which is against the law as well as the tradition. Khmer too. Therefore, Samdech asked the author to examine carefully so that the story does not deviate from reality.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also asked the writers and directors to check the pictures and content not to use each other. Like in one story, a woman dies and her lips are red.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Samdech wanted to see the film industry lost during the Khmer Rouge regime become a popular film of the Cambodian people during his leadership. Samdech Techo also wants to see this film industry not only popular among the Cambodian people, Samdech also wants to see Cambodian films become popular movies for other nations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that as long as Samdech continues to be the Prime Minister, taxes will not be imposed on artists.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts to continue to cooperate with the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports to promote the cultural sector.
* By watching the program "Khmer Family Song", Samdech Techo Hun Sen also noted the increase in the ability of contemporary singers who can sing in many forms.
* Samdech Techo stated that the progress in the field of national culture from the difficult period to the present is a matter of pride.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen has announced that he will continue to meet with artists until Samdech is no longer the Prime Minister.
* On behalf of the Royal Government, Samdech Techo praised and appreciated the achievements of the Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts, especially the heritage of living artists, elders, elders and veterans, as well as government officials, professors, teachers, artists of the institution. All cultures that have made an active and lively contribution to the preservation and development of Khmer cultural arts to be stable, prosperous and proud.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the Capital-Provincial Departments of Culture and Fine Arts, together with youth arts groups from all over the country from 25 capital-provincial secondary schools, 11 universities and 10 arts organizations / associations for their efforts in composing Writing, directing and training for many months to compete in the current Youth Art Festival across the country.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, considers the gathering of artists, artisans, musicians, both modern and traditional, singers, performers, writers and experts of all forms of national art and culture throughout the country as the Day of Harmony of National Art and Culture.
