CamControl officers continue to inspect goods at Kampong Thom market, but did not find any defective products
(Kampong Thom): In order to prevent all kinds of goods and food that are sold with poor quality and expired on the market, Camcontrol Kampong Thom Branch this morning, March 6, 2019, cooperated with officials of the Department of Commerce and Local authorities inspected goods at Kampong Thom market in Stung Sen city.
Kampong Thom Provincial CamControl official said that after inspecting with a test kit on some of the food on display in the market, including shrimp, squid, dried fish, the results were not good. No banned chemicals were found in the inspected food products.
Mr. Leang Sophea, President of Cam Kong Trul Branch in Kampong Thom Province, said that the discovery of food mixed with chemicals and defective products, such as out of date, indicates that the traders are more aware of the harmful effects.
CamControl officials also called on all traders and vendors to be careful and pay attention before traveling, distributing, selling and buying food safely without affecting the health of consumers.
