This afternoon, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit will celebrate the 21st "National Culture March 3"
The Royal Government of Cambodia under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen paid close attention to the revitalization of Cambodian culture until it decided to establish the "National Culture Day on March 3" in 1998. Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have always been invited to celebrate the "National Culture Day on March 3" to inspire and inspire the Cambodian people, especially young people to love the nation's culture.
In the circular, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also stated that the celebration of this Cultural Day aims to encourage all people, especially young people to participate more actively in the following essential points:
Raise awareness and participation in the transfer and acquisition of knowledge, skills, techniques, arts and culture to promote the preservation and development of national culture as well as multiculturalism of ethnic communities in Cambodia to be stable and stable, which is the mechanism of national unity and harmony. Peace of society
- Increase awareness of the true value of the national culture, which is an inexhaustible resource with high energy to contribute to socio-economic development by increasing services and cultural products for trade and tourism purposes.
- Encourage participation in research and understanding to compile and preserve all documents of all kinds of cultural heritage in their locality, as well as disseminate widely.
- Promote the use of cultural potential to contribute to the development of the national economy and reduce poverty of the people in order to increase employment and opportunities for all people, especially young people to strive to develop quality new cultural works.
Promote the responsible participation of young people in the preservation and development of national culture in a sustainable and peaceful manner, regardless of political affiliation, religion or color.
