In Africa, especially in Ivory Coast, non-communicable diseases are on the rise and are a major cause of death for Africans. In fact, according to the World Health Organization (WHO) in 2018, 37% of African deaths were related to non-communicable diseases, including diabetes, cancer and coronary heart disease.
In addition, the international organization said that in 2017, diabetes claimed the lives of 300,000 Africans and could affect 41 million people across Africa. In 2045.
According to the World Health Organization, Africa will be the most prevalent region in the world, with cases of various diseases rising by 156 percent in the last 30 years.
On the morning of March 6, 2019, Mr. You Sunlong, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, and Mr. Suong Heng, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, led an inter-institutional working group to inspect the site and hold a meeting to organize the groundbreaking ceremony for the construction of the expressway. Loeun Phnom Penh - Preah Sihanouk Province.
Kong Vimean, spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works and Transport, told Fresh News that the groundbreaking ceremony for the expressway under the presidency of Samdech Techo Hun Sen will be held between km 39-40 in Sla village. Vor Sor Commune, Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province, next to National Road 4.
The spokesman for the Ministry of Public Works confirmed that the first expressway in Cambodia will be built with a width of 24.5 meters, and the foundation structure will have a foundation layer of 16 cm thick gravel and a sub-foundation layer of concrete. New and 32 cm thick cement.
Construction of 3 road stop stations, 1 car park and 2 road operation and maintenance stations. In addition, equip road equipment such as traffic signs, traffic signs, navigation poles and kilometer poles.
It should be noted that the project to build the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway was signed between Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport of Cambodia, signed with Mr. Leav Chi Thao, President of the Chinese Transport Construction Company in early 2018. The signing ceremony was presided over by Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Chinese Premier Li Keqiang during his visit to Cambodia.
Mr. Sun Chanthol expressed the expectation that the Phnom Penh-Sihanoukville Expressway will play an important role in transporting goods to two major economic poles, Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville. In particular, the transportation of goods from factories to the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port for export to the country, as well as the transportation of goods from the Sihanoukville Autonomous Port to other regions.
