(Phnom Penh): The Supreme National Economic Council, in collaboration with the World Bank in Cambodia, is planning to hold the first National Consultative Workshop on "Policies and Directions for Cambodia's Digital Economy" to be held on the 12th. March 13, 2019 at Phnom Penh Hotel.
The consultation was attended by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Supreme National Economic Council, and will be chaired by Mr. Vongsey Visoth, Permanent Secretary of the Ministry of Economy and Finance, Deputy Chairman of the Supreme National Economic Council and Chairman of the Working Group on Drafting the Cambodian Digital Economy Policy Framework.
The workshop will feature presentations of regional countries' experiences in developing regional digital economic policy frameworks such as Thailand, Malaysia and Singapore, as well as participation from relevant institutions in the public sector. Banking and financial technology companies, international organizations, research institutes, universities, embassy representatives with a total of about 300 participants.
