Cuba Reduces Fuel Dependence and Renewes Solar Energy at Cheap Costs
(Havana): Cuba is continuing to reduce its reliance on fossil fuels by converting solar energy into renewable energy. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday evening, March 5, 2019.
Transformation of energy production in Cuba into renewable energy is one of the pillars of the Cuban government's economic reform program aimed at reducing the import of expensive fuels. Cuba's existing renewable energy resources, along with newly built bases, are expected to generate more than 1,100 megawatts by 2019.
NEC: Political parties registered in accordance with the law at the Ministry of Interior have the right to register to stand for election for the third mandate council.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Mean Sati, a member of the NEC, stated that all political parties that are properly registered in accordance with the Law on Political Parties at the Ministry of Interior have the right to register political parties and candidates for the election. Election of the third mandate council in 2019.
His remarks were made during a meeting with stakeholders on the registration of political parties and the list of candidates, and the resolution and handling of complaints related to the registration of political parties and the list of candidates in the hall. NEC meeting on the morning of March 5, 2019.
Stakeholders who attended the meeting included representatives of the Constitutional Council, the Senate, the National Assembly, the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Information, nine political parties, representatives of the Japanese Embassy, 17 non-governmental organizations, six media units and a total of 80 NEC officials. .
Mr. Mean Sith added that political parties wishing to contest the council election must start applying for registration of political parties at the Capital-Provincial Election Commission (CEC) for at least 80 days. Before the election date means that the registration of political parties and the list of candidates lasts only 5 days, starting from March 7 to 11, 2019.
Responding to questions from journalists on how many political parties will contest the council election, Keo Phalla, NEC adviser and head of the Legal Services and Disputes Department, explained that the NEC could not conclude that How many political parties will apply to run, but four political parties always contact professional officials for information. The four political parties are:
* Cambodian People's Party * FUNCINPEC Party * Khmer United National Party * Cambodian Youth Party.
Please be informed that the date of the draw determines the order of the political parties on the NEC ballot paper, not the determinant, it depends on the procedure of registration of political parties and the list of candidates and Complaints and resolutions related to the registration of political parties to stand for election officially end according to each BEC.
