The Supreme Court's reaction came after the president of the Khmer Krom Party, nicknamed "His Excellency Oak Kob Popok", on March 2, 2019, wrote that the court had issued an illegal decision. Related to land issues in Koki village, Bit Trang commune, Prey Nob district, Preah Sihanouk province.
In this statement, the Supreme Court also stated that the Supreme Court's decision so far still has legal value because no institution or authority has rejected or annulled it.
Reacting to William Guang's allegations of "taking state land for private distribution," the Supreme Court dismissed the allegations as "inadmissible and publicly misleading." To lose faith in the court's decision.
The Supreme Court claimed that the land that was the subject of the dispute was the result of a transaction, and that the competent ministry had issued a title deed to the pagoda, not state land. Therefore, the court only performs its role to provide justice to the actors when there is a lawsuit in accordance with the Constitution and the law in force.
Through this press release, the Supreme Court also declared that all courts, which are the third representative of the Kingdom of Cambodia, accept all constructive criticisms that are justified and dare to take legal responsibility for their actions. . However, it does not condone any attacks that are baseless, lose faith in the court and reserves the right to sue under Article 523 of the Penal Code.
