After the meeting, Mr. Top Sopheak, Undersecretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Tourism, told the media that the purpose of the meeting with the Minister and the leadership of the Ministry of Tourism now is the delegation of Philippines Airline would like to inform. That their company will start flying directly from Manila to Phnom Penh.
The Ministry of Tourism is optimistic that through this connection, the direct flight will help increase the number of tourists from the Philippines and third countries to Cambodia, while currently more than 90,000 Filipino tourists to visit Cambodia in 2018. .
Mr. Top Sopheak said that according to Minister Thong Khon, this Manila-Phnom Penh direct flight connection is the first in Cambodia's history because since 1970, Cambodia has not had any direct flights from Phnom Penh to Manila. However, due to the current peace, stability and development in Cambodia, Philippines Airlines as well as other foreign airlines are expanding their direct flights.
On the other hand, the factors that drive this direct flight are also due to the current trend of tourists, that is, they prefer direct flights that are easy and take a short time to reach the destination.
The above decision was made after the inspection team of the Ministry of Mines and Energy and Phnom Sruoch District Authority inspected regularly and found that on March 5, 2019, six companies did not comply with the spirit of the meeting. And the circular of the Ministry, which has already held two meetings, in which the company continues to affect the daily lives of people such as:
* Transport of sand and rocks causes road damage and is not repaired
* Driving at high speeds causes a lot of dust, affecting the health of people without paying attention to watering the road regularly.
* Transported day and night, causing noise to the rest of the people
* Some companies grind stones at night, causing a lot of noise to people living nearby.
Please be informed that on February 27, 2019, the Ministry of Mines and Energy sent a team led by Mr. Ung Dipola, Deputy Director General of the General Department of Mineral Resources, to inspect immediately and meet with all companies that are Operations involving mineral resources, with all companies pledging to abide by the law and address issues raised by residents.
Then, on the morning of March 1, Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu, invited the relevant parties, including representatives of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, provincial and district authorities, departments, units around the province and company representatives to discuss and push for a solution and reach Implement the points that the company has agreed with the working group of the Ministry of Mines and Energy, which includes:
1: Activities of transport, grinding and blasting must be done between 6 am to 6 pm, 2: Regular watering of the road to avoid affecting the lives and health of people living on the streets, 3: Transportation must maintain a distance of at least 150 meters from one vehicle to another, and by maintaining the slowest speed in the city;
In fact, after these two meetings, the inspection team of the Ministry of Mines and Energy and Phnom Sruoch District Authority regularly inspected and found that on March 5, 2019, the six companies still did not comply. In the spirit of the meeting and the circular of the Ministry, the Ministry of Mines and Energy decided to suspend the licenses of those companies for one week as a warning and reach the end of the licenses in case of non-recidivism.
