There are 161 children with their mothers in prison, of which 67 are currently seven pregnant women. Most of the women incarcerated in the prison are involved in drug offenses.
In addition to asking the Ministry of Justice and the Ministry of Women's Affairs to look into the case, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also urged his volunteer lawyers to help defend women in prisons who have not yet been tried.
Please note that every year, the Royal Government of Cambodia also pardons and commutes the sentences of prisoners three times a year, including the traditional Khmer New Year, Pisak Bochea and New Year. However, Cambodian prisons are now facing overcrowding due to the growing number of inmates.
