(Phnom Penh): Footprint International School on Saturday, March 2, organized the final "Song Contest" which took place at the multi-purpose hall of Footprint International School, Tuol Kork Branch.
The program has the technical support of Dr. Chan Sampov, Vice President of the Royal Academy of Cambodia and Chairman of the Technical Committee of the program.
According to the school management, Footprint International School has created this Khmer spelling competition program in order to strengthen the ability of students to hear, read and write Khmer correctly and cultivate their spirit of love and care. Preserve the Khmer language as its national identity.
In addition, the school has implemented many other projects to strengthen the general education of Khmer language as well as the national language skills of students, such as the first Footprint Reading Day program on March 11 to read. Participate in supporting the National Reading Day 2019 of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports. What is special about the game is the participation of the parents of the students themselves as the caretaker, the editor and the total score.
* Stage 1: A word-writing competition held in each class and branch to select 6 winners in each class to participate in the final stage.
* The final stage is divided into two stages, the first stage is a reading contest to select the 6 best candidates in each group to go to the finals. In the final round, all 18 candidates (6 in each group) competed in spelling words to win the 1st, 2nd, 3rd and 4th place winners in each group.
* Group B from grades 4-6 has 164 participants and the first place winner receives an award, a letter of commendation and a study tour to Singapore. The second place winner received a certificate of appreciation and a voucher of 2 million riels for a study tour in Singapore, and the third place winner received a certificate of commendation and a voucher of 200,000 riels for the purchase of books at Monum Book and Tour.
* Group C from grades 7-11 with 136 participants and the first place winner will receive a letter of commendation and a study tour to Singapore. The second place winner received a certificate of appreciation and a voucher of 2 million riels for a study tour in Singapore, and the third place winner received a certificate of commendation and a voucher of 200,000 riels for the purchase of books at Monum Book and Tour.
