Health Minister Asks Stakeholders to Jointly Intervene in HIV / AIDS Intervention in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bun Heng, requested all stakeholders, including the guardians of drug addicts, to respond jointly to intervene on HIV / AIDS in Cambodia.
This statement was made by the Minister of Health at the Joint Response Meeting on HIV / AIDS and Drug Intervention at the University of Health Sciences on the morning of March 4, 2019.
"For drug addicts, we must continue to work together to find real data on drug addicts to reduce and treat drug addicts. The Ministry of Health has continued to expand drug treatment centers in the center. Health Referral hospitals up to 430 places across the country where people can come for free treatment.
In addition, the Minister also asked parents with family members addicted to drugs to cooperate with stakeholders and help guide their children to receive this treatment.
In addition, the minister also called on drug addicts that drugs are not the food we eat every day, so we can make sacrifices because it is not the food we do not eat, but drugs. If you do not drink, you will not die, so in order to have a bright future without losing your mind, please stop using drugs, destroy your reputation and family, especially can lead to death by drugs and other murders.
General Meas Virith, Secretary General of the National Authority for Combating Drugs, said: "So far we have not been able to find out the exact data on how many drug addicts we have in Cambodia. But after implementing the two-year plan to fight illegal drugs (2017-2018), more than 20,000 drug addicts have been registered by the authorities, and so far it has dropped to more than 10,000. .
Please be informed that the meeting was held by Prof. Saphon Vattanak, Rector of the University of Health Sciences, in order to find appropriate ways to prepare a joint response to HIV / Drug Intervention in Cambodia.
