Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum Gives an Interview to Census Officer
(Phnom Penh): The Census is being conducted for two days to obtain specific demographic data for use in formulating policies and to be an indicator in monitoring national strategic development plans and goals. Sustainable development of Cambodia 2016-2030.
In the process of the census, on the morning of March 5, 2019, a group of census officials of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration, led by Mr. Huot Hay, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, visited the house of Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate. Of Cambodia.
The President of the Senate answered many questions from the census officials. This is the third census in the history of Cambodia, which is usually conducted every 10 years to get accurate population data, easy to prepare the development plan of the Royal Government.
In addition to conducting back-to-house censuses, Phnom Penh census officials also conducted censuses at the homes of the nation's top leaders, facilitating and providing excellent cooperation and facilitating the census staff. We.
In order for the census to achieve better results, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, called on his compatriots to support and participate in the general census of the Cambodian people by providing adequate information through interview questions. And loyal to the census officer.
He said the census was not politically motivated to serve the interests of all. "If possible, people should not travel far, and please understand the census officials to enter the house at night." ACLEDA Bank is an important driver in improving the financial environment in Cambodia!
(Phnom Penh): ACLEDA has contributed a lot to the financial sector in Cambodia, especially facilitating some public financial services such as payroll, water and electricity bills and taxes.
Dr. IN Channy, Chief Executive Officer of ACLEDA Bank Plc., Stated that ACLEDA Bank is one of the four or five other banks that the General Department of Taxation of the Ministry of Economy and Finance has selected as a partner in providing various tax services. Citizens can pay property and property tax at all ACLEDA Bank counters.
Dr. continued that people also use ACLEDA Unity Instant to help reduce time spent by paying anywhere and it is not difficult to carry cash to the bank because the tax must be paid. Riel. In addition, ACLEDA also provides easy payment of salaries to civil servants at both national and sub-national levels, who are required to pay their salaries twice a month.
In addition to facilitating the public sector, ACLEDA also facilitates the payment of workers' salaries in the garment and textile sector by signing a memorandum of understanding with the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia, which has more than 600 factories. But before signing a memorandum of understanding with the banking association, it has already worked on payroll with more than 250 factories.
The CEO added that in the past it took up to an hour to enter data in each account, but now there are many changes, faster than before, which takes only 5 to 6 minutes to process data in Up to 300,000 accounts due to the use of modern technology.
Although ACLEDA has begun to transform its bank into a digital bank, its management has no plans to lay off its staff, only to provide additional training to existing human resources to manage those technology systems. These are the things that ACADA has contributed to the public and private sectors.
Commander: Armed Forces Continue to Crack Down on Natural Resources Crimes Trafficking in Silent Forests and Illegal Truck Transportation
(Kampong Speu): On March 5, 2019, Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie Command held a meeting to review and strengthen the implementation of the plan on prevention and suppression of natural resource crime at the meeting hall of Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie Command.
The ceremony was attended by Commanders, Deputy Commanders, Deputy Chiefs of Staff, Chiefs and Deputy Chiefs of the 5 Departments, Chiefs of Offices and Local Assistants of the Municipal-District Gendarmerie, Security Headquarters, Mobile Squadron, Intervention Forces, and Natural Resources Crimes Suppression. 30 officers and deputies of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie.
Representative of General Sao Sokha, Lt. Gen. Hong Vinul, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie, instructed the Commander to assign a force to monitor the location of illegal forest crime or illegal theft of non-timber forest products and to investigate. For the perpetrators and those involved and use the strongest and targeted legal measures.
Brigadier General Chou Sarun, Commander of the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie, said that the Gendarmerie was ready to take part in cracking down on illegal transportation of natural resources in the area.
According to the commander, at the beginning of 2019, Kampong Speu provincial forces cracked down twice and confiscated 34.98 cubic meters of mixed wood, 2 sets of sawing machines and 1 tray.
"Despite the complex geography and remote mountainous terrain, the difficult road conditions make it easy to commit crimes. However, the Kampong Speu Provincial Gendarmerie is still cracking down on resource crime," he said. "The nature that the traders have been stealing in the quiet forest area and transporting them by car across the road is also illegal."
Under the high presidency of Lt. Gen. Hong Vinul, Deputy Commander of the National Gendarmerie, in charge of security and crime suppression, Senior Representative, General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander of the National Gendarmerie, Mr. Sar Sokha. And Delegates Conclude Nearly One-Week Visit to China, Bringing Good Knowledge and Experience in Education Management
(Phnom Penh): During his visit to Anhui Province, China from February 24, 2019 to March 1, 2019, Mr. Sar Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and Vice President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia The Ministry of Education is paying close attention to physical education and sports.
In fact, leading a Cambodian delegation to study in Anhuan Province, China in order to be an input for the experimental development of the sub-sector of physical education and sports. Well.
Regarding the sub-sector of physical education and sports, the Cambodian delegation visited kindergartens, primary schools, secondary schools and high schools in a total of 4 schools in Ling Pi district and met with the sub-sector of physical education and sports with the authority in charge of Anhui province. Well.
The team inspected the actual implementation of physical education and sports hours of Chinese students, as well as inspected the classrooms of students at all levels, with the leadership of each school from one stage to another.
The Cambodian delegation also visited the Lingpi District Police Inspectorate and Security Office to learn about general security management, drug issues and human trafficking. The leaders of the two units presented key security plans, mechanisms, methods, tactics, procedures, tools, and means of day-to-day security operations, followed by a panel discussion by the Cambodian delegation.
In addition to visiting on behalf of the founder of the Sar Sokha Scholarship, he led a working group meeting with the leaders of Hefei University in Anhui Province and also attended the opening ceremony of the second generation of Cambodian Scholarship students. After this, the team visited to talk, understand the living situation, listen to various requests and come up with solutions for a total of 114 students of both generations who are studying there.
Mr. Sar Sokha stated that as a result of this study tour, the Cambodian delegation gained a lot of input experience related to physical education and sports, security management, focusing on drug and human trafficking. Another proud result is that the Lingpi district authority has decided to provide high school scholarships to another 50 Cambodian students.
(Koh Kong): Mr. Hak Leng, Governor of Mondul Seima District, Koh Kong Province, bought and distributed water to people in two villages in Peam Krasop Commune, Mondul Seima District, Koh Kong Province.
Residents who received water said that they lived in Peam Krasop village, Peam Krasop commune, because they had no water for more than two months, but some time ago they bought water that was transported. Sold by boat and car, and the authorities also distributed.
However, these days, the people in Peam Krasop commune have no water, they immediately reported to the authorities, then the authorities immediately distributed water. In fact, on March 5, 2019, Mr. Hak Leng, District Governor and his team came down to distribute water to the people as intended, and he had to use the water they received economically and share it with anyone who He lacks drinking water.
Mr. Hak Leng said that there are more than 500 families in two villages in Peam Krasop commune who lack water. They have been living along the canals for more than two months.
He confirmed that the authorities will continue to work to distribute water to people who lack water and ask you to use water sparingly because the dry season is very hot and has a very long time until the rainy season, so please You are careful about health problems.
