Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum Receives a Delegation of Women to Celebrate the 108th Anniversary of International Women's Day March 8
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum, President of the Senate, on the afternoon of March 4, 2019, received a delegation of women led by Ms. Ing Kantha Phavi, Minister of Women's Affairs to celebrate the 108th anniversary. International Women's Day, March 8, 2019 under the theme "Promoting Gender Equality and Social Protection for Human Resource Development".
On that occasion, Samdech Say Chhum supported and celebrated the 108th International Women's Day on March 8 under the above theme to further promote the status of Cambodian women as mothers, family leaders and the backbone of the economy and A society in a public or private institution with good qualities succeeds in everything as an excellent citizen of the society.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey praised this important topic, which was raised in line with the Cambodian context, which the Royal Government of Cambodia has strived to set out as a key activity in implementing the Royal Government's National Social Protection Policy in the focus. It is important to promote morality, virtue and value to Cambodian women in all circumstances and everywhere.
Samdech Say Chhum emphasized that through the introduction of the win-win policy in 1998, the Royal Government of Cambodia has brought about national unity, which has brought peace, stability, national unity and social security to Cambodia. All this has made it easy for Cambodia to get a new face with full strength and peace throughout the country.
Samdech Say Chhum added that the country has progressed steadily and developed in all fields. The people of Cambodia have been reaping the benefits of peace, political stability, and economic growth, where poverty rates have been significantly reduced.
Samdech stated that the above topic aims to continue to implement the policy of gender equality and social protection, which is the vision for nation building is integrated as a common priority in achieving human resource development, which clearly states that Promoting gender equality, empowering women and girls, and social protection are closely linked.
Samdech Vibol Sena Pheakdey Say Chhum stated that the social protection system and the expansion of the social safety net really contribute significantly to the protection of women's rights, the empowerment of women and girls, and the promotion of gender equality.
