Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign on March 4: 714 illegal vehicles found and 476 fined
(Phnom Penh): Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign For March 4, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 2,946 vehicles and found 714 vehicles violating the law (33% motorcycles), 238 education vehicles and 476 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 1,108 helmets and goggles were inspected on March 4, 135 education helmets and 381 helmets were fined.
For the results of the 4-day inspection from March 1 to 4, 2019, the police inspected 11,038 vehicles and found 2,337 vehicles (30% motorcycles), including education. 712 units and fined 1,625 units. Pailin Governor Requests All Citizens to Cooperate with Census Officers to Provide Accurate Data
(Pailin): Mr. Phan Chanthul, Governor of Pailin Province and Chairman of Pailin Provincial Census Committee, requested people in all provinces, including the private sector, such as companies, casinos, hotels, guesthouses, to cooperate with census officials in their work. Interview and extract accurate and clear census information to make the 2019 census process successful as planned in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government.
This call was made on the occasion of Mr. Phan Chanthul and his team and census officials conducting a general census of Cambodians in Pailin province on March 3, 2019.
Mr. Phan Chanthul continued that in order for the census to be successful, the Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, issued a message calling on the compatriots to support and participate in the general census of the Cambodian people, which started on the 3rd. Until March 13, 2019, by participating in providing accurate and honest information through interview questions to the census officer.
It should be noted that the Kingdom of Cambodia has started the 11-day general census of Cambodians from March 3 to 13, 2019.
