Doha: Negotiations between US and Taliban fail!
Doha: A group of Taliban negotiators and a US delegation held in Doha, Qatar, have not yet reached an agreement or joint statement. A Taliban spokesman was quoted as saying by Sputnik on Monday afternoon, March 4, 2019.
Negotiations for peace in Afghanistan between the Taliban and the United States were reported to have made significant progress in January, but failed to produce a joint statement. But in a statement posted on Twitter on Sunday, Taliban spokesman Zabihullah Mujahid confirmed that the talks had yielded no results.
A new round of talks between the Taliban and the United States was held in Doha, Qatar, on February 25, three days after US Special Representative for Reconciliation in Afghanistan Zalmay Khalilzad Considered it a constructive discussion.
However, sources close to the talks claimed that the two sides were still at odds over the withdrawal of foreign troops from Afghanistan, with reports that Washington had not set a limit on troop reductions or withdrawals. Its not from this country.
