Ministry of Tourism-ILO expands community entrepreneurship development in response to tourism growth
(Phnom Penh): In response to the growing number of tourists every year and to expand tourism entrepreneurship, the Ministry of Tourism in collaboration with the International Labor Organization (ILO) organized a national consultative workshop on Community Enterprise Development (C-BED) training program for those who want to become entrepreneurs in tourism.
This national workshop was held for 2 days from 4-5 March 2019 at Green Palace Hotel, Phnom Penh, with the participation of officials from the 25 Departments of Tourism, Capital-Province, representatives of tourism skills training institutes and training schools. Tourism and hospitality, tour operators and tourism industry associations, professors, experts who are members of the network of experts who participated in this workshop, a total of 68 participants.
To support skills training and human resource development in tourism, the International Labor Organization (ILO) will continue to work with the Ministry of Tourism on other skills training programs in response to the development of tourism.
It should be noted that in 2017, Cambodia achieved an increase of 11.8% with the arrival of more than 5.6 million international tourists and brought about $ 3.638 million in revenue to contribute to the national economy. About 12.3% of gross domestic product (GDP) will directly create more than 620,000 jobs and indirectly tens of thousands more.
