Trapeang Thmor Reservoir in Banteay Meanchey Province is extremely dry, leading to a shortage of water for both humans and animals.
(Banteay Meanchey): Trapeang Thmor Reservoir in Banteay Meanchey Province, which has never been dry, is now historically dry, causing great concern for the daily use of water for people and animals, especially rare birds. Hundreds of cranes were there.
In the face of such a situation, the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, ordered the technical officer to cooperate with the relevant authorities to launch an operation to rescue the Trapeang Thmor Reservoir immediately to have water to be used for people and animals.
The operation to rescue the above Trapeang Thmor Reservoir was led by Mr. Chan Yutha, Secretary of State and Chief of Arrow, Battambang, Banteay Meanchey and Oddar Meanchey Provinces, and Mr. Chan Sinath, Undersecretary of Archeology, together with the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Oddar Meanchey-Banteay Meanchey Province. As well as technicians from both ministries and departments.
Although the Ministry and local authorities have issued special instructions, the Royal Government's directive on water conservation, it is not possible to ban farmers. This is why keeping the volume of water at 50% of the total capacity of 300 million cubic meters will face a serious crisis that causes the water to dry up to the bottom.
He said that through the above measures, we can save the shortage of water for daily use of both people and biodiversity and rare species (cranes).
Please note that in the dry season in 2019, Cambodia will experience severe drought, especially during April and May, the temperature will rise to 40 to 42 degrees due to the indirect effects of El Nino (El Nino). The Royal Government has called on the authorities and the people to take measures to conserve water for use.
