The group aims to oust Mr. Rainsy's role and declare that he is no longer affiliated with Mr. Rainsy's group, that is, break the fake alliance between Mr. Rainsy and Mr. Sokha and give important roles to Mr. Kem Sokha or one of the dignitaries from the quota. Mr. Kem Sokha (possibly the daughter of Mr. Kem Sokha, Miss Kem Monovitya) to continue to lead the opposition by completely eliminating the role of Mr. Sam Rainsy.
Kem Sokha's group, which calls itself the Reform Party, wants to adopt a new policy for the opposition that is constructive and soft, without using provocative painkillers, as Sam Rainsy did. The group also plans to announce a new foreign policy for its group that differs from Sam Rainsy's foreign policy.
For those who follow the coffee table politics, I see this as an important new political turning point for building the future of an opposition party that has a real role in Cambodia, because the opposition politics like Mr. Sam Rainsy, which has been tested for more than 20 years, sees that Completely failed.
The emerging Kem Sokha Niyum movement is a warning sign for Sam Rainsy and his co-workers that their political career, painting and igniting their anger, has come to an end.
