450 books on the history of Mr. Assu Ito distributed to students of Atsu School in Kampong Thom
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Sakaguchi Naoto, former Member of Parliament for the Lower House of the Regional Assembly in Japan, and Mr. Koichita Kumar, President of the Japanese Association of Cambodia in Cambodia, on March 2, visited primary schools and Atsu Secondary School in Atsu Commune, Prasat Sambo District, Kampong Thom Province, and distributed 450 autobiographies of Mr. Nakata Atsuito to students.
The visit and distribution of Nagata Atsuito's history book above because Sakaguchi Naoto wanted to commemorate the memory and heroism of Atsui Ito, a Japanese man who sacrificed his life to build peace in Cambodia. During his mission as a volunteer of the United Nations Transitional Authority in Cambodia (UNTAC) in 1992.
Asu Ito's autobiography, authored by Sakaguchi Nato, was the first of 3,000 copies to commemorate the history, personality, influence and heroism of Atsuito. Provided to Cambodia and Japan. This article is sponsored by Sakuranet Vaccine and facilitated by Lokomo Group in Japanese and Khmer.
Recall that Assou Ito traveled to Cambodia in 1992 to help organize Cambodia's elections in 1993 after the Khmer Rouge regime, which killed millions of innocent Cambodians and the protracted civil war. The year is over and Cambodia is holding its first free and fair elections, a step towards full peace and democracy under the auspices of UNTAC.
