Sim Sovanny is the third politician among former CNRP leaders to receive political rehabilitation, after Kong Koam, a former senior CNRP adviser, and Kong Bora, a former CNRP lawmaker. King on January 15, 2019. Mr. Sim Sovanny is ranked 44th on the Supreme Court's list of political ban.
A total of 118 former CNRP members were sentenced by the Supreme Court to a five-year moratorium on political activity on November 16, 2017, and blocked protests after a court found that the former opposition party had conspired with them. Foreigners in order to overthrow the legitimate Royal Government of Cambodia.
Yesterday, young politician Kong Monika, president of the Khmer Will Party, the son of Kong Koam, revealed that a number of former CNRP leaders would apply for political rights in the near future.
"If the King is willing to grant me the right to return to politics, I will accept to continue (locally) the path to positive change," he said.
