Man arrested after fleeing for almost a year after shooting his wife
(Preah Vihear): A suspect was arrested by the police force of Rovieng District Police Inspectorate, Preah Vihear Province, in cooperation with the Sandan District Police Force, Kampong Thom Province, after fleeing for several months after using a revolver to shoot his wife.
Colonel Say Det, Police Inspector of Rovieng District, Preah Vihear Province, told Fresh News on March 2, 2019 that the suspect who was detained by the police was named Srey Don, male, 37 years old, residing in Kak Poun Village, Reaksa Commune, Rovieng District. Preah Vihear Province. He said that the operation to arrest the suspect cooperated with the police force of Sandan District Inspector, Kampong Thom Province, leading to the arrest of the suspect on February 28, 2019.
The district inspector added that the murder occurred on April 22, 2018. After the incident, the suspect fled the scene.
He confirmed the story that before the incident, the couple argued about his wife giving his brother too little money to sell the wood that was cut together. Unable to control his anger, the husband pulled out a revolver and shot his wife. Not only that, the bullet also exploded on the child, causing injuries. After the incident, the suspect's husband escaped forever.
The suspect is now in charge of building a case to the court to proceed according to law.
