Legal Awareness: Termination of Employment Contract
For this week, our program would like to bring the topic of "Dissolution of Employment Contracts" to the public:
According to the 1997 Labor Law, the termination of an employment contract is mainly focused on two types of employment contracts, including fixed-term employment contracts and indefinite-term employment contracts. Under:
1. Termination of a fixed-term employment contract According to Article 73 of the Labor Law 1997, the provision that a fixed-term employment contract shall expire normally upon maturity. However, this contract may be terminated prematurely by the agreement of both parties, provided that this agreement is made in writing before the Labor Inspector and signed by both parties to the contract.
The voluntary termination of the contract by the employer before the deadline, in addition to the above reasons, allows the worker to receive a mental illness in the amount of at least equal to the wages that the worker received until the end of the contract.
The voluntary termination of the contract by the worker alone, in addition to the above reasons, entitles the employer to receive compensation equal to the damages inflicted on the worker. The work states: Serious errors are considered as follows:
* Workers' faults: theft, exploitation, elimination, giving a false degree when applying for a job, serious violations of security and hygiene rules, threatening, insulting, beating an employer or other worker, inciting other workers To commit serious mistakes, propaganda activities or political demonstrations in the establishment.
* Employer Mistakes: Deceptive tactics used to lure workers to sign contracts, refusal to pay in whole or in part, multiple delays in payment, insults, threats of beatings According to Article 85 of the Labor Law, the employer is not able to fulfill the "B" promise in the following cases: To:
* Closing of enterprises that the government requires to be closed * Disaster "floods, earthquakes, wars" that cause material damage, making it impossible to continue working for a long time. The death of the employer, which caused the closure of the establishment, opened the right for workers to receive compensation equal to the notice period.
At the end of the contract, the employer must provide the worker with a severance pay that is proportional to the salary, including the duration of the contract. In the absence of any stipulation, this indemnity shall be at least 5% of the wages paid by the worker during the term of the contract. .
2. Termination of employment contract has an indefinite duration According to Article 74, paragraph 1 of the Labor Law, the provision states: “An employment contract with an indefinite duration can be dissolved at the will of one party. The termination of the contract shall be carried out in the form of prior notice in writing, which the parties wishing to terminate the contract must give to the other party. The minimum notice period shall be set as follows:
* Admission to probation or internship stipulated in the contract * Any party to the contract commits a serious mistake
In the case of serious misconduct and in the case of a supervisor, there is no difference between a fixed-term employment contract as described in the above-mentioned point. Which is its responsibility before it is completed. If this work cannot be done within one month, the worker can be released from this work duty until the other party is notified 8 days in advance.
In a seasonal enterprise as listed by the Prakas of the Ministry of Labor, dismissal of a worker at the end of the term cannot be considered as dismissal and shall not be subject to any severance pay. Notice of the stop at least eight days in advance by posting a notice at the main entrance to the site and on each ship, if any.
In conclusion, for the termination of the employment contract between the worker and the employer, whether it is a fixed-term employment contract or an indefinite-term employment contract, each party must properly respect the obligations and responsibilities for this termination. In accordance with the requirements of the Labor Law 1997.
US, South Korea suspend major military drills to boost ties with North Korea
WASHINGTON (Reuters) - The United States and South Korea announced on Sunday that they would no longer lead two large-scale military exercises that the two allies have held every year. Made in support of efforts to improve relations with North Korea. This was quoted from the South Korean news agency Yonhap on Sunday morning, March 3, 2019.
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, this morning, March 3, 2019, gave an interview to the census officials led by Senior Minister Chhay Thorn, Minister of Planning, at his residence in Takhmao City, Kandal Province.
Ms. Hang Lina, Delegate of the Royal Government of Cambodia in charge of the Director General of the National Institute of Statistics, told Fresh News that the census will last 11 days from March 3 to 13, 2019, and will be interviewed by dignitaries. And the population of nearly 3 million households, including about 50,000 census officers nationwide.
She added that in the next 11 days, each census officer will interview 120 to 150 families, and the preliminary results of the census will be available within three months after the end of the census. Held between 6-9 months later.
Please be informed that the Cambodian Census is very important and the only source that can provide complete and accurate data as well as characterize the real living conditions of the people throughout the country. Only one that can provide complete data on the population and character of the population in the country.
In order for the census to be successful, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has issued a message calling on his compatriots to support and participate in the general census of the Cambodian people from March 3 to 13, 2013. 2019 by participating in providing sufficient, accurate and honest information through interview questions to the census officer.
Russia: "US attempts to intervene in Venezuela under the pretext of humanitarian aid have nothing to do with democracy"
According to the Russian Foreign Ministry, Lavrov made the remarks in a telephone conversation with Pompeo on Saturday. During the talks, Lavrov criticized the US threats against the government of Venezuelan President Nicolas Maduro as an interference in the internal affairs of a sovereign state and a violation of international law.
Lavrov also blamed the US Secretary of State for Washington's efforts to influence the situation in Venezuela under the guise of providing humanitarian aid to the troubled Latin American country. "These actions have nothing to do with the process of democracy," he said.
Regarding Washington's proposal to hold consultations on Venezuela, Lavrov stressed that Moscow was ready, but reminded Pompeo that the principles of the UN Charter must be strictly adhered to. Because only Venezuelans themselves have the right to decide the fate of their country.
The story of a couple in a time of crisis is another new episode. While the first part, Samdech Techo described the birth of the love life between Samdech and Samdech Kittipritthbandit until the wedding day. Please read the love life story between Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit part 1 (History of love life of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit part 1)
The following is the full text that Samdech Techo Hun Sen posted this morning:
Unfortunately, I did not respond to Rany, just nodded as a sign that I understand. The motorcycle left the brigade headquarters, which was then stationed in Koh Thmor village, Tonlong commune, Tramoung district. I tried to watch my wife until I could see and hear the sound of motorbikes with no pity, pity for my wife and pain.
I was a little relieved to receive information about my wife's whereabouts, but this was replaced by an attack in February 1976 when I went to see Rany at the Army Hospital but could not find her. Received information that Rany at the hospital was only a few days ago when the organization sent her to the field lighting system in Khnar village, Sralop commune, Tbong Khmum district. Outraged, a midwife was hired as a plowman.
Please note that Rany is still working with another female doctor named Tang Ly who can help take care of each other because Dr. Tang Ly used to be a battle doctor and has been treating me since 1971. Tang Li later married a former brigade commander under my command. They are kind people and now they are farmers in Stung Treng province with many children and grandchildren like me.
Upon arrival at the hospital, the doctor who treated me and who had studied medicine with Rany told me that my wife was also in the hospital, in the female ward. I was in a hurry. A trip to see my dear wife. The happy thing beyond meeting is that Rany told me she was pregnant and was losing a lot.
I arrived at the unit without information on how my wife was doing or where she was. Worked in the field lighting unit at Wat Prey Nokor Knong, the former capital of Luang Preah Sdach Kan in Ponhea Krek district. At that time, Rany was more than 3 months pregnant, but the symptoms of miscarriage continued.
During June 1976, my wife was allowed to work at the local military hospital located at Wat Popel, Popel commune, Teuk Chrov district at the time, after being disciplined for more than five months. At this hospital, Rany seems to be more comfortable and I often have the opportunity to visit with my wife.
There is a funny thing happening at this military hospital. When Rany was about 5 months pregnant, one of my fighters wanted to marry Rany because he did not know that Rany was married and had a baby because Rany's first child was not big.
The Tramoung district took a motorbike to take me to the hospital where Rany was staying at about 9 pm.
I invited the chief of staff to sit in my chair, but he did not, he looked at the map hanging on the wall with the drawing of the army stand. He then dialed the 75th Battalion, which was located about 3 km from the battalion headquarters. He checked everything without saying anything to me yet. After a while, he said to me that the subordinates live like this unchanged.
I said to the local youth leader, who was pale with this fear, "What do you really want?" The first time I ate cooked chicken, they accused us of being subordinates who wanted to eat delicious food, sleep well, and lacked savings. This time, let Prahok accuse us of being lazy and lacking in creativity.
I raised the question of whether or not he cheated me to arrest outside the unit? Or does he just not pay attention when you tell him something to do? The main problem that made me take orders so quickly was that I wanted to visit Rany, who was in Memot Hospital, because we had to take National Road 7 in front of the hospital.
The more I nodded, the more I missed my wife. I do not rest and wish the sky would be bright soon. I checked my equipment, which included a K54 pistol for the waist belt and another K59 pistol in my backpack. Both guns are unlocked, ready to fight, because I am worried that the military chief of the area cheated on me, took me away or killed me outside the unit.
After wrapping my baby's body and sending it to the hospital director, I hurried to Rany, who was on fire in another room. In fact, Rany did not see her face. We, a young couple, look at each other and cry with regret. I no longer have tears to wipe my tears because the scarf was already wrapped around my baby's body and has sleeves on both sides to wipe away this painful tear. Rany gave me a scarf and she shivered after giving birth for about an hour.
I was so angry that I could not bear to pull out this deadly gun in the area of Bosta Kok, between Sam and Dar villages, which at that time was completely forested, with no fields and houses like now. But I still have the patience to lead a struggle in which I have already mastered a number of secret forces and some have already been arrested, so the resistance movement must continue unabated due to my anger. Yes.
Before dawn on November 12, 1976, I hurried to the hospital to transport Rany to my unit, which was located in Koh Thmor village, Tonlong commune. When I arrived, I saw my comrades helping to set up a wall room for me. They knew the story of my child dying and my wife was sick, they shared the sadness and hardships with our couple.
Despite the difficulties, this is the first time I have been living together for more than a week after marriage. My husband and I lived together without the hassle of organizations as before.
During the end of January 1977, my wife became pregnant again, the birthplace of Hun Manet, my son today. Having a child this time is not in line with my intentions, because I should not have children in such circumstances, because I was ready to fight the Pol Pot regime. I have clearly decided to stand up and defeat Pol Pot. But the problem lies in the timing and the method.
If a fight breaks out, what will happen to my pregnant wife or baby? I love my wife and want her to live next to me, but I do not want to see my wife and children in danger when a fight breaks out.
During February 1977, I brought my wife, Vil, back to the Regional Military Hospital, located in Samrong Village, Dar Commune, Memot District, where she worked. Previously separated by organizations, but this time I organized myself to prepare for the genocide of Pol Pot. Fortunately, this time, Rany did not lose like her first child.
Returning to the political situation, organizations increase the killing of people without discrimination. In the face of this situation, I have four options to choose from:
The first option is to use the force under my command to occupy Tramoung district, Memot district of Kampong Cham province and Snoul district, Kratie province, to use it as a liberating area to conquer other geographical areas. This option is predictable, will end up in a pool of blood in half a month, everything will be over by then.
The second option is to withdraw and reorganize the struggle by going to the support of Vietnamese friends, as King Norodom Sihanouk did in 1970.
I decided to choose the second option, which was made on the night of June 17, 1977 at Wat Damber, Tambor district, at the end of the political course there, which the organization called to study more than a month ago.
We left at 9 pm on a secret route that did not let the troops in the fort know where we were going. We left in pain with tens of thousands, hundreds of millions of tears. But it was these tears and pain that strengthened my spirit to fight for the survival of the Cambodian people.
Taking advantage of the fighting and the rise of the army and the people in the Eastern Zone, led by Samdech Heng Samrin, Samdech Chea Sim on May 25, 1978, there are more opportunities for my resistance movement to move forward. Find success.
Many of my wife's family members were killed, and one family was killed. The crackdown intensified. My parents-in-law took their children and grandchildren into hiding in the forest during August 1978. Since my wife's sister and brother had all daughters, Manet, my son became the first grandson of this family.
I would like to confirm that what I wrote about my wife and children on June 20, 1977, which was the day we were separated until the day we met on February 24, 1979, is from my wife's description only. . Because from the time we broke up on June 20, 1977 until we met again, I never received any information from my wife. And if I get it back, it all proves that my wife is dead.
About mid-February 1979, I dreamed of Rany on the other side of the creek, which is bordered by deep water. Learning from a child. I was going to the boat to cross to her, suddenly the clock rang and I dreamed. I got up, sat crying and could not understand this dream.
I am writing now, after more than 40 years, from a young man to a grandparent with 20 grandchildren, some of whom are already in college and high school.
Hopefully this article will be helpful for those who want to understand the journey of my life and my wife.
