River Festival in Kampong Chhnang is ready to welcome people and tourists
(Kampong Chhnang): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism and Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission for River Festival, requested the relevant authorities and law enforcement forces to work hard to strengthen security and order, especially to solve traffic congestion in the city during the celebration. The 5th River Festival in Kampong Chhnang Province from March 15-17, 2019 soon.
This statement was made during the 5th River Festival Preparatory Meeting at Kampong Chhnang Provincial Hall on February 2, 2019 to review the previous (final) festival.
As the Chairman of the Inter-Ministerial Commission, Mr. Thong Khon reminded, "We request the relevant authorities and forces to conduct a thorough study on security and order, especially traffic congestion of vehicles. And tourists passing through and visiting the Kampong Chhnang River Festival.
Care must be taken to deploy traffic police and ambulances along National Road 5 24 hours a day and at key locations of the river festival.
At the same time, the Minister also reminded the provincial administration and all relevant departments to continue to cooperate with the pottery handicraft association to organize good exhibitions to show the identity of the province to the people and tourists.
On the other hand, be careful to choose to show agricultural products and handicrafts that are produced in the country and have the ability to export a lot.
Efforts must be made to organize more food fairs to serve the needs of the people and tourists visiting the upcoming river festival. Must organize food fairs well in terms of hygiene, service and reasonable prices.
The meeting concluded that everything was ready according to the plan, with some minor tasks remaining next week and finalized.
Please be informed that the 5th River Festival for 3 days in Kampong Chhnang will be held under the theme "River: connecting peace, people and tourism" under the light of the full moon and under the shadow of peace throughout the country. ASEAN, Japan Sign First Protocol to Amend Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement
The first protocol was signed by the Minister of Foreign Affairs of Japan, Mr. Taro Kono, on 27 February 2019 in Tokyo, Japan, which is included in the AJCEP to make all chapters on trade in services more efficient. Comprehensively facilitate the movement of individuals and investment, as well as set key goals in ASEAN-Japan economic relations.
According to the Minister of Commerce of Cambodia, Mr. Pan Sosak, the integration of these chapters will serve as a catalyst to strengthen and expand trade, services and investment more deeply and comprehensively to transform the ASEAN-Japan Strategic Partnership into Promote and support economic integration in Thailand in East Asia.
Please be informed that AJCEP was signed by ASEAN and Japan on April 14, 2008 and entered into force on December 1, 2008. Through AJCEP, the volume of trade and investment between ASEAN and Japan has been steadily increasing. Japan is currently ASEAN's fourth largest trading partner and the second largest source of foreign direct investment.
In 2017, trade between ASEAN and Japan reached 219.3 billion US dollars, accounting for 8.5% of the total ASEAN trade, while the direct investment flow from Japan was about 13.4 billion US dollars. Equivalent to 9.9% of total investment inflows into ASEAN countries. Justice Army football team played a friendly match with Ratanakkiri Provincial Court under the sponsorship and support of the Minister of Justice
