Minister of Agriculture calls on local rice companies and mills to procure farmers to stockpile rice at a reasonable price and then process rice for export
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on March 2, 2019, encouraged and called on local companies and rice millers to work hard to collect rice from farmers to dry and store at a reasonable price. Then processed into rice for export.
This call was made on the occasion of the Minister inspecting the rice procurement activities of Tycoon Lim Bunna in Stong District, Kampong Thom Province.
According to the management of the company, at the request of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the company has now collected more than 10,000 tons of dry rice from farmers at a reasonable price of 710-720 riel / kg. Take it to dry and store it in the warehouse and continue to collect.
The Minister considers that this action is to help keep the price of rice from falling during the Chinese New Year, which has responded in time to the call of the Royal Government as well as the Ministry to participate in the private sector effectively. To collect rice and process it for export.
