For the success of the 7th Inter-Ministerial Meeting in Angkor, Cambodia, the Prime Minister of Cambodia shared three recommendations as a basis for consideration and discussion, including:
First, the member countries of all parties to the negotiations on the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement must consider the current negotiations as a "win-win" process that is acceptable to all parties and the outcome of the negotiations. This agreement will greatly benefit all parties, no matter the different levels.
Second, all member states of the negotiating parties, despite their different economic agendas, must review the RCEP with a sense of responsibility for the overall potential and benefits so that the negotiation process can take place. Smooth and overcome the remaining obstacles to complete the negotiations in a timely and transparent manner.
