Hungary plans to help develop tourism, education and agriculture in Cambodia
In fact, on March 1, 2019, the Hungarian delegation met with Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province, focusing on strengthening cooperation and development in three areas, including: Tourism, Education and Development. 3: Agriculture.
The Hungarian side considers Battambang a strategic location for the implementation of the Cambodia-Hungary Development and Partnership. During future visits, Hungary will bring experts to teach both tourism and agriculture and provide scholarships to Cambodian students. After the meeting, the Hungarian delegation inspected Battambang airport and tourist port.
To further promote the economic development of the province, both sides have a vision to develop tourism infrastructure such as airports and tourist ports to connect tourists from Siem Reap and Phnom Penh by air and water.
The visit is aimed at implementing the Memorandum of Understanding on Tourism Cooperation signed by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation and Minister of Foreign Affairs and Trade Peter Szijjarto of Hungary.
