(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation will hold a two-day annual meeting from March 5 to 7, 2019, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon, Minister of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation. The Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen will preside over the closing ceremony on March 7, 2019.
Within the framework of this annual conference, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation will review the achievements and challenges in 2018 and set the direction for 2019.
Minister of Commerce: Cambodia and ASEAN Member States Strongly Commit to Supporting Multilateral Policy
(Siem Reap): The Minister of Commerce, Mr. Pan Sosak, stated that Cambodia and all ASEAN member countries are firmly committed to supporting multilateral policies and international cooperation.
On that occasion, the Prime Minister recalled the background of the RCEP agreement negotiations and thanked the leaders of all participating countries for their efforts to push forward the negotiations to achieve a free trade area. The largest in Asia in the near future, which will be a solid foundation for global economic prosperity.
At the same time, the Prime Minister also gave three important recommendations to the Ministers of the 16 RCEP Negotiations countries to avoid differences in some areas in order to accelerate the establishment of a full RCEP Free Trade Area as desired. Of the following participating countries:
1. All parties shall consider these negotiations as a win-win process, the final outcome of this Agreement will benefit all parties, albeit at different levels.
2. Despite the different economic agendas, all negotiating parties need to look at the overall picture of the great potential and benefits of the RCEP so that the negotiation process can overcome the remaining obstacles.
The following are the main remarks of Samdech Techo Hun Sen:
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in the whole world, the free and open multilateral trading system is in a tense situation and is facing threats due to some countries, including the great powers, adhering to the one-sided policy. Partisan and bilateral interests have fueled protectionist sentiment, which could affect free trade in RCEP member states.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia is once again honored to host the 7th Inter-Ministerial Meeting. Cambodia, as well as all RACEP member countries, congratulate Indonesia on the progress of the agreement negotiations, which are well under way, and thank Indonesia for acting as a facilitator. .
Samdech Techo shared three recommendations to the ceremony as a basis for considering and organizing the negotiation talks, including: First, all member countries of the negotiating parties of the Regional Economic Partnership Agreement must consider Negotiations are now a "win-win" process that is acceptable to all parties, and the outcome of the agreement negotiations will be of great benefit to all parties, albeit at different levels.
Second, all member states of the negotiating parties, despite their different economic agendas, must examine the ASEAN Agreement responsibly in order to ensure that the negotiation process can proceed smoothly. Smooth and overcome the remaining obstacles to complete the negotiations in a timely and transparent manner.
* Samdech Techo hopes that all negotiating member countries will have a joint political will to finalize the RACEP agreement in 2019, with Thailand to chair ASEAN in accordance with the commitment of the leaders at the summit. The second Asean meeting on November 14, 2018 in Singapore to lead to the negotiation of other free trade agreements in the region.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted that China, Japan, India and South Korea all have a vision to expand trade to ASEAN. In this regard, Samdech encourages these countries to work together to decide on the concept of RACEP.
* Samdech Techo called on RACEP member countries to live together peacefully and cooperatively, and to resist protectionist and unilateral policies that lead to the destruction of global liberalization and character.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen finished his speech at 9:54 am on March 2, 2019, thank you for watching the live broadcast.
