Fire destroys 15 houses in Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province due to electric shock
(Kampong Cham): A fire occurred in Svay Tananak village, Prek Romdeng commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province on the afternoon of March 1, 2019 due to electric shock.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Em Kosal, said that upon receiving this information, he immediately ordered the fire brigade to remove six vehicles from the province and district to immediately operate and ask for immediate cooperation from the Kandal Provincial Police. Two more vehicles of Muk Kampoul and Khsach Kandal district inspectors, a total of eight vehicles used in the operation.
After a careful rescue operation for nearly 2 hours, the fire was prevented and extinguished by the authorities. According to the commissioner, the cause of the fire was due to an electrical fault and the extent of the damage was 15 houses.
However, this social accident did not cause any harm to any citizen.
