According to the US Embassy, the fair is a unique opportunity for Cambodian students to connect with higher education institutions in the United States and learn about the benefits of studying at a US university. The exhibition will run from 2pm to 6pm at the Great Duke Hotel, formerly InterContinental.
This year, 30 representatives from colleges and universities in the United States will discuss with Cambodian students their degree programs, enrollment requirements, and scholarship opportunities for study in the United States.
Other exhibitors will be provided with information on student visas, US Government exchange programs, and the United States Education Counseling (EducationUSA).
High school and university students in Cambodia interested in pursuing higher education in the United States are welcome to attend. Parents of students are also welcomed and encouraged to attend.
EducationUSA is a US Department of State network of 400 international student counseling centers in more than 170 countries around the world. The network promotes US higher education to students around the world, providing up-to-date and accurate information on study opportunities at accredited institutions of higher learning in the United States.
