(Phnom Penh): The case of a male security guard who decided to hang himself on an Indian tricycle on the morning of February 1, 2019 at the intersection of Street 80, Village 7, Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, is not the hospital's personal security guard. Calmette is the security of a private company that has contracted with Calmette Hospital to collect taxes on bicycles, motorcycles and cars only.
According to Reasey, administrative director of Calmette Hospital, told Fresh Ndews on the afternoon of February 1, 2019 that a man who decided to hang himself to end his life on an Indian tricycle this morning. He is not the hospital's personal security guard, only a private company security contracted with the hospital.
The Calmette Hospital's administrative director said that the news that the hospital had fired him was untrue because it was the victim's responsibility.
The victim is Khim Veasna alias Sokha, 35 years old, security guard, living in a rented house with no number on Street 86, Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh, and his hometown is Kampong Basrey Village, Chey Kampot Commune, Preah Sdach District, Prey Veng Province.
The reason why the victim decided to hang himself was because 4 to 5 days before the victim had a work problem, the boss changed the security work from the inside to work outside. After this happened, the victim called his wife and children, saying that he did not earn much money, so he had to spend less because he had to be sent outside the hospital by his boss.
The body is currently being transported to Wat Toul Sangke, Sangkat Toul Sangke, Khan Russey Keo, Phnom Penh.
