(Battambang): The National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils on March 1, 2019 celebrated the 108th anniversary of International Women's Day on March 8, with the theme "Promoting Gender Equality and Social Protection for Human Resource Development". Attended by 55 out of 393 female Capital-Provincial Councilors nationwide.
Mr. Mop Sarin, President of the National Association of Capital-Provincial Councils, said that this is the third time that the National Association has organized a "program to understand the rights of women" and the policy of the Royal Government to promote the promotion of women in the field. Decide publicly and politically, both nationally and sub-nationally.
Also present at the ceremony were Ms. Kim Siphat, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, Mr. Uy Ry, Chairman of Battambang Provincial Council, Ms. Nhek Sokun, Deputy Governor of Battambang Province, and Ms. Nuon Nartey, Chairperson of the National Council for Women and Children's Affairs. Capital, province.
The National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils was established in 2013 with the aim of building the capacity of its members and protecting their legitimate interests. Currently, the National Association of Capital and Provincial Councils has 24 provincial councils and Phnom Penh Capital Council as members.
The establishment of the Association of Sub-National Administrative Councils aims to support the policy of decentralization and deconcentration reform of the Royal Government of Cambodia. May 2019. For the third mandate, there will be a total of 559 members of the Capital and Provincial Council, an increase of 166 compared to the second mandate.
The number of councilors in the third mandate will be 3,555, an increase of 624, compared to 2,931 in the second mandate. According to Sub-Decree No. 22 dated January 25, 2019 on determining the number of members of the Capital, Provincial, Municipal, District and Khan Councils for the third mandate.
