(Phnom Penh): The owner of the house arrested a suspect and handed him over to the Boeung Kak 1 Administrative Police Station in connection with a specific case of theft by stealing jewelry in a wedding house.
This incident happened at 7:15 in the morning at the wedding venue, house 34, street 351, group 7, village 2, Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
According to the witness, the suspect was named Chhoeun Veasna, alias Sna, male, 30 years old, Khmer, unspecified occupation, unspecified residence, place of birth, Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh, Phnom Penh. The victim is Huot Chanratha, male, 34 years old, Khmer, Occupation: Metfone employee, living at house 34, street 351, group 7, village 2, Sangkat Boeung Kak I, Khan Toul Kork, Phnom Penh.
After the arrest, the police confiscated the following items: jewelry, 1 gold ring weighing 1 g, 1 platinum ring weighing 3 g, 1 silver ring with purple gems, 1 platinum necklace weighing 2 g, platinum necklace 1 white necklace weighing 2 g, 2 pairs of platinum earrings weighing 1 g, 7 purple gemstone necklaces, 1 idol necklace totaling about $ 2,500 were returned to the victim upon request with the approval of Mr. Riel Sophin, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court.
The suspect is currently being held in police custody at the Tuol Kork Police Inspectorate for questioning to build a case to be sent to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court for legal action.
