More than 10,000 light guns handed over to CMAC for neutralization and destruction
(Phnom Penh): A total of 11,915 defective firearms stored in the warehouse of the General Commission of National Police in Sangkat Prek Pra, Khan Chbar Ampov were handed over to the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) for neutralization and destruction. Technique.
The ceremony was held on the morning of March 1, 2019, presided over by Lt. Gen. Sek Phum, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, Representative of General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, and Mr. Heng Ratana, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General. CMAC.
Lt. Gen. Theam Bunseng, Director of the National Explosive Ordnance Disposal Department, spoke about the history of the process of collecting and disarming weapons and held 54 official Cambodian weapons destruction ceremonies, totaling nearly 220,000 weapons.
In addition, Lt. Gen. Sek Phoum highlighted that today's ceremony was part of the implementation of the Memorandum of Understanding on Cooperation between the National Police Commission and the Cambodian Mine Action Center to reduce the accident rate. Due to mines and explosive remnants of war, signed on June 21, 2018.
On behalf of the General Commission of the National Police, General Sek Phum thanked the Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center for paying attention to the implementation of the contract, accepting the request to destroy the defective weapons of the National Police and hope That the two sides will continue to implement more and more in the spirit of the Memorandum of Understanding.
In the near future, the General Commission of the National Police and CMAC will be able to arrange for the handover of some defective weapons that are currently being stored at the Capital and Provincial Police Offices and handed over to the local CMAC units for destruction. Techniques at any convenient time.
The CMAC Director General also praised the good cooperation between the National Police Commissioner and local National Police officers with CMAC officials, and he strongly hoped that the two sides would continue to strengthen and double their cooperation. In addition, to support the reduction of mine risk and explosive remnants of war and the sustainable development of the motherland of Cambodia.
