DPM Chea Sophara Holds a Meeting on Construction of New Phnom Penh Airport on 2,600 Hectares in Kandal and Takeo Provinces
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of February 28, 2018, Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of the Planning Committee for the Construction of the New Phnom Penh International Airport, chaired a meeting at the Ministry of Land Management. Work for the construction of the new airport.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Land Management, after the meeting, there are some results as follows:
1: Inform about the decision of the Royal Government to establish a new Phnom Penh International Airport, size 4F, on an area of 2,600 hectares, which can accommodate large aircraft, located in Kandal and Takeo provinces.
2: Assign duties to HE Mao Havannal, Minister in charge of the Secretariat of Civil Aviation, prepare an agreement to consult with relevant institutions and units and request a decision from the Royal Government to sign with Cambodia Airports Non-Private Company and study the safety zone of Flight.
3. Assign the task to support the construction project site, determine the location of the new Phnom Penh International Airport project, set up border posts, demarcate residential areas and building heights, prepare detailed urban planning and infrastructure plans.
5. Kandal Provincial Administration and Takeo Provincial Administration cooperate with working groups and companies to implement their roles and responsibilities to support the airport construction project in accordance with the decision of the Royal Government.
6. Assign the Kandal Provincial Administration, Takeo Provincial Administration and the General Department of Cadastral and Geography to clearly identify the people who have land in the project location based on the actual occupation and relevant documents to have a basis for addressing the impact. Citizens. The next step, as necessary, is to temporarily suspend the land flow in a location that causes difficulties and hinders the project implementation process.
7: Ask the relevant institutions to think in advance about the infrastructure, support the installation of gas pipelines, water supply network, electricity system, sewerage system, fiber optic system, sewage treatment plant properly before draining public sewers, telephone towers and other underground infrastructure to avoid Prepare after causing damage to roads, especially flood protection and relief systems.
8: Propose the company to establish a temporary office to work on the recruitment site from the base with the appropriate number of qualifications and qualifications to work necessary to implement the project. The next step can recruit additional staff according to the actual needs.
9. Encourage the use of local human resources, both experts and non-professionals to the fullest extent possible in the implementation of the new Phnom Penh International Airport construction project.
The duties of the site planning committee for the construction of the new Phnom Penh International Airport include:
* Review and determine the location standard for the new Phnom Penh International Airport construction project
* Study and evaluate the price of land in the area of the new Phnom Penh International Airport construction project
* Facilitate the resolution of land issues to facilitate the construction of the new Phnom Penh International Airport
Coordinate with relevant ministries, institutions and units of the Royal Government and companies to implement the project successfully
* Recommend the company to complete various procedures to meet the requirements for project implementation
* Review and advise on the master plan of the project, as well as other requests of the company, monitor and monitor the implementation of the project to build a new Phnom Penh International Airport and related infrastructure.
* Report the results to the Prime Minister for review and decision.
