25 Iraqi officials successfully complete demining training in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): 25 Iraqi officials from the Ministry of Interior, the Ministry of Health and Environment and a demining unit have successfully completed a training course on the use and maintenance of demining equipment in Cambodia.
This training course lasts for 33 days from January 14, 2019 to February 27, 2019, conducted by the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC), funded by the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA).
The Closing Ceremony of the Training Course was held at CMAC Phnom Penh under the chairmanship of Mr. Heng Ratana, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the General Director of CMAC.
CMAC officials said that after completing the training in Cambodia, Iraqi officials expressed satisfaction and appreciation to CMAC officials for their ability to train demining skills.
The same official confirmed that this is the fourth training course that CMAC has provided to trainees from Iraq, which is practical, both the use of machinery, maintenance, with explanations, the theory and practice at the minefield directly. .
During their training in demining skills in Cambodia, Iraqi officials expressed their happiness and gratitude to the International Cooperation Agency (JICA) for recruiting highly qualified and skilled Cambodian officers. In training to them.
After completing both theoretical and practical training in the real minefield, all trainees had to take a careful examination, with all 25 Iraqi officials getting good results. What is special is that Iraqi officials expressed their happiness during their studies in Cambodia, giving them a warm home.
The 25 Iraqi officials also paid a courtesy call on General Meas Sophea, Senior Minister in charge of Special Missions, and visited the Victory Monument to learn about the win-win policy of Cambodian Prime Minister Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
