Minister Ith Sam Heng: The Royal Government pays attention to women to become a driving force for socio-economic development
(Phnom Penh): In the celebration of the 108th anniversary of the International Women's Day on March 8, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia has paid great attention to promoting gender equality and Strengthen the empowerment of women and girls so that they can become a driving force in social and economic development.
The International Women's Day on March 8 is celebrated annually to commemorate the heroism of women around the world in demanding the promotion of democratic freedoms and the equal rights of men and women. Women in society.
In Cambodia, the International Women's Day on March 8, 2019 was held under the theme "Promoting Gender Equality and Social Protection for Human Resource Development". For the Ministry of Labor, the celebration of the 108th anniversary of International Women's Day was held on February 28, 2019 at the Ministry.
During the ceremony, Minister Ith Sam Heng said, "The Royal Government of Cambodia has paid great attention to promoting gender equality and empowering women and girls so that they can become a driving force." In social and economic development.
He said that the strategic goal of the Royal Government is to strengthen gender equality and social protection to improve the socio-economic situation and strengthen the role of women as the backbone of the economy and society.
The Royal Government has set out a comprehensive national social protection policy framework for 2016-2025, focusing on two pillars: the social assistance system and the social security system.
This policy framework will play an important role in increasing access to social assistance and social security services that are important to women:
First: Maternity workers receive 120% of their salary for 3 months. From January 1, 2018, the Royal Government has implemented a program to provide maternity allowances to 400,000 Riel per child, 800,000 Riel for twins and 1.2 million Riel for triplets. And received an additional 5 million Riels from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
Third, allowing pregnant women to leave at least 15 minutes early. In addition, all factories must set up nursing rooms for workers under 12 months of age and have nurseries for workers over 18 months of age. Every special economic zone or industrial park must have a nursery in its area.
Fourth, at the same time, all factories allow Cambodian Muslim women workers to wear traditional Islamic clothing.
Fifth, the Royal Government announced to provide allowances to women civil servants, police and the armed forces who gave birth, in which one child received 800,000 Riels, twins received 1,600,000 Riels, 3 twins received 2 400,000 Riels together with 3 months maternity leave with 100% salary.
All this shows that the Royal Government always pays high attention to women's education, from year to year, women always get more personal benefits and reduce the burden on the family more, which is to promote gender equality. Better in all areas in Cambodia. The Ministry of Labor in collaboration with Swisscontact holds a workshop on "Implementation of the Competency and Qualification Assessment System"
