(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Tourism has urged its inspectors to carry out their work effectively, especially to inspect tourism business establishments to encourage tour operators to apply for and renew their business licenses. Aims to ensure quality and efficient management of the tourism industry and services.
Mr. Prak Chandara, Inspector General of the Ministry of Tourism, said that the purpose of the workshop was to respond to the Ministry of Tourism's strategy to effectively and efficiently manage the tourism industry and services.
Mr. Prak Chandara continued that strengthening the capacity of inspectors who are qualified as judicial police is the most important and necessary factor for inspectors to have the full capacity to encourage all tourism service businesses to respect and enforce the law and regulations. Effective regulations in tourism.
Mr. Chea Bora praised that this workshop really contributed to the development of knowledge and important human resources in line with the Strategic Plan for Tourism Development 2012-2020, especially the strengthening of human resources on tourism inspection. To assist all inspectors, the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Tourism has made some recommendations:
* The General Inspectorate shall cooperate with the General Department of Tourism Industry Management to conduct inspections to encourage tourism operators to apply and renew their licenses.
Before and during the inspection, all inspection officers must check and study the law on tourism and other legal documents of the Ministry of Tourism clearly.
* Must cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions to take action and resolve irregularities in the tourism sector, and all inspections must be approved by the Minister of Tourism or the head of the institution.
* During the inspection, all units under the Ministry of Tourism must prepare an action plan to inspect and record clearly.
* Plan and organize short and medium term training courses for national and sub-national inspectors.
* Must strictly implement the internal regulations for inspection officers to complete the mission of the Capital-Provincial Department of Tourism.
* Continue to plan human resource training on regular inspection work.
Strengthen the implementation of discipline and duties of civil servants as stated in the content of the Law on the General Statute of Civil Servants of Cambodia and other legal documents in force, especially the strengthening of work discipline in the General Inspectorate.
On the other hand, in case of irregularities or contrary to the law on tourism, as well as regulations related to tourism, the General Secretariat, which is the direct staff of the Ministry of Tourism, shall be responsible for the inspection, inspection and investigation of all units under the Ministry and the business service base. Tourism.
