This morning, Samdech Techo Hun Sen met with members of the Supreme Advisory Council to review the achievements of the past 6 months.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of Thursday, 9 Roch Khemak, Samreth Sak 2562, which is on 28 February 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and the initiator of the Supreme Advisory Council. It will meet with members of the Supreme Advisory Council to review the work over the past six months to find ways to improve and enhance the efficiency of the Supreme Advisory Council.
The Supreme Advisory Council was established by Royal Decree dated September 6, 2018 at the request of Samdech Techo Hun Sen after the 6th National Election. The Supreme Advisory Council is composed of 16 of the 20 political parties that participated in the election.
After its establishment, the Supreme Advisory Council acted in accordance with its duties and responsibilities, including reviewing and advising on draft laws before submitting them to the Royal Government for review and decision. The Supreme Advisory Council also summoned the leaders of various ministries and institutions to inquire about some irregularities under the jurisdiction of those ministries and institutions.
In addition, members of the Supreme Advisory Council are seen to be actively working to resolve issues for the people, especially land disputes in the provinces. Mr. Chhim Phal Varun highly appreciated the activities of the Supreme Advisory Council by collecting a lot of input to the Royal Government to solve problems for the people and other problems in society.
According to Mr. Chhim Phal Varun, the meeting between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and the Supreme Advisory Council this morning was attended by Royal Government officials at the Deputy Prime Minister level and was broadcast on video to the provinces and military headquarters.
