Authority: Factories, warehouses serving the existing garment sector in the city do not need to be dismantled, but new factories need to be moved to the suburbs
(Phnom Penh): On February 27, 2019, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration met with the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC) to discuss the relocation of factories, enterprises, warehouses to serve all garment sectors in Phnom Penh.
After discussions, the two sides agreed as follows:
1: Establish a joint working group composed of the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC), the Cambodian Road Freight Association, to meet to determine the type and size of heavy trucks entering and leaving Phnom Penh, clearing the prohibited roads and setting departure times. To reduce traffic congestion in Phnom Penh.
2. This Joint Working Group will meet once a month or three months as necessary to discuss solutions to reduce traffic congestion in Phnom Penh and address the concerns of the Garment Manufacturers Association of Cambodia (GMAC) related. Jurisdiction of Phnom Penh Capital Administration.
3: For the construction of a factory with an area of less than 3,000 square meters (three thousand square meters), the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will facilitate the procedures through the OWSO service of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration in order to reduce the time to run faster. Construction.
