Members of the Supreme Advisory Council will raise the issue of land disputes and inactivity of officials to inform Samdech Techo Hun Sen tomorrow
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, who initiated the establishment of the Supreme Advisory Council, will hold a meeting with members of the Supreme Advisory Council on Thursday, February 28, 2019. Provide feedback to review the performance as well as some of the challenges that have occurred in the past 6 months.
The Supreme Advisory Council was established in September 2018 after the 6th National Election. The Supreme Advisory Council is composed of 16 of the 20 political parties that participated in the election.
Mr. Pich Sros, President of the Cambodian Youth Party, who is also a member of the Supreme Advisory Council, said that in the past six months, he has pushed for a solution to the problems of people affected by land disputes and made suggestions. Some to prevent illegal acts such as landslides.
Mr. Kong Monika, President of the Khmer Will Party and a member of the Supreme Advisory Council, said that his party delegation visited provinces such as Kratie, Stung Treng, Mondulkiri, Ratanakkiri, Svay Rieng, Kandal, Banteay Meanchey and Battambang to address land grabbing and Examine the lease of farmland by people along the border to Vietnam and the rights of indigenous peoples in the Northeast.
Mr. Kong Monika said that according to the direct observation and information provided by the people, there is still land rent along the border in the form of hiring Vietnamese to work as workers or guard the farmland.
In the past six months, there have been many challenges that representatives of each political party have faced, and the challenges are the same. Mr. Chhim Phalvarun, as well as Mr. Pich Sros and Mr. Kong Monika, all said that the challenge for the Supreme Council was the lack of cooperation from sub-national authorities.
Mr. Chhim Phalvarun said that the authorities at the sub-national level did not understand and did not know the role of the Supreme Advisory Council, which made the sub-national authorities less cooperative. Among them, some provincial governors, when meeting with members of the Supreme Advisory Council, did not meet or did not return.
Mr. Chhim Phalvarun considers this gesture as an insult to the members of the Supreme Advisory Council.
In tomorrow's semi-annual meeting, members of the Supreme Advisory Council are ready to raise their challenges as well as the inactivity of civil servants to inform Samdech Techo Hun Sen to find a solution.
In a meeting with Samdech Techo Hun Sen tomorrow, Mr. Pich Sros plans to propose to Samdech Techo to examine the feasibility of sub-national and sub-national work and to respect the work of members of the Supreme Advisory Council. Mr. Pich Sros will also request to speed up the work of the authorities to respond to the problems that have arisen, especially the problems of the people who are facing.
For Mr. Kong Monika, he plans to raise the issues that have actually been seen and urge to take effective measures and solutions on border work and land disputes. He will also promote the role and responsibilities of the Supreme Advisory Council to sub-national officials and change the attitude of officials in cooperation with the Supreme Advisory Council and acknowledge the mistakes and shortcomings of Body.
After the meeting, Mr. Chhim Phal Varun will hold a press conference to present the results of the meeting, followed by a joint dinner between Samdech Techo Hun Sen and members of the Supreme Advisory Council.
The two-day trial in the case of Lay Vannak and his partner has not been decided yet, the court will continue the trial on March 22.
(Phnom Penh): After two full days of cross-examination of four defendants and key witnesses in the murder of Lay Vannak's mistress, the court has not been able to conclude the hearing by postponing it. Again this morning, March 22, 2019.
The trial was presided over by Mr. Horm Mengse, Deputy President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, who presided over the Trial Chamber and was represented by Deputy Prosecutor Plong Sophal.
Please be informed that the trial of 4 defendants involved in the murder of the victim, Chev Sovathana, was held once on January 23, 2019, with the court questioning only Mr. Lay. Only one class. Lay Vannak once admitted that the victim and he were in love, but claimed that he did not kill her, she wanted to commit suicide.
Chim Vuth replied that the police arrested him in Borey Peng Huoth, Boeung Snor and showed the video that his wife and Men Samai had agreed to confess, so do not lie about Lay Vannak and Lay Narith being the victims. After questioning Chan Ry and Chim Vuth, the police detained them at Pov Sokhom Guesthouse around Chroy Changva for 22 days before arresting Lay Narith and Lay Vannak.
In response, Mr. Chiao Vibol and Mr. Pol Ratana denied the allegations in connection with the alleged torture of the accused. For Chim Vuth and Chan Ry to stay at Pov Sokhom Guesthouse is to provide security for witnesses with the permission of the prosecutor.
Please note that the court charged:
During the interrogation, the accused Lay Vannak described that on the night of January 25, 2018, one day before her death, he had a conversation with the victim because he was jealous that he had an extramarital affair. On the evening of January 26, 2018, the day of the incident, Lay Vannak went to see the victim at the house he rented, and then Lay Vannak and the victim had an argument because she was jealous of having another girl. And asked Lay Vannak to take her as his second wife openly.
Late in the evening, Chanry called again to say that the victim had hanged herself, so she used a Tai Kong car named Men Samai to visit and called back to tell her that she was really hanged. Lay Vannak He also confirmed that he had given this information and called Lay Narith, his brother and deputy commissioner, to help look at the scene.
It should be reminded that Mr. Koy Sao, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the evening of April 3, 2018, decided to issue a detention order for Mr. Lay Vannak, former Governor of Takeo Province and 3 other party members to be temporarily imprisoned. The other two were released because they were not involved.
