General WEI FENG HE, Member of the State Council and Minister of Defense of the People's Republic of China, said he was pleased to welcome the Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, Commander-in-Chief of the Army in Beijing.
He said that Sino-Cambodian relations are now at a peak and better than ever, especially under the leadership of President Xi Jinping and Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. He stressed that China fully supports Samdech Techo's leadership in maintaining peace, stability and development for the Cambodian people.
Lt. Gen. Hun Manet expressed his deep gratitude to General WEI FENG HE, Member of the State Council and Minister of Defense of the People's Republic of China, for his warm welcome to the Cambodian Army delegation and expressed his gratitude. Deep down to the Chinese government, army and people who have always supported and assisted Cambodia in developing both human resources and infrastructure.
The lieutenant general continued that the two countries continue to strengthen friendship and cooperation in all fields, in general, and in particular, the armies of the two countries, Cambodia and China will continue to strengthen friendship and cooperation in all fields. The lieutenant general requested that the Chinese side continue to support and assist Cambodia, especially in strengthening the capacity of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces.
It should be noted that at the invitation of the Ministry of National Defense of the People's Republic of China and to further strengthen the cooperation between the People's Armed Forces of the two countries, Cambodia-China Lt. Gen. Hun Manet led a high-level delegation of the Army. The Royal Cambodian Armed Forces (RCAF) will pay a five-day official visit to the People's Republic of China from February 25 to March 1, 2019.
