SEOUL (Reuters) - A South Korean Air Force fighter jet crashed into the country's western seas, but fortunately the two pilots on board flew a parachute and jumped out. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Wednesday evening, February 27, 2019.
A KF-16D fighter jet carrying two South Korean Air Force pilots crashed into the western waters of South Korea at noon Wednesday after taking off from an air base in the city. Gunsan, located about 270 km south of Seoul for training flights.
The exact cause of the crash has not been determined, but the two pilots jumped out of the plane and escaped unharmed.
