In 2018, Cambodian Customs and Excise collected 2.5 billion US dollars
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhim, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, said that in 2018, the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia earned more than 10 trillion riels from import tax. Equivalent to about 2.5 billion US dollars.
At the same time, the Deputy Prime Minister provided guidance for implementation in 2019, emphasizing nine points, including:
1. Must continue to strengthen good governance in the unit and professional ethics of customs and excise officials and must adhere to the five principles of Samdech Techo Prime Minister: mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, treatment and surgery.
2. Promote compliance with the private sector by strictly enforcing the customs code of the customs and encouraging companies that are highly compliant but punishing companies that violate the law.
3. Further trade facilitation needs to be provided to increase Cambodia's competitiveness, such as reducing and simplifying customs procedures through decentralization and the use of information technology.
4. Continue to strengthen the consultation mechanism with the private sector by listening to concerns and challenges and strive to find solutions within its jurisdiction.
5. Promote a culture of compliance and fiscal culture through the voluntary promotion of compliance, while taking measures to prevent and suppress all kinds of smuggling in all geographies of its jurisdiction on a regular basis.
6. Continue to strengthen the technical work of customs, tax policy, customs and continue to edit the Cambodian tariff schedule, assessment of impact on revenue, improvement of services in a friendly but decisive manner in law enforcement.
7. The draft strategy for promoting law enforcement and information technology strategies must be finalized, both of which are important and indispensable part of the reform and modernization of the customs administration.
8. To review and revise the sub-decree on trade facilitation through risk management and the sub-decree on prohibited and restricted goods, and to take measures to strengthen the roles and responsibilities in the context of institutional reform.
9. Must implement the Prakas on other customs fees and 50% reduction in scan fees from April 1, 2019 onwards.
