(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, in collaboration with the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism of Japan, this morning, February 27, 2019, organized a public-private forum on "Cambodia-Japan Urban Development." For the first time, to present opportunities to 60 companies from Japan to explore and be interested in investing in Cambodia.
The ceremony was held in the presence of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, Mr. Fumihiko YUKI, Deputy Minister of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism of Japan and Mr. BESSHO Kenichi, Chargé d'Affaires of the Embassy of Japan in Cambodia. Delegates from the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism of Japan, representatives of relevant ministries, institutions, 60 Japanese investment companies and businesses.
The special forum is also attended by investment companies in real estate development, construction, architecture, housing, drainage, banking and insurance, and the Board of Architects of Cambodia, the Board of Engineers of Cambodia, the Cambodian Chamber of Commerce, the Cambodian Builders Association, the Cambodian Builders Association, and the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors. Well, a lot of crowds, too.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of February 27, 2019, the Phnom Penh Municipal Court continued to hear the case of Lay Vannak, former Governor of Takeo Province and his brother, former Deputy Commissioner of Takeo Province, along with two other accomplices. Regarding the case of killing the widow of Chev Vathana, Lay Vannak's mistress, after a full day of hearings yesterday, no decision has been made yet.
The hearing was presided over by Mr. Horm Mengse, Deputy President of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and Chairman of the Trial Chamber, after Mr. Lay Vannak and his brother were escorted from PJ Prison to the Phnom Penh Municipal Court at 8:00 am to enter. The hearing.
According to the court official, the case of Lay Vannak and his accomplices involved in the trial is related to the murder of Chev Vathana, which took place at a rented house in Phsar village. Takeo, Sangkat Roka Knoung, Daun Keo City, Takeo Province on January 26, 2018.
It should be noted that during the hearing on the morning of January 23, 2019, the accused Lay Vannak confessed that he had been in love with Chev Sovathana, a widow with three children, in the name of a deep but secret couple. For more than a year until the day she died.
According to court officials, the hearing was held throughout the morning after the court had been investigating for more than nine months in the case of the murder of Chev Sovathana, and included Lay Vannak, the former governor of Takeo province and his cronies. Three defendants were arraigned in court on January 23, 2019.
It should be reminded that Mr. Koy Sao, Investigating Judge of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, on the evening of April 3, 2018, issued a detention order for Mr. Lay Vannak, former Governor of Takeo Province and three other party members. The other two were released because they were not involved.
(Phnom Penh): The restaurant "Garden" with Mr. Lou Meng as CEO has won a special award from the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen for green business in tourism.
The award ceremony was held on the occasion of Samdech Techo Hun Sen presiding over the celebration of the 7th National Clean City Day under the theme "Clean City: A Warm City" at the Sokha Residence Hotel. Phnom Penh.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen was honored to present the 7th Special Award "Samdech Techo Prime Minister Award for Green Business in Tourism" 2018-2019 to Mr. Lou Meng, Executive Director of "Garden" restaurant.
(Phnom Penh): According to the report from the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police, on February 26, 2019, there were 18 traffic accidents nationwide, resulting in 6 deaths and injuries. 11 minor and 17 seriously injured.
According to the same source, in these 18 traffic accidents, 12 motorcycles, 9 cars and 8 trucks were damaged, and the causes of the accidents included speeding, not following the right, Turn dangerous, drunk, disrespectful and competitive.
