60 Japanese companies interested in investing in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism of Japan held a Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on "Establishment of Public-Private Forum on Cambodia-Japan Urban Development" in the afternoon. This is February 26, 2019.
The signing ceremony of the "Establishment of a Public-Private Forum on Cambodia-Japan Urban Development" was held under the chairmanship of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Mr. Fumihiko YUKI, Deputy Minister of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism of Japan.
Starting from this Memorandum of Understanding on the morning of February 27, 2019, the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction, in collaboration with the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism of Japan, will organize a private public forum on the development of urban planning in Cambodia. Japan for the first time in the presence of Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara and with the participation of Mr. Fumihiko YUKI.
As planned, the event will also be attended by a delegation from the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure, Transport and Tourism of Japan, representatives of the Japanese Embassy in Cambodia, representatives of relevant ministries, institutions, about 60 Japanese companies and investors interested in investing in Cambodia. .
(Siem Reap): To celebrate the National Day of Maternal, Infant and Child Health on February 26, 2019, the working group of the Cambodian Red Cross Branch Committee led by Mrs. Teang Eng Tea Seiha, Vice Chairman of the Branch Committee Conversation, visit and bring the humanitarian donations of the branch to the mothers of 59 newborns at Prey Chrouk Health Center and Sastamna in Puok District, Siem Reap Province.
Ms. Teang Eng Tea Seiha is determined to visit women, mothers, infants, children and people in all 100 communes / sangkats in 12 districts / municipalities in Siem Reap, and she requested that all mothers After giving birth, breastfeed your baby so that the baby has a better physical and mental development, protecting the baby against various diseases.
Today's visit is for the purpose of promoting and caring for the health of mothers, infants and children, and to support His Excellency Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and a national figure of the Joint Action Plan. United Nations for the Health of Women and Children.
Today, she also met with the accused, defendants and convicts, women with small children and 15 pregnant women in Siem Reap Provincial Prison.
Lt. Gen. Di Vichea Closes a Training Course on Security Skills at Kampong Thom Provincial Police
(Kampong Thom): Lieutenant General Di Vichea, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police and Director of the Central Security Department, representing General Santi Bandith Neth Savoeun, Commissioner of the National Police, presides over the closing ceremony of the refresher course on February 27, 2019. Provide experience in security work at Kampong Thom Provincial Police.
Lt. Gen. Di Vichea stated that the two-day training course on security skills was held from 26 to 27 February 2019 at Kampong Thom Provincial Police with trainees as police. National Security Plan at 150 District / Municipal Inspectorates and 81 Post Stations throughout Kampong Thom Province: 150 people, 3 females.
He added that this training is in line with the plan of the Central Security Department set out in 2019 to organize this security training course in 25 capitals and provinces throughout Cambodia.
Drought! Minister of Rural Development requests professional officers to inspect water sources for measures to maintain protection for people to use
(Kampong Chhnang): In order to reduce water shortage due to drought, Dr. Ouk Rabun, Minister of Rural Development, requested experts to inspect local water sources to take preventive measures to allow people to use in Daily life.
The request was made on the occasion of Dr. Ouk Rabun presiding over the closing ceremony of the meeting to summarize the work results of 2018 and the work direction for 2019 of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Administration on February 26, 2019. The ceremony was also attended by Mr. Chhour Chandoeun, Governor of Kampong Chhnang Province and many other stakeholders.
Speaking at the event, Dr. Ouk Rabun said that based on the forecast for this year, Cambodia may have hot and dry weather and the dry season will last longer than previous years.
"In the face of this natural phenomenon, the provincial administration must coordinate with the municipal, district, commune and sangkat administrations to monitor local water sources, both for daily use and for growing in the dry season," he said.
Dr. Ouk Rabun added that it is necessary to evaluate the period of use of these water sources in order to take measures to maintain, protect and use these remaining water sources economically and give priority to use in people's daily lives. .
At the same time, be prepared to intervene to solve the water problem for the local people who have a shortage of water for daily use, without leaving the victims due to the shortage of water for daily use. This is the additional emphasis of the Minister of Rural Development.
He added that in addition, the Department of Health and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries must co-educate local people on health care, prevention of communicable diseases in humans and livestock on farms and prepare Intervention measures to treat both human and pet diseases in a timely manner.
At the same time, the Minister said that people need to be educated to be more vigilant in preventing fires on houses, plantations and participate in preventing wildfires in the dry season. Fire authorities must inspect fire trucks and firefighting equipment to prepare for timely intervention.
According to General Chhum Socheat, spokesman for the Cambodian Ministry of National Defense, the exercise was aimed at strengthening good cooperation between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Chinese People's Liberation Army to exchange experiences in joint humanitarian relief work. Disasters, counter-terrorism, peacekeeping, and so on.
The General also stated that this exercise is also to reflect the position of the Royal Government, especially the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces in the implementation of defense policy between Cambodia and China on international cooperation to help each other in all fields and all angles.
