The main weapons used in this year's Golden Dragon exercise include: armored vehicles, tanks, artillery, mortars, helicopters and aerial support.
Battambang Provincial Court issues arrest warrant for fortune teller in case of $ 240,000 fraud
(Battambang): Battambang Provincial Court Judge Loy Chantra has sentenced a woman fortune teller to nine months in prison and fined her $ 50,000. The mastermind, who is the nephew of the victim, was acquitted by the court for not having enough evidence in the $ 240,000 fraud case.
The victim, Chang Kimny, a resident of Kor Than village, Sangkat O'Ambel, Serey Sophorn city, Banteay Meanchey province, stated that after he heard the verdict in the court hearing on February 25, 2019 that the scammer was a nephew. He was acquitted. Separately, Chea Sinath was ordered to pay $ 240,000 and $ 50,000 in damages and was sentenced to nine months in prison.
The victim continued that on February 25, 2019, he was dissatisfied with the announcement of the verdict by Loy Chantra, Judge of the Battambang Provincial Court, who decided to drop the charges against the accused. In the case of fraud up to $ 240,000 during July 2017.
Defendant Mech Kamnit, a 40-year-old male resident of Banteay Meanchey Province, was also the victim's nephew and conspired with another accomplice, Chea Sinath (acting as a fortune teller and impersonator), involved in two fraud cases. A total of $ 240,000 from the victim, who is in an elderly condition with a chronic disease.
At the same time, the victim urged his superiors to intervene and provide justice to him as a real victim, so that there would be no forgiveness for those who planned to commit the crime by themselves. Named after the idea of being his nephew.
In relation to the above case, Ms. Teang Sambo, Director of Administration and Spokesperson of Battambang Provincial Court, said that the name of the concept was announced by the court verdict No. 145. H. Dated February 25, 2019, stating that the name Mich Knam was acquitted, but Chea Sinath, the court ordered the victim to pay $ 240,000 and $ 50,000 in damages. Sentenced to 9 months.
