Lt. Gen. Hem Theng emphasized that after the deadline of June 30, 2019, if foreigners continue to use the Cambodian identity card or other relevant documents, it is a criminal offense to face. Imprisoned because before the deadline, all documents were typed in the appendix and were completely dismissed.
This statement was made by Lt. Gen. Hem Theng this morning, February 27, 2019, on the occasion of Mr. and Mrs. You Saphea, Deputy Governor of Siem Reap Province, Lt. Gen. Tith Narong, Siem Reap Provincial Commissioner, chaired a meeting to expedite the meeting. Disseminate the implementation of the sub-decree on the cancellation and confiscation of irregular Cambodian administrative documents that foreigners are occupying and using at the Siem Reap Provincial Police.
In the above meeting, Ms. You Sophea, Deputy Governor, requested the relevant authorities and authorities to cooperate and widely disseminate to the foreigners who are currently using and remaining to apply for a declaration and apply for a permanent residence permit. In the implementation of Sub-Decree No. 129 dated 15 August 2017 on the cancellation and confiscation of irregular Cambodian administrative documents.
Lt. Gen. Hem Theng stated that the cancellation and confiscation of all irregular Cambodian administrative documents held by foreigners is a new policy of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, to control and eliminate the rumors. That Cambodia has illegal immigrants.
Lt. Gen. Hem Theng added that in order for the implementation of the work to be smooth and successful, the Royal Government of Cambodia has established an inter-ministerial working group with four ministries: First, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs has supervised National and international law, second: the Ministry of Justice with the judiciary, third: the Council of Jurists of the Office of the Council of Ministers, and fourth: the Ministry of Interior, the General Department of Immigration.
The same lieutenant general also called on all immigration authorities to cooperate with relevant officials to carry out transparent and accurate work in order to respect the law of the Kingdom of Cambodia and avoid living without the recognition of the authorities and Royal Government of Cambodia.
Of these, 670 irregular Cambodian administrative documents were confiscated, including 392 residence books (A2), 53 family books (A4), 133 birth certificates / birth certificates, 4 marriage certificates, 81 Khmer identity cards, 7 passports. Garbage collection business owner in Memot district asks the provincial governor to help find justice after the business was confiscated for unknown reasons
(Tbong Khmum): The owner of Memot district sanitation business, Ms. Phuong Bopha, asked Mr. Tbong Khmum provincial governor Cheam Chansophoan to help find justice after the governor of Memot district gave others the right to do garbage collection business while he was doing this business.
Ms. Phuong Bopha told Fresh News that she has been licensed to do sanitation business in Memot district since 2012, but on January 1, 2019, a new business owner was recently found to have done so. The activity of taking garbage trucks in Memot district, while she received the right to continue the business issued by the Tbong Khmum Provincial Department of Environment.
Ms. Phuong Bopha said that after the incident, she asked Mr. Meng Bunnara, the governor of Memot district, but the district governor said that he had made a notice to stop her business.
According to Ms. Phuong Bopha, he did not receive the notification from the Memot District Governor until February 26, 2019.
Ms. Phuong Bopha said that she had previously written to the Tbong Khmum provincial governor to help find justice, but as of February 26, 2019, she has not yet received a solution.
