Announcing the appointment of the Director of the Intelligence Department of the General Commission of the National Police, Major General Hun Samnang to replace the retired Lt. Gen. Hippo
(Phnom Penh): Major General Hun Samnang has been officially announced as the new Director of the Intelligence Department of the National Police, replacing Lt. Gen. Hippu, who has been retired.
The inauguration ceremony was held on the morning of February 27, 2019, presided over by General Thong Lim, Deputy Commissioner of the National Police, on behalf of General Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner.
Speaking on the occasion, General Thong Lim, on behalf of General Neth Savoeun, thanked Lt. Gen. Hippu, a former intelligence officer who had been retired while exhausted. Work according to their duties as assigned by the management.
In addition, General Thong Lim also instructed Major General Hun Samnang, the newly-appointed Director of the Intelligence Department, to work hard to do what his superiors trusted and entrusted him. In addition, there must be unity within the unit without any partisanship.
The General Commission of the National Police will upgrade the skills of private security agencies across the country, more than 2,000 security guards receive training a year
(Phnom Penh): Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department of the National Police, said that the Private Security Management Department, which is the staff of the National Police General Commission, will provide skills training to private security agencies across the country to increase and Strengthen capacity.
During the opening ceremony of the 12th Private Security Agency Training Course, which was attended by nearly 200 participants this morning, February 27, 2019, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharasmey said that during the 12 sessions of the National Police. Trained more than 2,000 private security agents nationwide.
According to the director of the department, all these factors are why the Ministry of Interior as well as the General Commission of the National Police always pay the most attention to this private security sector, which is a sector that has grown significantly in line with the national development. In all areas.
