(Phnom Penh): A man driving a truck with no steering wheel crashed into people's houses, causing some property damage, but fortunately this incident did not cause any casualties.
This incident happened at more than 12 midnight on February 27, 2019 along Street 217 at the traffic light of Thnal Bot Market, Sangkat Dangkor, Khan Dangkor, Phnom Penh.
After the incident, the local police arrived and contacted the professional police to bring the car and store it at the Phnom Penh Road Traffic Office, waiting for a legal settlement later.
CMAC Signs Agreement with Japan's JMAS to Implement Mine and Cluster Clearance Project in Santuk District, Kampong Thom Province
(Phnom Penh): On the afternoon of Tuesday, February 26, 2019, Mr. Heng Ratana, Director General of the Cambodian Mine Action Center, participated in the signing ceremony of the cooperation agreement between CMAC and JMAS are launching a demining and cluster munitions clearance project with more than $ 310,000 in machinery support.
Mr. Heng Ratana confirmed that this project has a period of one year from March 1, 2019 to February 28, 2020 in Santuk district, Kampong Thom province, which is the second year of the project.
He added that in addition to demining work, this project also focuses on the development of physical infrastructure, such as: repairing roads, digging ponds, digging wells and canals.
It should be noted that SIMAC and JMAS have been cooperating for more than 17 years, since 2002, with the majority of JMAS leaders being former leaders of the Japanese Armed Forces, including the former Commander-in-Chief of the Japanese Armed Forces.
