Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration: The problem of liquid waste into the sea continues to be addressed as a priority to reduce to a minimum
(Preah Sihanouk): With the support of the national level, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration has prepared and rehabilitated sewage canals in front of the provincial hall to reduce the impact of beaches and seawater caused by liquid waste. As a solution, the provincial technical team decided to dig the canals to contain the sewage and put EM substances to convert the odor before discharging into the sea.
In fact, on the afternoon of January 25, 2019, Mr. Chiao Vicheak, Deputy Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and Chairman of the O'Pralay Technical Working Group, led a team from the Department of Public Works and Transport, the Department of Environment, and the Department of Water Resources to carry out this work.
Mr. Chiao Vicheak confirmed that the rehabilitation of the canal now is to maintain the reservoir before the sewage into the sea, and the canal to be restored is 100 meters long and 15 meters wide. Through this measure, he said, it will reduce the smell of dirty water to a certain level before flowing into the sea.
Mr. Chiao Vicheak added that under the guidance of the Governor of Sihanoukville, he urged the team to collect water from the Star Canal to collect wastewater around the area, such as from Kamsap to O'Mario. Go to sea as much as possible.
According to the official of the Department of Public Works, the technique of lifting the soil into the dam and then placing the EM into the wastewater to improve the water quality before discharging into the sea and in the future. This one will be prepared to be a wastewater pumping station, continuing to the first station in Ochheuteal.
