Health officials call on pharmacists to abide by professional ethics and other laws to avoid legal confrontation (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh) Pharmacists across the country must respect professional ethics, respect the laws and regulations of medicine and other laws to improve the health of the people, especially to avoid facing the law.
This statement was made by Pharmacist Ban Bota during the census of Phnom Penh Pharmacists on February 25, 2019.
"So far, a total of 3,300 pharmacists across the country have come to conduct the census to obtain the registration of nearly 2,000 Cambodian pharmacists, so those who have not yet come," he said. Census, please come and do the census for everyone. ”
On the other hand, this census to know the number of pharmacists across the country and whether they adhere to the code of ethics or not, because it is a necessary benefit to help the Ministry of Health and to help improve the health of the people, including promoting the pharmaceutical sector. We are also growing.
At the same time, Mr. Ban Botda appealed to all pharmacists who have not yet come to the census or know the news, and please hurry to participate in the census in time to set clear goals and hand out registration certificates to all.
Mr. Ban Bota stated that those who did not take the census will not be able to obtain the Certificate of Registration of the Board of Pharmacists of Cambodia from the National Council of Pharmacists, and for those who do not comply with the rules and regulations of the Board of Pharmacists of Cambodia and will violate the law. Medicines The law governing any professional is subject to delisting from the list of the Cambodian Pharmacists Association and to face the law in force.
The former opposition leader, who is also the former president of the Sam Rainsy Party and a senior adviser to the former CNRP, has claimed that the suspension or removal of the EBA was a decision to serve the ambitions of Sam Rainsy prisoners and put the hardships of the innocent at large. .
In a letter to the EU Ambassador on 25 February 2019, Kong Koam congratulated Cambodia on its commitment to the work of the European Union (EU) and the interests of Cambodia, as well as businesses, producers and groups. Loyal EBA related money users of the EU Representative to Cambodia.
Mr. Kong Koam said that the claim of the EU Ambassador representing the decision to suspend or withdraw the EBA from Cambodia was not politically motivated and was not immediately enforced (at least six months or until the end of the procedure). That year 2019) is helping stakeholders, especially those who are trying to save the EBA, have prepared in advance the necessary work for further growth and, in particular, helped to avoid unrest from various circles in Cambodia.
Mr. Kong Koam also described the progress made on the political situation in Cambodia by deciding to bring Mr. Kem Sokha from the Trapeang Road Detention Center to his home, as well as to amend the law to open the way for political prisoners. Re-do politics and so on.
Mr. Kong Koam stated, "I am confident that His Excellency noted the change in the detention of Mr. Kem Sokha, the only legitimate President of the CNRP, from Trapeang Phlong Prison to his own residence in Phnom Penh and the amendment of the law." "On political parties, 118 banned CNRP leaders can regain their political rights before the Supreme Court ruling."
In the letter, Kong Kong stated that both he and the EU Ambassador were hopeful that the situation of democracy and respect for human rights in Cambodia would continue to develop in a positive way. However, he also expressed regret that Sam Rainsy and a handful of Sam Rainsy activists had used Kem Sokha and other detainees as a means of preventing the democratic space and human rights situation from getting better and faster as desired by the media.
As a former senior adviser to the former CNRP, Kong Koam stated that he regretted that in the end the EU proceedings decided to suspend or withdraw the EBA from Cambodia. He said that if such a decision is implemented, it will not uphold the EU's principles for the development of Cambodia to grow stronger towards promoting true democracy and promoting respect for human rights.
However, Kong Koam expressed strong hope that the EU Ambassador to Cambodia would continue his firm and sincere commitment to the EU that the decision to suspend or withdraw the EBA from Cambodia now is Serving Sam Rainsy's ambitious ambitions and dropping the hardships of the general innocent only.
