Preah Vihear Governor Warns Against Illegal Handicrafts Near Forest Conservation Area
(Preah Vihear): In the spirit of participating in the protection of natural resources to survive, Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, instructed environmental officials to protect the protected areas to prevent trees from falling. If the trees are cut down, we will face the loss of natural resources and the loss of land.
At the same time, he also ordered professional officers and local authorities to crack down on illegal handicrafts, especially handicrafts nearby and conservation areas.
Separately, village-commune authorities must not issue certificates on illegal possession of forest land. The provincial governor also recommended cracking down on illegal wood processing factories, especially those near and in protected areas. For legal handicrafts, it is necessary to check the source of the wood, where does the wood come from? From which company? Is there a pie?
