(Prey Veng): Senior Minister Him Chhem, Minister of Cults and Religions, on February 25, 2019, attended the closing ceremony of the 27th General Assembly of Priests in Prey Veng Province with the participation of Chief Preah Anukon, Monks and Preah Thera-Nutthera: All of them, as well as leaders and local authorities at all levels.
Speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Him Chhem stated that Buddhism has really contributed to the building of the society, so the results of the discussion, let the monks of all levels of Buddhism at all levels adhere to all those principles to be a beacon. The path for educating the morality of the next generation of Buddhists, based on the spirit of compassion to be consistent in all circumstances.
In order to contribute to the program of the 27th General Assembly of Priests in Prey Veng Province, Senior Minister Him Chhem has made the following recommendations:
* First, the Provincial Priests at all levels must work together in the ranks of the Provincial Priests to unite in fulfilling their hierarchical duties in order to serve Buddhism in the provinces and contribute to the development of the country in accordance with the policy of the Royal Government in the fourth phase. Sixth Legislature of the National Assembly under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
* Second: Let the clergy at all levels cooperate with the specialized departments and local authorities at all levels to fulfill their duties, solve and calm down all the abbots in Buddhism in accordance with the Buddha's precepts, the precepts, the precepts and special state laws. Must abide by the Royal Proclamation of the 27th National Congress of Priests, as well as the Circulars and Priests.
* Thirdly, the provincial priests must pay attention to expand the dissemination of the Dharma through the program "Buddhism connects with society" to help Buddhists to do good deeds, adhere to the truth in society, avoid all kinds of sins.
* Fourth: May Theranut Thera: All of you must continue to make efforts to pay attention to the study of Dharma and Vinaya in order to practice it properly as a field for a place of worship for Buddhists.
And 5: There must be good tolerance with Buddhists, know how to get along with Buddhists in general and do not adhere to the trend of color, status, rich or poor. Elephants continue to be hunted by hunters, one elephant dies from hunters
(Mondulkiri): The body of a wild elephant was found in the cashew plantation of the people in Sre Levi village, Sre Khtom commune, Keo Seima district, Mondulkiri province. Caused by a shot by a hunter. This was confirmed by Mr. Keo Sopheak, Director of the Provincial Department of Environment and Mr. Net Pheaktra, spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, confirmed to Fresh News on February 25.
After a thorough autopsy on the elephant's body on February 24, experts found that the elephant was a male, not a female, and had a bullet wound to the head. About 1 sting from the eyes.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Environment added that officials were also monitoring and investigating to find those involved in the shooting. The dead elephants will be buried in a safe place to preserve their skeletons for further scientific research on biodiversity benefits.
It should be noted that the male elephant that was killed was found by the park officials in the late night of February 23, until the morning of February 24, 2019, then the professional officer can bring other materials to work. An autopsy found the cause of its death. This elephant weighs about 2 tons and is 2.70 meters high, 4.50 meters long and 1.50 meters wide.
According to wildlife officials, between 375 and 500 wild elephants are currently living in Mondulkiri province, and herds often flock to the village for food. This is not the first time that wild elephant carcasses have been found.
After the incident, Mr. Svay Sam Eang, Governor of Mondulkiri Province, confirmed to the relevant departments or units in this province to prevent all crimes, especially all kinds of wildlife crimes. He said that please do not forgive and go to search and arrest the perpetrators to be punished. Japan Provides Nearly $ 930,000 Grant to Two Units in Cambodia for Pediatric Surgery Project and Mechanical Clearance Transfer Project
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Japan has provided grants totaling $ 925,630 to two units under the Grant Scheme for Japanese NGO projects.
The signing ceremony for the grant took place on February 25, 2019 at the Embassy of Japan, in which the Japanese side was represented by Mr. Horino Uchihi Hidehisa, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, and the Japanese NGO side was represented by Ms. Yumiko Minami, Director of the Foundation for International Development and Relief in Cambodia;
* First: Kratie Pediatric Laboratory Project and Demining and Cluster Munitions Clearance (Year 1), $ 237,666. Recipient Unit, Foundation for International Development and Relief in Cambodia (FIDR).
In this project, JMAS will develop mechanical clearance techniques using deminers, cluster munitions, and dumpsters in areas rich in mixed and cluster munitions. JMAS will transfer effective and safe clearance methods to the Cambodian Mine Action Center (CMAC) in order to strengthen the capacity and accelerate CMAC's efforts to secure the country.
For JMAS, the Japanese government provides about $ 687,000 for JMAS, Horinouchi Hidehisa said. The organization will transfer the technology for the use of cluster munitions and drones in areas rich in landmines and mixed cluster munitions to CMAC. Through this project, he strongly hopes that the people living in the area will be free from the fear of landmines and explosive remnants and will contribute to further development in the region.
Mr. Eng Hee: Military and military officers who kicked and beat people during the execution of the land order in Sihanoukville have filed a case to the court
(Preah Sihanouk): Violent incident during the execution of a land case in Preah Sihanouk province in January 2019, a military officer and a military officer who kicked and beat people with guns were charged. The court while some other military police officers were disciplined. This was confirmed by Brigadier General Eng Hee, spokesman for the National Gendarmerie.
In a press conference at the Sihanoukville Provincial Gendarmerie Headquarters this morning, February 25, 2019, Mr. Eng Hee said that after a thorough investigation, the National Gendarmerie Disciplinary Council. Decided to discipline 5 military police officers, including:
Third: Mr. Puth Chan is a member of the Gendarmerie in Sihanoukville. Mr. Puth Chan did not use violence, but he was still at the scene of the violence. As a law enforcement officer, he witnessed the violence and did not detain the perpetrators, but received written discipline.
Fourth: Mr. Sek Kompheak is a member of the Gendarmerie in Sihanoukville. Mr. Sek Kumpheak disobeyed the order by detonating an AK-47 assault rifle and fired four shots, subject to written discipline.
Fifth: Mr. Sim Veasna is an office assistant and a member of the Gendarmerie in Sihanoukville. Mr. Sim Veasna did not specifically obey the order and detonated a Mac 98 assault rifle, firing two shots.
Mr. Eng Hee said that in the operation to participate in the implementation of the Supreme Court ruling on January 24, 2019, there were 100 members of the Royal Gendarmerie, 10 long weapons and 6 small arms.
Eng Hee said that the victim, who was shot and was being treated at the hospital, has now recovered, but his lower limbs have not been able to move. Doctors are continuing to focus on treating victims.
According to the confessions of military and military officials who used violence against the victims, Eng Hee stated that the violence was because they were so angry with the people that they fired rubber bullets and stones at them. Use violence in return.
In this morning's press conference, Eng Hee also publicly apologized on behalf of the military and military officers to the victims of the forces' misconduct.
He said that since then, all forces have gone through a lot of education, especially he and his team also went directly across the country, instructing them to take the role to serve the people or the people. It is right to consider the people as the owners, because the people are the ones who pay taxes to the state in order to get money to pay the salaries of the forces every month. Therefore, military officers must serve the people well.
