The ceremony was presided over by Dr. Aun Porn Moniroth, Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance and Chairman of the Steering Committee for Public Financial Reform on the morning of February 25, 2019 with the participation of Ministry leaders. Economy and Finance, Representatives of the Departments of Economy and Finance of the 25 capitals and provinces, Representatives of ministries and institutions, a total of 230 people.
He noted that the significant progress made in implementing the FMIS project from 2014 to date is the backbone and has contributed significantly to the progress of the public financial management reform program. Face with a solid foundation for achieving the goal of 2025 is "Accountability Achievement".
"This is a source of pride for Cambodia's public financial management reform program because we are doing better and faster than some other countries, according to the World Bank," he said. "This" progress and achievement "is the result of our collective efforts based on gathering, discussing and working together in a team spirit."
This year, 2019, under the Public Financial Management Reform Program, the Ministry of Economy and Finance has launched an action plan to streamline the implementation procedures in the FMIS system, which clearly defines the procedures to ensure compliance with "Strategy for budget reform 2018-2025."
1. Management and budgeting and finance officers must participate in a proactive and interactive spirit with high will, alertness and ownership, especially from the management and members of the FMIS project implementation team in the Ministry. Institutions.
2: Prepare and recruit officers who must use FMIS system according to the needs and professional skills, avoid taking officials who are not involved or have the wrong function, as well as encourage and encourage subordinates to participate in various training courses organized. Within the framework of the public financial management reform program, especially in the FMIS project.
3: To consider, analyze and clearly define the number of leaders and officers to be assigned as users of FMIS to prevent additional requests and changes of users of the system that can cause complications both in the training and when using System.
4. Examine the necessary legal and regulatory bases that need to be prepared for improvements to support the effective use of FMIS, especially streamlining procedures in their institutions to reduce potential complications. Available when FMIS is launched.
5: Prepare the workplace and its FMIS project implementation team to work closely with the FMIS management team of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and work together as a team to achieve success on site. Each and according to the action plan set out.
