Highlights of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's Speech on the Occasion of Presiding over the Celebration of the 7th "Clean City Day"
(Phnom Penh): On February 25, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, presided over the celebration of the 7th "Clean City Day" under the theme "Clean City: A Warm City". At Sokha Hotel, Phnom Penh.
The event was attended by senior officials of the Royal Government of Cambodia, leaders of the Ministry of Tourism, leaders in the 25 provincial capitals operating in the tourism sector, as well as a number of relevant partner organizations.
The following are the main contents of Samdech Techo Hun Sen's speech at the celebration of the 7th "Clean City Day":
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his congratulations and appreciation for the achievements of the Ministry of Tourism and the National Committee for Clean City Assessment in the past, especially the initiative to have a clean city competition, clean resort, good service, hospitality. Good at both national and ASEAN levels.
* Samdech Techo praised the leaders of civil servants, ministries, institutions, the private sector, the people, the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and development partners who always provide good cooperation and actively support the development of sustainable tourism in Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, stated that through the reassessment, Cambodia's economic growth in 2018 was up to 7.5% and the poverty rate has been reduced to around 10%. Cambodia has now become a popular tourist destination in the world and the Royal Government considers tourism as green gold.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister stated that in 2018, Cambodia received a total of 6.2 million international tourists, an increase of 11.5% from 110 countries around the world. In 2019, Cambodia is expected to receive about 6.8 million international tourists and is expected to reach 7.5 million international arrivals in 2020 and 15 million in 2030.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that while the Cambodian economy is proudly growing, the living standards of the people have been steadily improving, stabilizing the annual demographic growth rate at around 1% to 1.5%. And by 2030, the population of Cambodia is projected to reach 20 million and reach 25 million by 2050, when most people will come to live in cities and towns.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the launch of the Clean City Competition, Clean Resort, Good Service, Good Hospitality is a joint thinking, joint action, joint responsibility, adhering to the concept of the future, the present, which we all need to consider in time. Now to create competitive excellence and ensure sustainable development.
* Samdech Techo Prime Minister reminded that in order to continue to develop cities throughout Cambodia as a clean, green, sustainable development and smart tourism city in response to the 2030 Agenda for Sustainable Development of the United Nations. Our nation needs to work together to develop a more sustainable city in line with the slogan Clean City: The city provides warmth to its people and national and international tourists.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen announces Clean City Campaign: Provide Warmth as a National Agenda to Prepare to Host the 2023 SEA Games and Achieve 2030 Sustainable Development Goals by Implementing Five Priority Work Programs Includes:
First. Increase the attractiveness and vibrancy of cities through the use of technology to create smart cities (Smart City) by establishing a specific policy framework on sustainable urban development towards 2030 and 2050. Meanwhile, the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications must provide free Wi-Fi (Free Wifi) in each tourist destination, especially in Phnom Penh, Siem Reap, Sihanoukville, Battambang before 2023.
Second. To increase the attractiveness and vibrancy of the city by ensuring clean and green Cambodia is clean Cambodia Green Cambodia Clean habits of clean homes, clean villages, clean neighborhoods that start from all of us. Taking this opportunity, I would like to congratulate the first ASEAN Public Toilet winner and the first Cambodian Public Toilet winner for their contribution to the promotion of cleanliness and hygiene.
Third. To make the city more attractive and vibrant, we need to think about public order. I would like to ask the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of Land Management, Urban Planning and Compensation to prepare a law on public order to reduce traffic congestion in the city. At the same time, authorities at all levels of sub-national administration must ensure that their cities are in good order, have proper parking, and have sidewalks to facilitate the travel of people and tourists.
* Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, called on the people, ministries, institutions, authorities at all levels, especially the sub-national administration, the private sector, development partners and all stakeholders to support and promote the clean city competition movement to be active and comprehensive. Promote the development of a green economy in Cambodia to be more vibrant and sustainable.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called on people not to be shocked about rabies and to seek vaccination services until the Institut Pasteur provides services. Samdech Techo pointed out that some people did not even have a dog bite and were surprised to get vaccinated.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also recommended the deployment of vaccines in hospitals in the provincial capital or the possibility of private clinics providing additional immunization services.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen called for the creation of a national movement from children to adults to participate in maintaining a clean environment.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called for joint prevention of infectious diseases and efforts to maintain hygiene in order to ensure that Cambodia remains a tourist destination without fear of infectious diseases.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called for joint prevention of the fight against terrorism to ensure Cambodia's tourism destinations.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen praised the tourism police, heritage officials for their hard work in keeping the tourists safe.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also called for joint maintenance of political and social stability in Cambodia, because no tourists to visit the country is in turmoil.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that the effort to attract tourists to visit Cambodia is a good thing, but continue to make tourists come to visit once and want to visit again and bring friends and relatives to visit again is better .
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that food hygiene is also important for tourists. Samdech Techo supported the establishment of the "Food Street" competition movement. Samdech Techo Hun Sen considers this movement as a contribution to improving food hygiene on the streets.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen also urged people to grow vegetables and raise animals to supply tourists.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges the use of local agriculture to serve tourists.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Japanese farmers have worked hard to cultivate for local supply and export.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges the tourism sector to determine the market in hotels to bring farmers' agricultural products to supply in those hotels.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that in 1994, Samdech was responsible for the tragedy of the French, British and Australian who had an accident while traveling by train to visit Cambodia.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urges the construction of more infrastructure systems, including roads along the border, to facilitate the travel of tourists.
* Samdech Techo Hun Sen urged all sub-national authorities to pay attention and encourage people to cultivate and raise animals for supply to tourist sites or hotels.
