(Battambang): Mr. Lim Kean Hor, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, this morning, February 24, 2019, accompanied by the Director of the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Battambang Province, continued to inspect the progress of the construction project of Sala Ta On Dam in the district. Ek Phnom.
According to the report from the director of the department and the project implementation team, the construction of the Sala Ta On Dam project under the financing of the Republic of Korea, which has so far achieved about 20 percent, has been under construction work to divert water across the Sangker River. Excavation of the four canals (Prek Khpor, Preap, Samrong in Prek Daun Teav and Prek Snor) and preparation of concrete bottoms and legs.
On that occasion, Minister Lim Kean Hor thanked for the hard work of the project implementation team and highly appreciated the progress made so far.
The Minister instructed the project implementation team to implement the work according to the set technical standards to meet the objectives of the project: First: to increase the irrigation capacity of tens of thousands of hectares in the lower part, second: to Maintain water stability to serve the use of clean water for Battambang and third: to improve the aesthetics.
In addition to ordering his officials to inspect the water situation in all provinces, Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology Lim Kean Hor also visited the water situation in the provinces to prepare for the intervention of people facing Lack of drinking water.
