Remarks by Senior Minister Kun Kim Presiding Over the Meeting to Review the Results of 2018 and the Directions of the Veterans Association Committees of Battambang, Pursat, Pailin and Banteay Meanchey Provinces The Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport and the Director of the Provincial Department of Rural Development are the Vice Chairmen of the four Provincial Veterans Association Committees.
The ceremony was held at the 5th Military Command in Battambang City, Battambang Province to monitor the activities of the 5th Military Region and the implementation of the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and President of the Cambodian Veterans Association. .
According to the report, the work done in the past includes the movement to attend the funeral, the payment of death allowances for 440 bodies and social security allowance for 336 families, visited and donated a total of 1 veteran. , 072,310,500 Riels.
So far, 176 houses have been donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit to poor veterans who are members of associations in the provinces in the 5th Military Zone, including 4 in Pursat, 104 in Battambang. One in Pailin and 67 in Banteay Meanchey, while another 77 are under construction in 2019.
Speaking on the occasion, Senior Minister Kun Kim praised the efforts and achievements of the association at all levels over the past year, which have contributed significantly to solving the difficulties and reducing poverty of veterans. . In addition, Senior Minister Kun Kim instructed the leaders of the provincial association to inspect and find the veterans who are in dire need in order to give priority to providing them with housing first.
At the request of the Provincial Veterans Association, Mr. Kun Kim decided to build a house donated by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to 49 veterans, including 11 in Pursat and 38 in Pailin. Mr. Him Chhem Dissemination Meeting on the Outcome of the 41st Central Committee Meeting of the 5th Mandate of the Cambodian People's Party
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Him Chhem, Member of the Central Committee of the Cambodian People's Party and Chairman of the Party Committee of the Ministry of Cult and Religion, this morning, February 24, 2019, chaired a meeting to disseminate the contents of the results of the Central Committee Meeting. 41st, 5th mandate of the Cambodian People's Party.
The content that Mr. Him Chhem disseminated to the members included the meeting expressing the deepest respect and gratitude to the compatriots everywhere and in all walks of life in the society that gives justice and trust to the Cambodian People's Party by voting. Extremely supportive of the Cambodian People's Party to lead the country for the sixth term.
Proud of the achievements of the economic sector, which actually achieved a high growth rate of 7.3%, supported by strong growth of industry and services, despite the low growth of the agricultural sector. Promote the successful implementation of the fourth phase of the Royal Government's Rectangular Political Program and Strategy, with the fourth strategic goal of building a foundation to achieve the vision of Cambodia as a high-income country by 2050.
In addition, the Conference called on all compatriots everywhere, all political parties, civil society organizations and other circles in society to unite as one national force under the umbrella of the Constitution and the cool shadow of the King. It is our highest sanctuary to continue to build and defend our homeland for the sake of independence, unity, peace, freedom, democracy and social development.
Please be informed that the 41st Central Committee Meeting of the 5th Mandate of the Cambodian People's Party was held from 18 to 20 December 2018 under the chairmanship of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, President of the Party, Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Honorary Chairman of the Party and The Standing Committee of the Central Committee has a total of 3,164 members.
The meeting expressed the deepest respect and gratitude to His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni, King of the Kingdom of Cambodia, and Her Majesty Queen Norodom Monineath Sihanouk, Queen Mother of Cambodia. Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong: Samdech Techo Hun Sen sacrifices everything to alleviate the suffering of people with disabilities throughout the country
(Phnom Penh): Speaking in front of more than 100 students with disabilities in Kampong Cham province, Deputy Prime Minister Hor Namhong said that Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross All kinds of personal resources, millions of dollars to help alleviate the suffering of Cambodians with disabilities throughout Cambodia.
The Deputy Prime Minister's remarks were made on February 24, 2019, on the occasion that the Deputy Prime Minister and Mrs. accompanied by Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information and Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Kampong Cham Province, brought the Hor Namhong Foundation. Borey Hor provides to a special education high school in Kampong Cham province to support 165 children with disabilities and deafness with 480 million riels (120,000 US dollars) per year.
