(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thea Kuy, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, considered and recognized the need to take care of people's health effectively, especially maternal and child health.
Mr. Thea Kuy said that the Royal Government of Cambodia, especially the Ministry of Health, has given priority to the welfare of infants because the infant mortality rate in Cambodia is still high.
He said that the success of the team can be measured depends on the team of doctors in the field of maternal and child health and the response of the health system to this need.
Mr. Thea Kruy made this remark while presiding over the opening ceremony of the second updated conference of the Cambodian Pediatric Association.
Prof. Im Sithikar, President of the Cambodian Pediatric Association, said that the workshop was organized to ensure that participants have a better understanding of the management and treatment of respiratory diseases in newborns, especially premature infants with respiratory problems. This usually occurs in the first few hours after the baby is born and is also the cause of infant death.
She stated that the infant mortality rate in Cambodia due to respiratory diseases in newborns is 18 per 1,000 births, which is a high rate compared to neighboring countries. Minister Vong Soth tells people not to believe in the incitement of some unscrupulous people and must believe in the Royal Government of Cambodia
