(Phnom Penh): The relationship between workers and employers occurs through a contract called an employment contract, which can be made orally or in writing as required by law.
Employment contracts are defined and defined precisely through the Labor Law, which came into force in 1997 and the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia in 2007, covering all employment relations that occur in the Kingdom of Cambodia, including Textile (garment and footwear) as well.
However, the employment contract stipulated in the Labor Law and the above-mentioned Civil Code shall not apply within the framework of the work of public servants and the Armed Forces, as the employment relations of public officials are subject to the Civil Servants' Statute. And the armed forces must be subject to their own special statutes.
At the same time, free professional relations are not subject to the rules of the labor law, such as the legal profession, which is subject to the Law on the Statute of Lawyers, and the medical and engineering professions also have separate statutes.
For this week, Fresh News' Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Bar Association for International Cooperation, brings to light the topic of employment contracts set out in the 1997 Labor Law and the 2007 Civil Code. As follows:
According to Article 65 of the Labor Law 1997, Article 65 states: "An employment contract is a contract that establishes an employment relationship between a worker and an employer. "This contract is subject to arbitrary rules and may take the form agreed upon by both parties."
Article 664 of the Civil Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia defines an employment contract as: That labor "" The party that promised to work is called the worker and the other party is called the employer.
According to the 1997 Labor Law, employment contracts are divided into two types: fixed-term employment contracts and indefinite-term employment contracts, the two types of which are clearly distinguished as follows:
1: Limited employment contract
2: Employment contract for an indefinite period
It is a contract made between a worker and an employer, with both parties not stating a specific date or time of termination in the contract, and this contract can be made orally or in writing. In the event that the employment contract has a silent term, it shall be considered as an indefinite indefinite employment contract.
In conclusion, understanding the employment contract is important so that the parties to the employment contract can avoid violating the rights or conditions in the employment contract and enable the parties to the employment contract to choose any type of employment contract for the benefit of Body. Construction of a school worth $ 60,000 in Soeur commune, Banteay Meanchey province, General Ke Kim Yan reminded Samdech Techo "do not trade national sovereignty for absolute aid"
