According to a press release obtained by Fresh News on the morning of February 24, 2019, prior to the meeting of the Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Mr. Salem Sai Kum Masit met twice. The two sides exchanged views on recent political developments in their respective countries.
In the field of security, the two sides agreed to continue to share and exchange information related to the prevention of human trafficking and to enhance cooperation between the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and the Lao People's Army through exchanges of visits at all levels.
The meeting welcomed the preliminary arrangements for cross-border transport by bus between Cambodia and Laos, especially between Phnom Penh-Pakse and Siem Reap-Pakse. The two sides also agreed to strengthen civil aviation cooperation in the fields of safety, security, aviation development and exchange of training, and explore the possibility of further increasing direct flights between the two countries.
The meeting also agreed to increase cooperation in other areas, including education, information, agriculture, tourism, culture, public health, post and telecommunications, law and judicial cooperation and consular cooperation.
In addition to bilateral cooperation, the two sides expressed their commitment to continue cooperating in sub-regional and regional mechanisms towards integration and sustainable and comprehensive economic connectivity.
At the end of the meeting, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon and Mr. Salem Sai Kummasit signed the Minutes of the 13th Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation and agreed to hold the Second Joint Commission for Bilateral Cooperation. 14th in Cambodia in 2021.
During his visit to Laos, Deputy Prime Minister Prak Sokhon also paid a courtesy call on Lao President Bun Nhang Vorachit and Prime Minister Thongloun Sisoulith.
