Russian media: Kim Jong Un's bullet train leaves Pyongyang for Hanoi for next week's summit with Trump
(Pyongyang): North Korean leader Kim Jong Un has begun his train journey from the capital, Pyongyang, which will pass through China to Hanoi, Vietnam, where he is to hold a summit. For the second time with US President Donald Trump. This is according to a source from a North Korean diplomat quoted by the Russian newspaper TASS on Saturday night, February 23, 2019.
At 5:00 pm (Pyongyang time), Kim Jong Un left Pyongyang for Hanoi via a low-light train and will travel in a train, a North Korean diplomatic source revealed. This line runs through China to Vietnam. The total distance between Pyongyang and Hanoi is more than 4,500 kilometers, so Kim's trip is expected to take more than 48 hours without stopping in China.
