Minister of Labor announces legal action against "Samsung Korean Language Training Center" after defrauding Cambodians to seek employment in Korea without exams
(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Labor and Vocational Training, Mr. Ith Sam Heng, announced the legal action against the "Samsung Korean Language Training Center" which deceived Cambodians by guaranteeing jobs in South Korea without Exam fee in exchange for about $ 2,500.
The Minister's announcement came after the fraudulent activities of the "Samsung Korean Language Training Center" were leaked on February 22, 2019, when many Cambodians went to withdraw money from the center because they did not Went to work in Korea as promised by the center.
It should be noted that on February 22, many Cambodians from the provinces went to sit at the "Samsung Korean Language Training Center" in Sangkat Kakap, Khan Por Sen Chey, waiting to withdraw their money. After the center could not find jobs for them in South Korea as promised.
A Cambodian who was waiting to withdraw his money told Fresh News that he had paid the center about $ 2,500 to get a job in South Korea. The Cambodian people who cheated the center's promise also stated that after paying the center, they were guaranteed to find a job for a short period of time.
Victims of money laundering by the center said that after not going to work in South Korea as promised, many victims returned to withdraw money. But this withdrawal is not as easy as when they take the money to pay.
According to the description of the victim from Kampong Cham province, who asked not to be named, she said that for about $ 2,500, she had to come to Phnom Penh many times and sometimes had to cry for the management of the center. Also, they agreed to return some money. The last money, about $ 800, the center just opened for the victim on February 22.
The victims, who were waiting for the money to be returned from the center, made the same claim and expressed outrage at the center's management. They said that because they wanted to get a high-paying job in South Korea, they borrowed money from financial institutions to pay the center.
But waiting from month to month without going to work makes them even more difficult because they are unemployed and have to earn money to pay interest.
According to the agreement between the Royal Government of Cambodia and the Government of Korea, the sending of workers to work in South Korea does not allow private companies to send, only the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training to organize the examination and send workers.
According to the victims of the scam, the "Samsung Korean Language Training Center" secretly sent workers to work in Korea under various guises, with some workers able to go to work for six months and others to return for three months. Come back to the country.
The center's management told Fresh News, acknowledging that they had promised to find jobs for Cambodians working in South Korea. But there are some problems so they can not find a job and also try to pay back. Pursat Governor Urges All Religious Persons in the Province to Cultivate New Culture and Nationalism for the Next Generation
