(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Sokun alias Jem Sok, a commentator on Cambodia's social and political issues, criticized the opposition, especially the former CNRP leaders, over the issue of migrant workers.
Mr. Sok Sokun's criticism was made in response to the remarks made by former CNRP Vice President Mu Sochua. Ms. Mu Sochua said that the Royal Government of Cambodia's inability to provide employment for the people has led to more Cambodians being forced to migrate to work in neighboring countries as well as other countries.
In a video commented live on Facebook on the night of February 22, 2019, Mr. Sok Sokun said that the issue of migration is not only Cambodia, Thailand, Vietnam and the Philippines are sending countries. Work abroad. Even Mexico has tens of millions of people seeking employment in the United States.
The rising social commentator says opposition parties in Thailand and the Philippines, for example, have never linked politics to workers. Do not associate politics with workers, because in these two countries, if workers interfere in politics, the government will cancel their passports and they will not be able to find work abroad.
Regarding this labor issue, Mr. Sokun criticized the former leaders of the National Rescue Party that they always talk about sympathy for migrant workers, but instead go to raise money for those workers, especially in South Korea to come to work Its politics.
The commentator said that if the former CNRP leaders really sympathized with the workers, they would not have gone to raise money for the workers. Mr. Sok Sokun also reminded all Cambodian workers to think long and hard, not to believe the fraud of politicians.
Mr. Sokun urged overseas workers to work hard to save money and send it to their families in the district to build a house or save money to start a business when they return to the country.
