Cambodian Minister of Commerce participates in the opening ceremony of the 4th ASEAN-India Exhibition and Summit on "ASEAN-India Future Cooperation"
(New Delhi - India): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, led a Cambodian delegation to the 4th ASEAN-India Expo and Summit from 21-23 February 2019 in New Delhi, India.
In his opening remarks, the Minister expressed his deep pleasure, admiration and gratitude to the Government of the Republic of India for inviting him and the Cambodian delegation to this special event, which was attended by Key communities, including successful businessmen, entrepreneurs in various fields and senior officials from ASEAN and India.
In this regard, in order to further boost trade and investment between ASEAN and India towards achieving a trade volume of 200 billion US dollars by 2022, which is the goal set, he stressed the completion of negotiations on the agreement. The Regional Comprehensive Economic Partnership (RCEP) is very important for ASEAN and India, and the talks are expected to be completed this year as promised by the leadership.
In addition, the Minister also informed about the progress of Cambodia that with peace and political stability, Cambodia's economic growth has achieved an annual growth rate of about 7% in the last decade, which makes Cambodia an economic country. One of the fastest growing in the world.
According to a 2016 World Bank report, Cambodia is classified as a low-middle-income country, and according to the Royal Government's plan, Cambodia will become a high-middle-income country by 2030 and A high-income country by 2050.
Cambodia has also included international trade and investment in the fourth rectangular strategy of the sixth mandate of the Royal Government of Cambodia. Integration and liberalization remain key goals of Cambodia, and the Ministry of Commerce has been playing a key role in achieving this vision.
In an effort to facilitate trade, the ministry has created online business applications and registrations. The Ministry has also abolished export control fees (EMF) and issued regulations allowing exports to the EU, Norway, Switzerland and Turkey without CO, all reflecting Cambodia's commitment to the TFA's implementation of TFA. The world.
To facilitate trade, Cambodia has recently revised border inspection and release procedures to reduce delays and export-import costs. The Royal Government of Cambodia has also launched a plan to reduce the price of water and electricity for industrial use and low-cost transportation.
Cambodia also implements existing investment laws that guarantee a wide range of incentives for investors. All of these regulations and the latest reforms benefit foreign investors who consider Cambodia as their investment destination. Executive Director of Disability Cambodia: Disability sector in Cambodia begins to expand to the regional level
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Ngin Sau Rath, Executive Director of the Cambodian Organization of Persons with Disabilities, said that the ASEAN Master Plan for the Disability Sector 2025 is the main road map to promote and integrate the rights of persons with disabilities into the ASEAN region. He said that through this plan, the disability sector will be given more attention and covered more than ever before.
Mr. Ngin Sau Rath, Executive Director of the Cambodian Organization of Persons with Disabilities, said at a press conference on the implementation of the April 2025 April ASEAN Plan held at the headquarters of the Cambodian Organization of Persons with Disabilities on the morning of February 22, 2019.
The Executive Director of the Cambodian Organization of Persons with Disabilities added that this is another level of progress for the disability sector, as the disability sector is now not only being taken care of nationally, but is now being expanded to a regional level. .
On that occasion, Mr. Tep Un, Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Disability Action Council, said that we have now done many activities to help people with disabilities to have better access. He added that in addition, people with disabilities receive more attention in the social, educational and health sectors and many other important sectors.
The Deputy Secretary General of the General Secretariat of the Council for the Action of Persons with Disabilities said that today our disability is progressing day by day under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia. A good role model for people without general disabilities.
It should be noted that in recent years, the disability sector in Cambodia has received more and more attention from stakeholders, and as a result, it is generally recognized that the situation of people with disabilities has continuously improved, including the economic situation. Social work, education, health and other participation, and in 2018 alone, nearly 6,000 people with disabilities were recruited to work in both public and private institutions.
