(Phnom Penh): When it comes to international relations, there is no such thing as true friendship, only personal interests. If we recall the United States and Vietnam about 50 years ago, during the 1960s and 1970s, the two countries used all means to kill each other.
Ten years after independence, in 1955, Vietnam erupted in war and divided the country into two countries, South Vietnam and North Vietnam. This ethnic war ended in 1975. A Vietnamese government report released in 1995 showed that more than 2 million Vietnamese civilians and soldiers had died during the war.
Despite painful scars from the past, the US government, under the leadership of Barack Obama, has begun to improve US-Vietnam relations, despite the fact that Vietnam is a non-democratic communist country. . Through these gestures, they are able to evaluate the forgetfulness of the past and rebuild good relations between the United States and Vietnam for their own benefit.
The participation of Vietnamese people abroad and in the country is in their national interest. In fact, according to the Vietnam News Agency on February 18, 2019, Vietnam has exported mangoes to the US market and launched the first direct flight between Vietnam and the United States.
The question is: What is this? Is this in Vietnam's interest? What about Vietnamese people living in the United States and living in countries that do not like the leadership of the Vietnamese leader, why do not they protest against foreigners putting economic pressure on their country or calling for severing ties with their country? That is because they understand the national conscience and the people as a whole.
If we look at the former opposition party in Cambodia, who took refuge abroad with Sam Rainsy as the instigator, why always call for foreigners to put pressure on the people and the country?
Therefore, in order to achieve its poisonous ambitions, the group of prisoners Sam Rainsy seeks all means to hinder the development of the nation, such as trying to get foreigners to collect taxes from the Cambodian people to cut off ties with Cambodia.
On behalf of the people, I hope that the Cambodian people, both inside and outside the country, will unite to support the nation, support the policies of the Royal Government, support the cooperation of the nation and the countries in the world, and consider national independence and national sovereignty firmly in order to move forward. Face.
