In the future, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology has assigned and assigned tasks to the leadership as Secretary of State, Undersecretary of State, responsible for the provinces under the direct supervision of the Minister.
In the past, the leaders of the Ministry in charge of the arrow, together with the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, held a meeting to educate the local authorities on water conservation measures, saving and avoiding the misuse of water. Goals and non-permits for the second dry season rice cultivation since October 2018.
As a practical measure to solve the water for the daily use of the people, the Ministry has used all means and equipment, the Ministry has recently provided 20 cranes to the 20 provincial departments of water resources and meteorology to facilitate the intervention.
The work that has been intervened is as follows:
* Second: Banteay Meanchey Province * Dredged a canal to bring water from Stung Sreng Reservoir into Trapeang Thmor Basin as soon as possible to support the daily use of the people as well as the biodiversity in Trapeang Thmor Reservoir. Due to the high demand for water for irrigating wet season rice as well as dry season rice, the water in Trapeang Thmor basin almost dried up due to the previous rainy season, Ang Trapeang Thmor received less rainfall.
* Third: Oddar Meanchey Province
* Considering the shortage of water for daily use in Oddar Meanchey Provincial Prison in Samrong Sangkat, Samrong City as a solution for water use there, the Ministry has assigned the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology to transport 10 cubic meters of water in One day using a car equipped with a water tank of the Ministry provided in the past. This is a water solution to face and in the dry season.
* 6: Preah Vihear Province * Due to the lack of water for daily use in Preah Vihear Provincial Prison in Bal Hal Sangkat, Preah Vihear City, Mr. Lim Kean Hor decided to provide one large water well and put it into daily use in Prison.
7th: Pailin Province * Distribute water to people in need of water for daily use in Sala Krao commune and Stung Trang commune, Sala Krao district, using the vehicles equipped with water tanks of the Ministry provided in the past. .
* 8th: Koh Kong Province * Delivering water to people who lack water for daily use in Sangkat Dang Tong, Khemarak Phoumin City, using a vehicle equipped with a water tank provided by the Ministry in the past. Water transport is currently suspended as the water supply network is reconnected.
At the same time, the Ministry team in cooperation with the Department of Water Resources and authorities in other provinces are also intervening to bring water to the people.
WASHINGTON: The United States will keep 200 peacekeepers in Syria for an undisclosed time after the withdrawal of thousands of troops from the Middle East country. According to the original plan. This is according to the White House quoted by Reuters on Friday morning, February 22, 2019.
In December 2018, Donald Trump ordered the Pentagon to withdraw more than 2,000 US troops from Syria, claiming that ISIS had been defeated. But US allies, especially France, have strongly criticized the decision and called on Trump to change his policy to ensure the protection of Kurdish fighters fighting ISIS and under threat from Turkey.
The White House announcement came after Donald Trump had a telephone conversation with Turkish President Recep Tayyip Erdogan, in which the two leaders also agreed to continue cooperating on the establishment of the region. A security in Syria. But at the same time, the White House did not specify when the 200 US troops will be stationed in Syria or where they will be based.
Cambodian Customs Officer Requests Representatives of Ministries and Professional Institutions to Prepare for the Second Phase of the One-Stop-Shop System by the End of March
(Phnom Penh): Dr. Kun Nhem, Royal Government Delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia, as the Permanent Vice Chairman of the National Standing Project Steering Committee and Chairman of the National Standing Project Implementation Team on the afternoon of the 21st. In February 2019, the second meeting of the National Standards Project Implementation Team was held at Sunway Hotel.
The main purpose of this meeting is to monitor the progress of the development of the second phase of the single system and to continue to discuss and provide additional input on work related to the second phase of the system. At the same time, the meeting also reviewed the presentation of the functions of the second phase of the national single stand system, which VCC has already developed in line with international best practices.
Dr. Kun Nhem praised the achievements of the past and asked the representatives of all ministries and institutions to be ready and prepared to test the use of the national single-phase system, the second phase, which will begin at the end. In March 2019, it is requested that the working group review the legal aspects to support the implementation of the second phase of the One-Stop-Shop project.
Taking this opportunity, he also mentioned the guidance of the Deputy Prime Minister, Minister of Economy and Finance in proposing to accelerate the development of the national stand system to be completed as soon as possible to update the situation. Of recent reforms related to border trade facilitation.
He also thanked the representatives of relevant ministries and institutions for their cooperation and positive support in the past and advised all members of the National Standards Project implementation team to continue their active participation. For the one-nation stand-alone project, the second phase can be achieved in the planned time to further facilitate trade.
