Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that recently, in order to facilitate the investment of investors and traders, Samdech has issued a new sub-decree to end the roles and responsibilities of the General Department of CamControl at all international border crossings and assign duties. The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia is the only institution responsible for inspecting export-import goods at international gates.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen wrote on Facebook, "I would like to support and encourage more investors to invest in Cambodia. Recently, the Royal Government has restructured the authorities to control the export-import goods to facilitate trade and strengthen competition for investors and traders to benefit more, as follows:
Article 1: The role and duties of the General Department of Cambodia to inspect the export-import of goods, to inspect the export and import of goods and to crack down on fraud (Camcontrol) of the Ministry of Commerce from the international gate, international border gate, border gate Bilateral border gates, seaports, special economic zones, temporary customs warehousing facilities and other export-import control points throughout the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Article 2: The General Department of Customs and Excise of Cambodia of the Ministry of Economy and Finance is the only body competent to inspect the export-import of goods at international gates, international border gates, bilateral border gates, border areas and Ports, seaports, special economic zones, temporary customs warehouses and other import and export checkpoints. I wish you all happiness and good luck.
Please be informed that Samdech Techo Hun Sen on February 20, 2019 welcomed all investors, both domestic and foreign, to come and invest in Cambodia under the roof of peace, democracy, liberalism, multi-party without discrimination. .
The Prime Minister encouraged all foreign investors to have the right to invest in their own shares (100%) without the need for local partners or local shareholders to participate.
