(Phnom Penh): A fire at Khemarak University forced four Chinese women to jump from the third floor of a building, causing serious and minor injuries. This incident happened at 1:15 AM on February 22, 2019 along Street 1986, point 72, in Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh.
According to eyewitnesses, before the incident, he was asleep when he heard an explosion outside the house, he ran out to see the flames. The fire at Khemarak University is gone.
When he saw this, he shouted for the people living nearby to help put out the fire with fire hoses, and some even called the local police to cooperate with the fire brigade to intervene. Immediately.
While fire trucks were fighting, many residents shouted for help in front of the building as four Chinese women were trapped on the third floor.
Two Chinese women were forced to jump from the third floor of the building due to heavy smoke and sound, and two others were standing on the window sill. But the authorities went up to help suddenly caused the fall seriously injured both.
It should also be noted that the fire was intervened by several fire trucks to prevent the fire from spreading to other places. Four Chinese women were seriously injured and taken to hospital by ambulance, while some equipment on the ground floor of Khemarak University was burnt to the ground. Nothing.
As for the cause of the fire, the authorities confirmed that it was due to electric shock.
