Director General of Taxation: Tax reform affects some individuals but benefits a lot for the nation (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): Mr. Kong Vibol, the Royal Government delegate in charge of the Director General of the General Department of Taxation, confirmed that he is not afraid of No tax reform because he followed the strategy of the Royal Government to implement, although this reform affects the interests of some individuals, but the benefits for the nation greatly.
Mr. Kong Vibol made this remark while attending a Vipassana seminar on the progress of the information technology system of the General Department of Taxation and preparing a strategic information technology plan of the General Department of Taxation for 2019-2023 at the hotel. Angkor Palace Resort and Spa on February 21, 2019.
"I believe in myself that the government requires us to reform, and if we do, I do not believe that the government is to blame," he said. Being a leader in the Director General of the General Department of Taxation must always be courageous, no matter how much I touch or disagree, I do not have to be afraid of what we are doing as long as we think that this is Accuracy and in line with the strategy of the Royal Government.
He said that the General Department of Taxation must be reformed, and this reform is to set up a good system to enable the General Department of Taxation to serve taxpayers. He said that like today, a good registration means that the General Department has done a good service by serving them to pay taxes anywhere in the bank, such as ACLEDA Canadia and other banks.
He added that currently more than 90 percent of taxpayer data is in the system, and it is a way for all new registrants to follow the path of the new reform when registration is undocumented. At the time of registration, it is maintained by the management system of the General Department of Taxation. Russey Keo District Women's Association Sub-Branch Holds a Meeting with Members to Celebrate the 108th Anniversary of International Women's Day March 8, 2019
