The Beresheet spacecraft weighs just 600 kilograms and is considered one of the smallest spacecraft. It is 1.5 meters high and 2 meters in diameter and can hold 75% of its total fuel. The spacecraft will travel 6.5 million kilometers in an elliptical orbit around the Earth until it orbits the moon at 36,000 kilometers per hour, or 10 kilometers per hour. Seconds.
If the mission is 100% successful, Israel will be the fourth country to be able to send a spacecraft to land on the moon after the former Soviet Union, the United States and China. The IAI team expressed its pride and high hopes for what it will achieve in the future, raising Israel's profile on the international stage.
