Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth inspects the progress of the implementation of the Public Financial Management Reform Program
Based on the results of monitoring the progress of the implementation of the action plan for 2018, it is shown that the implementation of the action plan for the public financial management reform program in 2018 achieved 90% compared to the implementation of the total action plan. Achievements achieved in each section of the Joint Action Plan Framework Phase 3 include:
* Section 4 "Preparation for the next step" has made significant progress, including: a detailed action plan to support the strategy of budget reform 2018-2025 has been prepared, guidelines on budgeting, achievements have been The organization and internal audit functions of 13 ministries and institutions were inspected.
* Section 5 "Supporting Successful and Sustainable Reform Programs" The Institute of Economics and Finance has developed a strategic plan for capacity building and development within the framework of the Public Financial Management Reform Program and technical skills training on management. Public finance to 850 government officials from ministries and institutions.
In addition, in order to orient and support the implementation of a successful and sustainable public financial management reform program, the Ministry of Economy and Finance will complete the preparation of key strategic documents in the first quarter of 2019, including strategies for Sub-national budget system reform 2019-2025, public procurement system reform strategy 2019-2025 and revenue collection strategy 2019-2023.
Overall, based on the results of monitoring the progress of the Public Financial Management Reform Program 2018, the Public Financial Management Reform Commission evaluated and concluded as follows:
* Financial accountability system has been built through the implementation of information technology systems for public financial management, Phase 1 and 2 with high caution,
Strengthening and expanding the implementation of program budgets as a basis for preparing and determining changes to the Cambodian budget system,
* Cambodia's Budget Reform Strategy is a key component for achieving accountability, the ultimate goal of the Public Financial Management Reform Program, and
