Eng Depot Development Co., Ltd. prepares drainage system to distribute to people for dry rice in Kampong Os commune, Ponhea Leu district
(Kandal): Mr. Ly Samet, General Director of Eng Depot Development Company, is preparing to distribute the drainage system to the people for the irrigation of the second phase of dry rice in Kampong Os commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province.
On the morning of February 21, 2019, the General Director of Eng Depot Development Company visited nearly 300 families in Kampong Os commune, Ponhea Leu district, Kandal province to meet and provide water to people who are short of water this dry season. Many hectares.
Mr. Ly Samet said that because Cambodia is peaceful under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, investors have confidence in investing in all sectors. Therefore, the agricultural investment company Eng Depot Development has the capacity to store water for thousands of hectares of dryland rice throughout the project and distribute it to the people around the project for many more hectares.
Many families who are facing water shortage problems in their rice fields have expressed their happiness to the company that has water ready to help them who are facing water shortage problems. Worry again.
At the same time, Mr. Ly Samet inspected roads and bridges (Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Prek Dangkom Bridge and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen Prek Tamey Bridge), canals and reservoirs to take measures to repair damaged roads. Due to the rising water during the rainy season and the arrangement of the drainage system to distribute to the people for irrigation in the second phase of dry season rice.
Ministry of Agriculture issues circular on measures to reduce the impact of animals due to drought and prevention of animal diseases
