Mr. Sok Sokun said that the banned politicians' search for a way back to politics came after they lost faith in the struggle of Sam Rainsy, who announced his release from Cambodia in 2019.
Sok Sokun, who has a network of supporters of the former CNRP in the United States, claimed that the 115 banned politicians wanted to find a mechanism to apply for political rights in three groups. The first group wants to enter independently, not the other, the second group wants to join the group and the third group leaves Sam Rainsy to return to politics in time.
Mr. Sokun suggested that the banned politicians rush to re-apply for political rights because Mr. Rainsy would not return.
It should be noted that 118 former CNRP leaders and members have been banned from engaging in politics. But now there are only 115 people left, as two of those banned have re-applied for politics: Kong Koam and Kong Bora. Separately, one of the banned people who died was Cheam Channy.
With Mr. Sok Sokun revealing that a group of politicians have been banned from engaging in politics to find their way back into politics, on February 21, 2019, the Ministry of Interior also issued procedural instructions to apply for this right to engage in politics. Back, too.
The procedure for re-applying for political rights includes:
A. A person who has been banned from political activity by a court must re-apply for rehabilitation to the Ministry of Interior at all working hours.
B. The application must include the identity of the person requesting the court decision prohibiting political activity, as well as the fingerprints of the applicant.
C. The application must be made separately by the person who has been banned by the court from engaging in political activity.
D. After reviewing the application of the individual who submitted the application, the Ministry of Interior will propose to the Prime Minister to request the King to waive the ban on political activities in accordance with the provisions of the new Article 45 (a) Law on Political Parties.
E. They will be able to resume political activities in accordance with the laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia after the Royal Decree on Rehabilitation.
