According to the instruction of the Ministry of Interior, according to the new Article 45 (one) of the Law on Political Parties, individuals who have been banned from political activity by the court will be able to regain their full political rights in the following cases:
1: Full legal restoration of political rights after the expiration of the prohibition period determined by the judgment of the Supreme Court
2. The restoration of full political rights by the rehabilitation of the King at the request of the Prime Minister at the request of the Minister of Interior.
The Ministry of Interior added that in order to ensure the implementation of the second point above, the Ministry of Interior would like to introduce the following procedures and procedures for political rehabilitation:
* A. A person who has been banned from political activity by a court must re-apply for rehabilitation to the Ministry of Interior at all working hours.
* B. The application must include the identity of the person requesting the court decision prohibiting political activity, as well as the fingerprints of the applicant.
* C. The application must be made separately by the person who has been banned by the court from engaging in political activity.
* D. After reviewing the application of the individual who submitted the application, the Ministry of Interior will propose to the Prime Minister to request the King to waive the ban on political activities in accordance with the provisions of the new Article 45 (a) Law on Political Parties.
* E. They will be able to resume political activities in accordance with the laws of the Kingdom of Cambodia after the Royal Decree on Rehabilitation.
It should be noted that the proposed Law on the Amendment of Article 45 (Duplicate) of the Law on Political Parties, which paved the way for banned politicians to resume their political activities, was approved by His Majesty King Norodom Sihamoni. The King of Cambodia issued the Royal Kram, which was officially promulgated on January 2, 2019.
Since the law came into force, two former leaders of the former Cambodia National Rescue Party (CNRP) who have been banned from politics have applied to the Ministry of Interior for political rehabilitation, including Kong Koam and his son Kong Bora. The two also submitted separate applications.
