(Phnom Penh): Mr. Huy Vannak, President of the Federation of Cambodian Journalists (UCJC) and Secretary of State of the Ministry of Interior, on February 21, 2019, led a delegation of leaders and members to review the progress of Construction of the headquarters of the Union of Cambodian Journalists, located in Chroy Changva, Phnom Penh.
The headquarters of the Union of Cambodian Journalists will be built on an area of more than 2,000 square meters, 20 meters wide, 25 meters long, 4 stories high, and about 65% of the construction work is scheduled to be completed in June 2019.
Mr. Huy Vannak revealed that when the headquarters building is completed, it is here not only for the media, but we will jointly create this new achievement from here to contribute to the society in accordance with the goals and Its vision is to strengthen professional capacity and professional ethics, that is, "Journalists shine, a prosperous nation."
Mr. Huy Vannak emphasized that starting from this building, we will try to contribute to building good human resources from here. The new building will be a library, an exhibition venue, a workshop, a meeting place for national and international journalists, and in particular a training program to strengthen the journalism profession in line with advances in technology, society and economy.
