Agriculture Minister Introduces Measures to Prevent Wildfires, Floods and Mangrove Forests and Fish Rescue Interventions in the 2019 Dry Season
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, on February 21, 2019, issued instructions on measures to prevent wildfires, floods and mangrove forests, and fish rescue interventions in the 2019 dry season.
In order to avoid possible problems when Cambodia suffers from Nino phenomenon, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries would like to advise the Fisheries Administration and the Department of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries to take care of Measures to prevent wildfires and mangrove fires and to intervene to rescue fish at the following conservation areas immediately:
1. Prevent and prevent deforestation, burning of flooded forests to develop agricultural crops, nomadic farming and resettlement by illegally taking land.
2: Prevent burning forest to catch animals.
3: Prepare a fish sanctuary by tying it in a deep canyon or in many places in the fishery conservation area.
4: Prepare a pump to pump water into the atmosphere to fall on the board to increase oxygen in the water for fish to breathe in the fishery.
5: Must strictly protect the activities of people fishing in the fishery conservation area.
