Kratie Provincial Prosecutor Forces to Close Many Gold Mining Pits in Sambo District
(Kratie): A joint force led by Mr. Sok Kiriroth, Director of Kratie Provincial Department of Mines and Energy, under the coordination of Mr. Chea Sopheak, Deputy Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, on February 21, 2019, led a force to close the gold mine site. Many pits at Tron point, Kbal Damrey commune, Sambo district, Kratie province.
Mr. Sok Kiriroth said that the joint forces that closed the location of the gold mine, including: Prosecution, the Department of Mines and Energy, the police and the military closed down many gold mines with machinery. As of this afternoon, the team has removed eight pits and called two pit owners to sign a contract to stop the illegal mining of gold.
The other pit owners have not yet come to make a contract, but the department will call all of them to make a contract, and the team will continue to remove all the pits until tomorrow to clear all the pits.
He added that in the case of the demolition of the gold mine, the department has already terminated it several times by signing a contract with the owner of the mine, but the group is still stealing gold mining activities, and this time he led the force. Remove the excavator with an excavator and continue digging until the pit is empty.
It should be noted that the people who mined gold at Tron point, Kbal Damrey commune, Sambo district, had collapsed and died in the past, but they did not relent because they had been in this business since the beginning.
The Ministry of Agriculture has taken seven urgent measures to control and prevent the spread of African swine fever (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): The Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, Mr. Veng Sakhon, issued a circular on February 21, 2019. Urgent measures to control and prevent the spread of African swine fever
It is a deadly infectious disease that is extremely difficult to eradicate and causes a high rate of morbidity and mortality. By. In the past, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries has also requested the relevant ministries to cooperate in preventing the spread of this disease into Cambodia.
Therefore, in order to prevent and control the spread more effectively, especially during the recent outbreak in Vietnam, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries would like to recommend the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production, Department of Agriculture and Forestry. And Fisheries and Capital-Provincial Production and Veterinary Offices, especially the provinces bordering Vietnam, must implement the following seven specific measures:
2. To prevent the import of live pigs and all kinds of illegal pig products in cooperation with sub-national authorities at all levels, especially the border entry and exit authorities.
3. All traffic of pigs and pork products must have a sanitary certificate from the exporting country and must be under the supervision of animal health and meat hygiene by a veterinarian by concluding the beginning and end correctly. .
4: Increase the monitoring and monitoring of the health status of pigs in breeding grounds and farms on a regular basis, as well as collecting samples and sending them to the laboratory of the General Department of Animal Health and Animal Production for virus analysis to implement veterinary rules in a timely manner. .
5. Cooperate well with the Vietnamese side in exchanging information related to the disease in a timely and effective manner.
6: Educate people, village animal health agencies, pig farmers at all levels from the preparation of the chest, care, water supply, health monitoring and proper implementation of biosafety according to the technique.
7. Continue to educate the people and pig farmers to be aware of the impact and serious damage if economic pig production is caused by the African plague. Vietnamese government tries to provide E-Visa to 35 countries
