(Kampong Cham): Although some cultural treasures have been lost, Phnom Pros Phnom Srey is still two cultural tourism destinations at the same time, leaving many more cultural and historical properties for national and international tourists to visit and Enjoy the natural beauty around the two mountains accompanied by fresh air under the shade of trees.
Phnom Pros Phnom Srey Cultural Tourism Resort is located in Trapeang Char Village, Krala Commune, Kampong Siem District, Kampong Cham Province, which has a history related to the tradition of "Srey Choul Dandeng Pros" and changed to "Pros Choul Dandeng Srey".
Sean Sokun, director of the Kampong Cham Provincial Department of Tourism, said that Phnom Pros Phnom Srey is also one of the most attractive resorts in Kampong Cham. In addition to pagodas, temples, stupas, Buddha statues, places of worship and genocide sites from the Khmer Rouge era, there are also many monkeys that tourists can visit or feed.
A trader who sells in Phnom Pros said that in addition to selling cakes, food and beverages for tourists, he also sells peanuts, bananas, sugar cane, etc., which tourists can buy for monkey food, and according to the same business, monkeys in Phnom Pros are close. 100 heads.
At a distance of about 300 meters from Phnom Pros, Phnom Srey also attracts tourists to visit every day. Yes, the natural scenery, shade of trees and the fresh air there also encourage tourists to climb to the top of the mountain and continue to enjoy the surrounding scenery.
According to Mr. Sean Sokun, in 2019, the Department of Tourism of Kampong Cham Province will organize the Phnom Pros Phnom Srey Cultural and Historical Resort to be more attractive in order to participate in the competition in the "Clean City Movement, Clean Resort, Good Service and Hospitality". "Good" at the national level. General Neth Savoeun verbally warns a deputy commissioner in Kandal province after using a fire truck for personal gain
(Phnom Penh): General Dr. Neth Savoeun, National Police Commissioner, verbally told Kandal Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Eav Chamroeun to warn Kandal Provincial Deputy Commissioner Ul Bunna that he used a fire truck for personal gain. By transporting water to mix cement with relatives in Saang district, Kandal province.
Lt. Gen. Eav Chamroeun told Fresh News this morning, February 21, 2019, that the National Police Commissioner had ordered him in a meeting to give an oral warning to Deputy Commissioner for Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Plan Ul. Bunna around taking the unit's car for personal use and if there is a next time will be punished by the forces.
General Eav Chamroeun stated, "His Excellency the National Police Commissioner has ordered me to verbally warn a Deputy Commissioner in a meeting related to the use of fire trucks without permission and for personal gain. Next time, we will follow the discipline of the National Police Force. ”
Please be informed that in relation to this case, the Fire Prevention and Extinguishing Department of the General Commission of National Police, Ministry of Interior has ordered all specialized offices in the Capital-Provincial Commissions to affix the name of the province (Capital-Provincial Police ...) on the vehicle. To avoid confusion from the public after a deputy commissioner of Kandal province took a fire truck for personal use, which led to the outcry of public criticism.
