The owners of the trucks told Fresh News in Svay Rieng province this morning that in the Mehathen Economic Zone, there were 700 trucks carrying workers every day, and this morning the area called them. The meeting discussed paying the region $ 10 per year for a car, but the workers' truck refused and the protest erupted.
Workers 'trucks claim that in the factories in the Mehathen Special Economic Zone, the factory has already paid all the money, so why are they still taking money from them, and no special economic zone is taking money from the workers' trucks? Just saw this one area that requires them to pay.
Workers 'trucks also requested the Special Economic Zone to reconsider taking money from workers' trucks because it can lose a lot of time that workers can not work overtime to walk to the national road to find a car to make a loss. From the factory owner. In that, the group of trucks transporting workers requested the Governor of Svay Rieng to intervene in this matter as well, so that the area would not take money from the trucks carrying workers because it would lead to the loss of workers.
