(World): While many observers criticized the US-North Korea agreement at last year's summit in Singapore due to the use of ambiguous language and lack of commitment, there was some controversy. He affirmed that the summit is very useful in stepping up cooperation between the two countries, which have been enemies for decades.
At the meeting, Trump will try to get North Korea to commit to the elimination of nuclear weapons, while Kim's top priority is to get relief from sanctions to liberate its economy. This means that both sides wish to benefit from the above meeting in the future.
1: Ask North Korea to provide a list and information on all nuclear weapons This proposal sounds a bit awkward, as we know that North Korea is unlikely to easily agree to this proposal, but at least it Can be considered as a strategy for political gain.
2. Agree to reward North Korea by stopping military exercises with South Korea. By suspending these exercises, Trump could save some money and make North Korea happy. The suspension of the annual military exercises, which are exercises to protect South Korea from attacks by North Korea.
In addition, this is not a new thing to suspend the exercise, because in the past, some annual exercises between the United States and the South Korean military have been reduced or suspended in the past. In the past, North Korea has criticized and warned of retaliation if US or South Korean troops approach its borders.
Such an incentive would be a gesture of goodwill, and would not break the United States' commitment to defend South Korea, as the United States could keep its promise through a network of bases in South Korea.
At the same time, South Korea's leftist government will be satisfied with the proposal to abandon the exercise, as the current South Korean administration considers the military exercise to be a major obstacle to negotiations with North Korea. Therefore, the decision to suspend this military exercise makes North Korea happy, South Korea is not offended by the United States, and the benefits can be considered as a win-win, win-win policy.
3. Make it clear that the talks focus on "denuclearization of North Korea", not "crisis on the Korean Peninsula". Completely nuclear weapons on the entire peninsula. And at the summit it was not clear whether it was referring to North Korea's nuclear weapons.
Emphasize that North Korea understands that although the United States has not deployed nuclear weapons on the Korean Peninsula, the United States may use nuclear weapons to defend South Korea if necessary. Thus, through the previous agreement, North Korea explained that "nuclear disarmament" could only happen without a military presence in South Korea, which is completely contrary to US perceptions.
4: Propose to establish a clear work plan and discussions in the future. In fact, the summit between the two leaders is open to the public, which always receives high attention from the general public. From the actual work to be done after the negotiations are hidden. Do not know where to go, what kind of results to achieve, will there be any meeting to monitor and evaluate.
While the elimination of nuclear weapons may take a long way, at least North Korea seems to be reducing its threats and provocations with its enemies.
From generation to generation, the next generation of North Koreans may see the United States as a potential partner rather than an enemy of the United States, which is considered a good thing, despite the summits. Twice is not enough to end the decades-old conflict.
