Samdech Techo Hun Sen Delivers a Message to Compatriots on the Occasion of the 20th National Mine Awareness Day
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that February 24 will be the 20th anniversary of the National Mine Awareness Day to commemorate people all over Cambodia, especially compatriots living in areas affected by national landmines. Explosions from war and cluster munitions, be extremely careful of the dangers posed by those bombs.
Samdech Techo added that landmines, explosive remnants of war and cluster munitions, a legacy of the Indochina War and Cambodia's internal conflict for more than three decades, not only caused serious tragedy to the lives and health of our people. But it is also an obstacle for the rehabilitation and development of family life and the national economy.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that in order to solve this problem, the Royal Government of Cambodia has considered the field of mine action as the 18th goal of the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals and has included this sector as an important element in Its rectangular strategy.
