Ministry of Health warns people not to eat 3 types of crocodiles that are poisonous and cause death
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health has once again reminded people across the country not to eat three types of crocodiles that are toxic and can cause serious illness and death when the toxins penetrate the central nervous system.
All three of these toxins are most toxic during the breeding season, which usually occurs in February, March, and between July and September. The difference is that the eggs and sperm are the most toxic, followed by the liver, intestines, skin and meat.
Symptoms begin 20 minutes to 2 hours after eating the fish. Symptoms include itchy bumps on the lips and mouth, followed by headache, dizziness, itchy tingling in the extremities, difficulty speaking, loss of balance. Muscle weakness, paralysis, numbness in the extremities, vomiting, diarrhea, fatigue, stiff jaw or may cause death.
