The Ambassador's assessment was made at the 17th meeting of the Cambodia-Japan Joint Committee under the agreement between Cambodia and Japan on liberalization, promotion and protection of investment on February 20, 2019, chaired by Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister, Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia.
The meeting is part of the Investment Maintenance Mechanism, which provides an opportunity for discussions between representatives of Cambodian state institutions and Japanese investors to explore challenges and suggestions aimed at improving the investment climate in Cambodia.
Mr. Sok Chendasophea thanked the Government and people of Japan for their continued support of Cambodia in the rehabilitation and development of the national economy. This morning, an exchange of letters was signed on the continued support of the Government of Japan for the implementation of two projects. Under concessional loans and grant financing of more than US $ 43 million.
He also briefed the meeting on the background of the meeting, which is a mechanism established under the agreement between Cambodia and Japan on liberalization, promotion and protection of investment, which was signed by Samdech Techo Prime Minister and Mr. Shinzo Abe. Shinzo Abe, Prime Minister of Japan on June 14, 2007.
He added that at the same time, in response to changes in the economic and geopolitical structure, the Royal Government is finalizing the preparation of new laws on investment and the law on special economic zones, taking into account the provision of smart incentives and incentives. Simplify the procedure.
Mr. Sok Chendasophea thanked all the participants and requested that this good spirit of cooperation continue to be in order to further improve the investment climate of Cambodia and contribute to attracting more foreign investment. .
At the same time, he also informed the meeting about the recommendations of Samdech Techo Prime Minister, which requires the Council for the Development of Cambodia to cooperate with stakeholders to organize the 18th Royal Government and Private Sector Forum on March 29 for further discussion. More on issues related to reforms to be implemented to accelerate economic growth.
