A factory in Sangkat Rokar Thom, Chbar Morn City, drains water with chemicals that cause serious harm to people and animals, people request immediate intervention from the authorities
(Kampong Speu): An unidentified factory in Toul Thnong village, Rokar Thom commune, Chbar Morn city, Kampong Speu province, has leaked blue water, suspected to have chemicals into the canals that people use daily until killed. Hundreds of chickens and ducks have been drinking water from the canal.
The owner of a duck farm and the people living near the main canal informed Fresh News Agency on the afternoon of February 20, 2019 that there is suspected sewage with chemicals from the factory every day. To harm their health, in particular, have killed hundreds of their chickens and ducks.
They said that the water that flows into the canal through the sewer from the factory above seems to be intended to be embedded into the canal, secretly from the eyes of the people and the authorities, until the water recedes to see the sewer into the canal for many years.
The villagers insist that the relevant authorities, the environment and the Department of Water Resources, intervene so that the factory can close the sewer and stop it from entering the canal, otherwise the health and the animals he raises will be severely affected.
