Minister Mam Bun Heng Urges Health Officials to Strengthen Malaria Eradication Strategy to Eliminate by 2025
(Siem Reap): The Minister of Health, Prof. Mam Bunheng, urged health officials across the country to strengthen the implementation of malaria eradication strategies to achieve the goals of the program by 2025.
This statement was made by Minister Mam Bunheng on the occasion of presiding over the opening ceremony of the 2018 Annual Meeting and 2019 Orientation of the National Center for Malaria Control, Parasitology and Bacteriology of the Ministry of Health on 20 February 2019 at the Hotel. Angkor Era, Siem Reap.
Minister Mam Bunheng said that the active contribution of relevant officials is absolutely necessary to achieve the National Strategic Plan for Malaria Eradication 2011-2025, especially in the early stages to eradicate malaria. Defeat Falciparom by 2020 and strive to prevent the spread of dengue fever in a timely manner, maintain and expand the coverage of collective deworming to more than 90%.
Moreover, Professor Mam Bunheng said that the death rate from malaria has decreased significantly, but the number of patients is still large, which needs to be focused on continuing to provide malaria testing by Test for malaria in high-risk groups in malaria-endemic areas and provide immediate treatment for malaria.
In addition, the Minister further recommended:
* Helping military families to treat malaria
Exchange experiences from one place to another to eradicate malaria, dengue fever
* Inspect the construction site, car park and the area around the house to eliminate tiger mosquitoes, worms.
