Senior Minister Sun Chanthol Attends Annual Meeting of the United Nations Road Transport Commission in Geneva
(Phnom Penh): Senior Minister Sun Chanthol, Minister of Public Works and Transport, led a Cambodian delegation to the 81st Annual Meeting of the United Nations Road Transport Committee at the United Nations in Phnom Penh. Geneva, Switzerland.
The meeting was held from 19 to 22 February 2019 with the participation of the Minister of Transport and the heads of delegations from Africa, Asia, Europe and the Middle East and various relevant international organizations.
On the afternoon of February 19, 2019, the meeting adopted a resolution on promoting cooperation, harmonization and integration in the era of transport automation.
The meeting also approved the strategy of the UN Road Transport Commission 2030, the Committee's action plan and revised work plan.
Four wastewater treatment plants in Sihanoukville are 80 percent complete and scheduled for completion by mid-March
(Preah Sihanouk): Four wastewater treatment plants at Ekareach Beach, Sokha Osaat Beach and Ochheuteal Beach, as well as the preparation of concrete drainage system and HDPE pipe in Sihanoukville, Preah Sihanouk Province, so far completed 80 % And is scheduled to be completed by mid-March.
The report of the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia said on the afternoon of February 20, 2019 that the first and second wastewater treatment plants will be completed by the end of February, while the wastewater treatment plants. The third and fourth will be completed in mid-March 2019.
Please be reminded that four wastewater treatment plants have been built along the coast in Sihanoukville to avoid the discharge of wastewater into the sea. This wastewater treatment plant started on November 27, 2018. With the decision to build a wastewater treatment plant, the owner of a hotel and a large-scale construction project in Sihanoukville, Sihanoukville Province, contributed a total of US $ 3,100,000.
The decision was made during a meeting on water pollution in Sihanoukville between Deputy Prime Minister Chea Sophara, Minister of Land Management, Urban Planning and Construction and Chairman of the National Committee for Coastal Management and Development of Cambodia with representatives of companies and hotel owners. In Sihanoukville.
