(Kandal): The Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on February 20, 2019, expressed his satisfaction with the stability of the riel in Cambodia and further instructed the National Bank of Cambodia to continue its efforts to pay attention to Exchange rate fluctuations.
He said this on the occasion of Samdech Techo's meeting with a total of 11,227 workers from 34 factories in Kandal province.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen confirmed that the Royal Government has set the base exchange rate of 1 dollar equal to 4050 Riels. However, the value of the Cambodian riel has been relatively stable, with prices below 4,050 riel per dollar, only in August or September, when the riel depreciated by the dollar, up to 4,050 riel or above 4,090 riel.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that maintaining the stability of the riel exchange rate has thus benefited more than 1 million workers who pay their salaries in dollars.
Samdech continued that the National Bank of Cambodia has a duty to intervene to keep the exchange rate stable, not too low and too expensive. When the riel appreciates, the riel is released to buy dollars, and when the riel depreciates, the dollar is released to buy back the riel.
The Prime Minister stated that the Royal Government not only considered raising the wages of workers and raising the salaries of civil servants in the Armed Forces, but also considered macroeconomics, especially to prevent the rise in commodity prices. Purchasing power of the increased salary for workers and civil servants of the Armed Forces.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the Royal Government has tried to keep the market price of goods from rising while salaries have been increased. If wages are raised but commodity prices rise, then wages and salaries will not make sense.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Hun Sen reminded that in order to help prevent the increase in fuel price, the Royal Government of Cambodia has provided 2 cents per liter and the fuel company has provided 2 cents. At present, the price of regular gasoline is 3,400 riel per liter and diesel is 3,450 riel per liter.
