After a series of meetings with workers, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, decided to put in place a policy to subsidize workers during childbirth to alleviate their hardships. Samdech Techo decided to provide 400,000 Riels for maternity workers, 1,800,000 Riels for those who gave birth to twins and 1.2 million Riels for those who gave birth to triplets.
