Under the policy of turning the former war zone into a development area, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, has started to launch a series of development plans for Vel Veng district. Initially, demining forces were deployed to provide land for people to grow crops and avoid danger to their livelihoods.
In addition, the Royal Government of Samdech Techo Hun Sen also built an additional road, National Road 55, connecting National Road 5 near Pursat provincial town to the battlefield until the border of Thmor Da. Thailand. The construction of this road is very difficult, having to cross the mountain range to be able to connect to the rocky border area.
In addition to the construction of a connected road infrastructure, the Royal Government of Cambodia decided to authorize Tycoon Try Pheap's company to develop the Thmar Da border area into a special economic zone in 2010. The granting of investment rights in the area aims to turn the border area, which was once a quiet area, into a former war zone into an economic and development zone.
The development in this area has encountered many problems, such as the transportation of materials, because at the beginning of the development was not as easy as today, the company tried to clear the mountain to get access to the construction of other buildings. In addition, the problem of unexploded ordnance left over from the war era is also a major obstacle to development.
