Please be reminded that until the 15th day of the full moon day of March, Buddhists who always celebrate a big festival called "Meak Bochea". This ceremony is an opportunity for Buddhists to commemorate some important events that took place in the Buddhist era. Meak Bochea ceremonies are usually held by Buddhists or Buddhists at pagodas or at the Shakyamuni Stupa, where the relics of the Buddha are kept.
Buddhist scholars confirm that Meak Bochea Day is an important event in Buddhism, or a great time to commemorate the Buddha's teachings when he was still alive.
