The Ministry of Health celebrates the 8th anniversary of the National Maternal and Child Health Day under the theme "Importance of nutrition during the first 1000 days of life"
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health of Cambodia, together with development partners, on February 18, 2019, celebrated the 8th National Day on Maternal, Infant and Child Health under the theme "The Importance of Nutrition during the First 1000 Days of Life". . The program was presided over by the Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health, Prof. Eng Huot.
According to Professor Tung Rathavy, President of the National Center for Maternal and Child Health, the first 1,000 days are from the time a woman becomes pregnant until she is two years old. This period is very important for the survival of children and, in addition, for their lifelong growth.
"When children do not get enough nutrition during the 1,000 days, it can cause many serious complications and be difficult to improve, which can lead to frequent childhood illness," she said. Stunting delays growth and can even kill. "Therefore, we need to check and take care of health before, during and after childbirth until the child is 2 years old is very necessary."
