A Chinese province plans to build a 6,000-kilometer forest road network to conserve and enhance natural resources
Guizhou, a mountainous province in southwest China, plans to build a 6,000-kilometer forest road network, which will be completed by 2025, in a defense-oriented tourism network. And conserve the natural environment at the highest level. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Monday evening, February 18, 2019.
Guizhou is known as home to China's vast natural resources, with forests covering about 57 percent of the southwestern province, and Chinese authorities plan to build five forest lanes and a length. A total of 6,000 km are networked in the mountainous areas of the province to facilitate tourism and conserve diverse resources.
Authorities and environmental officials inspect and ban Korean companies from grinding cassava, draining wastewater into lakes
(Kratie): Kratie Municipality Authority and Provincial Department of Environment on February 18, 2019 led a team to inspect the Korean company Sing Song Cassava Mill on National Road 7, Sangkat Orussey, Kratie City, Kratie Province. Drainage of wastewater into canals and lakes affects the livelihoods of local people in Kratie and Chit Borei districts.
Authorities confirmed this afternoon that after the authorities and the Department of Environment visited the company, the company confirmed that the drainage is good water, but in November 2018, there was heavy rain to allow dirty water to flow into the pool. It flows through the end of the Sayo and the company is trying to fix it so that there is no bad smell and no more dirty water flowing in.
Mr. Chhay Duong Savuth, Director of Kratie Provincial Department of Environment, said that after he visited the company and asked to bring the company, he said that the drainage from February 7 until February 17. The fish were found dead and it was suspected that the water was poisoned by the company. He said that this case does not know the truth yet, and he took the water that flows into the lake to check the Ministry of Environment, but do not know the results.
He added that if the preliminary conclusion is that these days, the sky is very hot and the fish appear, then people see and go fishing, causing murky water and poisonous fish die.
The director of the department also stated that he had banned the company from draining water to public places. Seeing that the water did not have an impact, the department allowed it so that it would not affect the general population anymore.
It should be noted that the Korean cassava flour company SingSong, located on National Road 7, Sangkat Or Russey, Kratie City, Kratie Province, has been dumping the company's waste into canals and lakes, causing serious damage to people's lives. In Kratie city and Chit Borey district.
According to the report of the local authorities, the fish poisoning in the lakes and streams was caused by the people due to the poisoning caused by the discharge of waste from Korean companies into the lakes and streams. In such a toxic situation, people are concerned about the safety of their health as well as the animals that now rely on lakes, canals and streams.
