"Who is the most important teacher of children" is what psychologists will reveal on February 24 in the workshop "How to educate children"
(Phnom Penh): Education is really important for people in today's society, especially for young children, which is an important resource for the future, and education does not only refer to sending children to school, but also includes With parental education to children directly as well. If you look at the problem in the family today is the lack of attention and insufficient time of parents to their children.
Due to the lack of time, busyness, abandonment of children makes children develop bad habits in the use of electronic devices and many technology products, which is the problem of creating a gap with parents, creating a child irritability when nothing. They want to be unaware of the external environment and create health problems as well.
With all of this in mind, psychologist Hoeur Sethul suggests that all parents should spend more time with their children and should understand the needs, attention and development of children by developing reading habits. With your child or start doing more fun activities than just giving your cell phone or other gadgets.
She also added that the development of children's brains is an important part that parents should understand at what age children should study what skills.
Various issues in the family will be raised in the workshop on "Methods of educating children" with the participation of two distinguished speakers, Mr. Hoeur Sethul, a psychologist who specializes in family counseling with experience. For more than 20 years, Ms. Khoy Rany, an early childhood educator with 8 years of experience, works with parents or guardians of children and teachers on key topics such as:
First: Understand the development and needs of children. Second: Build a positive relationship with children. Third: How to cultivate good habits, discipline and active behavior.
The workshop on "Child Education Methods" will be held on 24 February 2019 at Singapore SCIA International School from 9am to 4pm. Mr. Chea Chanto instructed officials to continue to monitor the implementation of laws and regulations of microfinance institutions and rural credit operators
