The National Council for Social Development and Economic Development of Thailand on Monday released a report saying that economic growth in 2018 was 4.1 percent, the highest rate since 2012 in the fourth quarter of last year. As a result, Thailand's gross domestic product (GDP) has also risen sharply. The number of tourists returning during the last three months of 2018 increased by 4.3 percent compared to the same period last year (2017).
However, all the positives in the Thai economy could be at risk due to the potential for chaos if the Thai people perceive the first general election to be held since. The 2014 military coup on March 24 was not free and transparent.
Senior official of the Ministry of Cult: The next generation of Cambodians does not seem to have much understanding of Meak Bochea like foreign festivals!
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pen Vibol, Undersecretary of State of the Ministry of Cults and Religions, requested the Cambodian people, who are Buddhists, to help post more content related to the Meak Bochea festival on various social media, because this festival does not seem to have much understanding from children. The next generation of Cambodians is not like foreign festivals.
Mr. Pen Vibol said this on the occasion of his participation in the Meak Bochea Ceremony, which was organized by the Buddhist University of Sihanoukville in collaboration with the Lotus Company at the Chaktomuk Conference.
The program was also invited and invited as speakers by experts in Buddhism and society, as well as invited and invited by senior officials of 5 ministries, monks, students and the general public about 500 people / person in order to discuss in detail. The meaning and philosophy learned from this festival.
Mr. Pen Vibol said that at present, the Meak Bochea festival does not seem to have as much understanding of the next generation of Cambodian children as other foreign festivals in the world, and for some Cambodians who are Buddhists do not understand clearly. From the true meaning of Meak Bochea. He urged people to pay attention to the organization of this big Buddhist festival, especially in schools to teach students to understand more about the celebration of Meak Bochea.
According to the Undersecretary of State for the Ministry of Cults and Religions, Cambodians at the university, companies and many people do not know that February 19 is Meak Bochea Day. The problem is that not many people know and know this important festival because the promotion of this festival does not have a clear picture.
Ms. Neth Phoumery continued, "In supporting Buddhism, we Buddhists need to know the Dharma, know the rules of the Buddha, so we can support, we do not just support. So we go with all our heart and all our materials to make the process go smoothly. ”
Preah Moha Vimal Dhamma Pin Sem, a member of the Royal Council, a member of the National Assembly of Cambodian Buddhist monks, said that the Meak Bochea festival is a special festival for Buddhists all over the world.
Venerable Vimal Dhamma Pin Sem emphasized that Meak Bochea is celebrated to commemorate the day of the Apostles' Assembly of Preah Samma Samput, our teacher. In the Meak Bochea ceremony, there are two important things: first, the quadrangular assembly is the day on which the Buddha declared the establishment of Buddhism, and second, the imposition of the age of his Nirvana.
