(Tbong Khmum): During the Mine Awareness Campaign in Prek Touch Village, Chiro I Commune, Tbong Khmum District, on February 18, 2019, Senior Minister Ly Thuch, First Deputy Chairman of the Mine Authority, called on all people to report to the authorities. When mines and unexploded ordnance are found, do not touch or recycle because some of them are still causing harm to the people at all times.
The senior minister said that our country is peaceful, but the remnants of the war are still threatening the lives of the people at all times, while unexploded ordnance is left a lot on Cambodian territory.
He stated that in order to solve this problem and not to see the people continue to suffer from the remnants of the war, Samdech Techo Prime Minister has made efforts to clear all mines from our territory through the CMAC team that carried out clearing activities. Clear all mines and unexploded ordnance from the territory of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
At the same time, Mr. Cheam Chansophorn, Governor of Tbong Khmum Province, also said, "We must join together. When we see unexploded ordnance, do not touch it, put a sign and then report to the authorities to provide information to experts Check and remove.
He added that since Tbong Khmum is a province with a large number of unexploded ordnance left over from the war, he asked the Mines Authority to step up research work to find all the ammunition as soon as possible so as not to cause any danger to Every citizen.
There will also be presentations on the dangers of landmines and other unexploded ordnance, as well as Q&A sessions to raise awareness among the people and students involved.
