The Royal Government of Cambodia is preparing a new draft law on investment to be more attractive and more competitive.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea, Minister Delegate to the Prime Minister and Secretary General of the Council for the Development of Cambodia (ECCC) on 18 February 2019, chaired a consultation meeting to gather input from private sector representatives. Development partners of about 70 research institutions and legal consulting firms.
The purpose of this meeting is to discuss and collect input from all these institutions as a basis for preparing a new draft law on investment to be more attractive and increase Cambodia's competitiveness.
During the meeting, Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea expressed his deep gratitude and warm welcome for the large presence, which clearly showed the high attention of all participants on the Law on Investment of Cambodia.
He recalled the background of the establishment of Cambodia's first investment law after the first parliamentary elections in 1993, which was approved and implemented since 1994, which was then amended in 2003. In line with the economic and social development of Cambodia at that time.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea further stated that the Council for the Development of Cambodia has already studied and received some input from the Japan International Cooperation Agency (JICA), the report on the review of investment policy in Cambodia. Cambodia of the Organization for Economic Co-operation and Development (OECD), and the International Finance Corporation (IFC) on the experience and practice of drafting investment laws of countries in the region.
Representatives of the private sector, development partners, research institutions and legal consultants who attended the meeting expressed great interest in drafting a new investment law and provided some preliminary input, as well as pledging to submit comments and suggestions. More input to the Council for the Development of Cambodia in the near future.
Mr. Sok Chenda Sophea expressed his deep gratitude to all the participants who provided a lot of input in today's meeting and made the meeting fruitful. He hopes that with the continued cooperation of all stakeholders, the new Investment Law of Cambodia will emerge in the near future, which will be welcomed by local and foreign investors.
