Ministry of Environment and community plant trees in Prey Lang while people are still worried about criminals stealing trees and shooting wild animals
(Kampong Thom): The Ministry of Environment, together with more than 300 people from the protected communities of the four provinces of Preah Vihear, Kampong Thom, Stung Treng and Kratie, which is covered by Prey Lang, held the first tree planting ceremony to strengthen the management of natural resources. Longevity persists as people in key areas remain deeply concerned about the problem of crooks logging and hunting.
On that occasion, the Prey Lang Provincial Committee of Preah Vihear Province, Ms. Phok Hong, said that the purpose of organizing the tree planting was to preserve the traditions of the indigenous people and to commemorate the forest that helped to preserve and nurture the people. Citizens as well as urging people to participate in the conservation of forests and protect biodiversity in the "Prey Lang" wildlife sanctuary even better.
Vong San, head of the Kbal Khla community of Prey Lang in Kampong Thom province, stated that Prey Lang is very important for the people because it can help provide rain, reduce heat, as well as provide forest products such as fruits, vines, mushrooms and resin. Including rubber poles that help communities earn income in all seasons.
"But the area also faces challenges as some thugs continue to steal trees and hunt wildlife, while community forestry networks and authorities are lacking after patrols," San stressed.
However, Mr. Khieu Borin commended the communities of the four provinces, including park rangers, for taking care to protect and love the forest, making the forest in Prey Lang in good condition to this day.
He considered that today's event will make people more aware of the value of the forest to all people and they will be able to better manage their resources.
He also stated that the Ministry of Environment has been paying attention to community development in all protected areas from 2017 through the provision of animal breeds, agricultural equipment and other community livelihood activities, and the community in the sanctuary. Prey "Prey Lang" will receive the same support in 2019.
It should be noted that the traditional tree planting festival is now organized by the Ministry of Environment in collaboration with the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) and the Prey Lang Community Network in order to raise awareness of the benefits of forests to the people and to get started. Strengthen the cooperation in the conservation and management of natural resources of the community in the "Prey Lang" wildlife sanctuary is still beautiful, covered with natural veils.
"Prey Lang" Wildlife Sanctuary was established by Sub-Decree No. 074, dated May 09, 2016, with a total area of 431,683 hectares, located next to Kratie Province, Kampong Thom Province, Preah Vihear Province, Stung Treng Province. This protected area has the potential of rich natural resources and biodiversity, which is the rainfall slope for Stung Sen and flows into the Tonle Sap, serving the agricultural sector in economic, social, environmental and cultural development.
