According to Sok Touch, the announcement of the EBA suspension process has led the Royal Government of Cambodia to implement a number of reforms to help local businesses and improve Cambodian trade. Measures that Sok Touch sees as taking place after the EBA suspension include the elimination of Camcontrols at the border, the abolition of naval units (Kamsap), and the ban on exporters obtaining certificates of origin.
