(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs considers Kem Sokha's mention of the US Embassy as an act of lack of diplomacy and disrespect for Cambodia's sovereignty.
In a statement issued on February 16, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation was shocked by the gesture. The Ministry of Foreign Affairs considers this one-sided comment on Kem Sokha's case to be a clear intention to mislead the public.
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation also expressed grave concern over such actions, calling the gesture "non-diplomatic and disrespectful to Cambodia's sovereignty."
"The State Department is obliged to remind the US Embassy in Phnom Penh of Article 41 of the 1961 Vienna Convention on Diplomatic Relations, which specifically requires the US Embassy to respect laws and regulations and not to interfere in Cambodia's internal affairs. No, ”he said. This is the confirmation of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of Cambodia.
"The Kingdom of Cambodia has always respected the sovereignty of other countries and has never commented on the shameful scandals of its senior officials and politicians," the statement reminded the United States. "This move by the US Embassy is contrary to the current efforts of the two countries to improve bilateral relations for the common benefit of both countries and peoples."
While urging the US Embassy in Phnom Penh to immediately suspend politically motivated and non-diplomatic activities, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation reaffirmed Cambodia's commitment to upholding the rule of law and maintaining peace. The stability and public order that the Cambodian people are enjoying today.
