MOSCOW (Reuters) - US Secretary of State Mike Pompeo has called on Pakistan to stop providing safe havens for asylum seekers after 46 Indian security forces were killed in a deadly suicide bombing in Kashmir. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Saturday afternoon, February 16, 2019.
"The United States condemns the deadly attacks on Indian security forces and I extend my deepest condolences to the victims and their families," Pompeo said on Twitter on Friday. "But we will stand with India to fight terrorists, and Pakistan must stop providing a safe haven for terrorists who are threatening international security as a whole."
On Thursday, 46 Indian security forces were killed in a suicide bomb attack on their convoy in Kashmir, a disputed area between India and Pakistan. Pakistan-based militant group Jaish-e Mohammed has claimed responsibility for the attack, but Islamabad has denied any wrongdoing.
