(Kampong Chhnang): A suspect who was arrested in connection with the murder of the victim, the owner of pure water in Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province in May 2018, was acquitted. This is according to the letter of notification to the victim's family, which was received by Fresh News on February 16, 2019.
It should be noted that at 7:50 pm on May 16, 2018, the owner of the water craft, Mr. Bin Hoeun, 61 years old, was shot by a gunman with three long weapons in the waist, causing him to fall under the car. Pure water while robbing a house to earn money in Trapeang Chrey village, Khlong Popok commune, Teuk Phos district, Kampong Chhnang province.
After the murder, Kampong Chhnang Provincial Police conducted a search and arrested a suspect named Chhom Chhorn, 48 years old. Teuk Phos District, Kampong Chhnang Province.
According to the notification letter of the Investigating Judge of the Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court, Mr. Khieu Phanna, on 30 January 2019, “We have decided to issue a waiver order under Article 247 of the Criminal Procedure Code. Chhom Chhorn was acquitted of premeditated murder in Trapeang Chrey village, Khnong Popok commune, Srok Teuk Phos, Kampong Chhnang province on May 16, 2018. The offense is punishable under Article 200 of the Penal Code.
(Kampong Thom): Major General Ouk Kosal, Provincial Police Commissioner of Kampong Thom Province, this morning, February 16, 2019, led 30 police officers of Santuk District Police to help build a house measuring 6 meters by 4 meters made of wood. Laying of flooring, wall panels, floorboards, roofing, zinc roof, handed over to the families of veterans living in Kang Meas village, Phnov commune, Santuk district, Kampong Thom province.
The house was built for 46-year-old Tuy Lai Huot, the wife of Horn Hay, a Royal Cambodian Armed Forces officer, who died during a war mission with Pol Pot soldiers in Santuk district during 1997. . This house was donated by Mr. Chea Chanto, Governor of the National Bank of Cambodia and Ms. Khieu Sina.
