General Chhay Sinarith Asks All Casino Owners to Reset Security Cameras to Provide Convenience to Authorities (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): General Chhay Sinarith, Deputy Commissioner General of the National Police Businesses (casinos) throughout Cambodia to redesign security cameras to provide convenience to law enforcement in the event of a problem.
The request was made on the occasion of General Chhay Sinarith's participation in a meeting to disseminate security measures to the owners of gambling companies, which was held at the Ministry of Interior on the afternoon of February 15, 2019. .
The meeting was held in the presence of Ms. Nguon Sokha, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Economy and Finance and Chair of the Joint Commission for the Suppression of Gambling, Casino, Lottery, Online Gambling and All Kinds of Illegal Gambling and its subordinates. More.
General Chhay Sinarith stated, "We urge all casino companies to reset their security systems, including: security cameras, security gates and X-ray machines."
According to the Deputy Chief of the National Police, when something goes wrong, the casino owner only takes a long time to check the security camera system to show the authorities that it is responsible for the perpetrators. Easy to escape.
In connection with such cases, General Chhay Sinarith said, "In all casinos, we want to have two separate cameras, one for security and one for the casino to facilitate. Reach the authorities when something goes wrong. ”
At the same time, the general said that the police force does not have a clear position in the casino company, at the gate, only security forces. The general said that in their country, through the gates of the casino company, they always have the police force.
General Chhay Sinarith emphasized that if the casino owners do not want to show people, they should adjust the technology to have scanners, security gates, security cameras and so on. The general added that the police did not want to go to the camera, which only shows the table of gamblers.
