Pursat Orange Plans to Register Geographical Indication
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Abrady, Director of the Intellectual Property Department of the Ministry of Commerce, said that Pursat oranges are planned to register geographical marks soon to protect the interests of producers and help improve the lives of producers. Better. This is according to the release of the Ministry of Information on February 16, 2019.
A senior official of the Ministry of Commerce said that the registration of geographical marks to Pursat oranges to help prevent fraud and to improve the livelihood of producers to source goods for domestic supply and export. Go abroad because some countries require goods with this geographical mark.
Mr. Abradi continued that the Ministry of Commerce officials visited the workshop to promote the geographical mark of Pursat-Battambang orange to the relevant parties to study before registering the geographical mark in the future to help increase the price. Add another level to producers, while currently Pursat-Battambang oranges cost between 20,000 to 40,000 riel per pound.
The director of the department also claimed that in addition to Pursat-Battambang oranges, the Ministry of Commerce also noted some other agricultural products that are planned to be registered in the future geographical mark, such as duck eggs, rice fields in Takeo province. Kampot and Prahok, Siem Reap and so on.
Mr. Rady stated that the registration of GI trademarks has some difficulties and takes a long time. For example, Koh Trung grapefruit in Kratie province took about two years to study in detail and used more than half a million US dollars before receiving. Registered a geographical mark with Kampot pepper and Kampong Speu palm sugar.
