Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, February 15: 1,227 illegal vehicles found and 869 fined
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for February 15, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 6,433 vehicles and found 1,722 vehicles (82% motorcycles), 504 education vehicles and A fine of 910 units, according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 3,507 helmets and goggles were inspected on February 15, 3,594 education helmets and 739 glasses were fined.
For the results of the 15-day inspection from February 1 to 15, 2019, the police inspected 76,932 vehicles and found 13,205 offending vehicles (78% motorcycles), including education 4,975 units and fined 8,230 units. Vietnam is considering science and technology through many exemptions for investors
(VOVworld) - The Vietnamese government has decided to provide additional benefits to businesses operating in the science and technology sector, including corporate tax cuts and tax exemptions, lower land and water rents, and incentives. Loans, etc. This was quoted from the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Friday evening, February 15, 2019.
Under the new Vietnamese government law, which will take effect on March 20, science and technology businesses will generate revenue from the development and sale of products from scientific research and development. Technology will receive the same corporate tax deduction and exemption as businesses planning new investments in scientific research and technology development.
In other words, these businesses will be exempt from corporate tax for four years and receive a 50 percent tax deduction for the next nine years. With regard to credit incentives, the decree states that projects that invest in products derived from scientific and technological research of businesses will be provided with state-owned investment loans.
Businesses working in the field of science and technology, as well as the application of science and technology in production and trade, will receive financial support or credit with low interest rates from the National Fund for Technology and other funds.
Vietnam has attracted a lot of attention in the last decade through the launch of its own satellites, the establishment of the National Science and Space Development Agency, and the attraction of large international car and aircraft technology companies to open factories. Domestic equipment and the establishment of a car factory as well as smartphones themselves.
