The Ministry of Culture will hold a nationwide youth art festival on February 20 to celebrate National Cultural Day on March 3.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Culture and Fine Arts will open the 5th National Youth Art Festival (2015-2019) on February 20, 2019 at the Chaktomuk Conference Hall to celebrate the 21st National Cultural Day on March 3. Presided over by Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia.
The main purpose of this art festival is to educate and train young Cambodians, especially middle and high school students to understand the true value and techniques of performing traditional arts, as well as to promote the spirit of love, preservation and protection of intangible cultural heritage. Sustainable and progressive over time.
