The Cambodia Securities Exchange continues to share its stock trading strategy with the public to boost the sector.
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodia Securities Exchange continues to make every effort to share its stock trading strategy with the public in order to make the sector more dynamic and dynamic.
In particular, the Cambodia Securities Exchange also held a press conference on "Stock Trading Strategies to Become Successful Investors in the Third Stock Trading Competition". The conference was held to share knowledge with the participants, with the participation of Mr. Jong Weon HA, Deputy General Director of the Cambodia Securities Exchange, as well as many successful speakers.
In that conference, many experts shared their knowledge and important importance about stock trading in Cambodia.
"To be successful in the stock market, investors should first understand the business situation and management of the company, then step into investing in stocks," he said.
Mr. Lak Hong, the third winner speaker, also shared his experience on stock trading. He said that in order to be successful in trading, you must have three main points, including: 1, the potential of the company, 2, the company's report and third, how the company plans for the future?
He added that these three points have different meanings, including the potential of the company is focused on profit or services, the second, the company report is focused on finance, how much are the real assets of the company? And third is the company's revenue and expenses.
Ms. Som Ny, the second winner, also shared, "For me, who bought and traded this stock, I have three goals: 1, to understand the stock trading and profit in this field 2. "Buying stock is not complicated and thirdly, the participation of all of you will become a participation to make the stock market run smoothly."
Mr. Tieng Chhnom, the first winner, added, "Anyone can trade stocks, and this trading requires traders to understand the price fluctuations and the time, because not all stocks can rise forever. "No, so it is necessary to monitor and study the stock when it goes up and when it goes down a lot."
