Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia grants derivatives broker license to PP Link Security
(Phnom Penh): PP Link Security has officially launched in Cambodia after receiving a derivatives broker license from the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia, and PP Link Security will be the first company to offer three different types of financial trading services in Cambodia. Cambodia.
The license, passed in February, allows companies to do business and provide trading services on a wide range of derivatives products, including precious metals, foreign currencies and crude oil.
With rich international experience, professional team, transparent trading program, leveraged trading products and excellent service, PP Link Security is expected to grow rapidly in the Cambodian market and expand its presence. Its consistently worldwide.
"We are proud to have the license as well as the support of the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia (SEC) to enable us to contribute to the financial markets of Cambodia and to help Cambodians develop knowledge and skills in trading," said Alex So, Governor of Phi Phi Securities. They.
He said that through our expertise and professionalism, after spending a lot of time identifying what the market needs and improving the quality of our consulting team, PPL Securities is ready to make a difference. And provide friendly competition to bring out the best in investors.
He added that PPL Securities is currently expanding its services by adding securities trading and financial advisory services. The official licensing for the launch of these two services will make PPLing Security the first and only company to have such a service in Cambodia.
"The stock market here has been operating for many years, so we see a point where it can be improved and we believe it can add value on the road to success," said Alex So. Great. At the same time, we aim to help investors analyze the market and make professional trading decisions, and this is why we are applying for a financial advisory license from the Securities and Exchange Commission of Cambodia.
