(Phnom Penh): A case of domestic violence occurred after a husband called his wife and refused to pick her up while she was home, resulting in a verbal dispute that led to the use of violence The husband beat and strangled his wife until he fainted in the field. The children cried all over the house.
The violent incident in the family happened at 8:00 pm on February 14, 2019 in Thmor Koul village, Sangkat Choam Chao II, Khan Por Senchey, Phnom Penh.
Police said that before the incident, residents heard the family quarrel, cheating on household items and the sound of children crying all over the house, and then their son came out. From inside the house and told that their parents were beating each other immediately, the villagers in the above village also called the authorities to intervene immediately.
Police said that as soon as the people complained, the police arrived at the scene and saw the husband with full nail wounds, but did not see his wife, while the police shouted for his wife but did not hear a response. Suspicious authorities went up to the dwarf, saw the wife fainted on the mattress, immediately called the people nearby to help move the breathing and sent to a private hospital immediately.
Police said that the case that caused the violence in the family was because the husband was not comfortable and called his wife several times, but his wife refused to accept after a while. When his wife picked up the phone because he was too angry, he insulted his wife and went to work.
He also had a heated argument when he got home, his wife cheated on his wedding photos and his husband cheated on his wife's phone. Until the violence broke out, the husband grabbed his hair and strangled his wife, causing her to faint. The husband was also injured because his wife was bitten by a nail.
