(Phnom Penh): Along with highly appreciating the efforts of the police force and civil servants under the control of the Ministry of Interior, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, urged the police force of civil servants. Justice officials and public service providers strive to work more efficiently to meet the needs of society and the people.
At the Closing Ceremony of the Annual Meeting of the Ministry of Interior on February 14, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen gave eight recommendations to the police force and civil servants. At the Advisory Group of the Ministry of Interior. These eight recommendations are expected to contribute to maintaining security, order, peace, and development, especially to improve access to public services.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's eight recommendations include:
Third, to continue to cooperate with the authorities, competent forces and neighboring countries in the region and internationally to jointly prevent and timely suppress terrorist activities, international crimes, information crimes and transnational crimes of all kinds to strengthen security and Social order.
Fourth, to strengthen the responsibility to manage immigrants by paying attention to and improving the control of entry and exit through the border by land, sea and air. At the same time, it is necessary to increase cooperation in the management of accommodation, business and activities of foreigners, immigrants in the country in accordance with the immigration law, labor law and other regulations in force of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
Sixth, to make effective, transparent and accountable in the provision of public services under the jurisdiction of the Ministry of Interior and the sub-national administration by expanding the provision of sub-national services through the OWSO mechanism. Sub-national level to expand more to narrow the provision of services closer to the people.
Seventh, according to the forecast, our country will have hot and dry weather and the dry season will be longer than last year, so please the Ministry of Water Resources to cooperate with the Capital and Provincial Administration to control the local water system and water sources for use. In daily life and increase the dry season to have measures to protect and use the remaining water sources for use in the daily lives of the people.
