Four Vietnamese arrested in Bavet for drug possession, large number of exhibits confiscated
(Svay Rieng): Svay Rieng Provincial Police in cooperation with Bavet City Administration and Bavet City Police led by Mr. Lim Seang Heng, Deputy Governor of Bavet City and Colonel Khorn Darasambath, Deputy Commissioner for Immigration Planning on February 14, 2019. The administration of rented houses found 4 Vietnamese people, 3 women, involved in drug trafficking and use cases at rented houses in Bavet Kandal village, Bavet commune, Svay Rieng province.
During the operation, the police confiscated 3 large packages of white gram powder (methamphetamine I), 40 tablets (ecstasy) and 5 mobile phones. Authorities said that the four suspects and exhibits have been handed over to Bavet City Drug Specialists to continue the proceedings.
The EBA is an EU initiative that allows the import of all goods except arms to the EU from less developed countries, which enjoy preferential tariffs and quotas. The EBA is part of the EU Preferential System, which came into force on March 5, 2001.
All imported goods will receive preferential tariffs and quotas if they comply with the rules of origin and other relevant rules. The project gives priority to 48 least developed countries, including Cambodia, which has benefited from the initiative.
In this regard, some questions have been raised that without trade preferences, everything except the "EBA" weapon from the European Union, what would the Cambodian economy be like now and in the future?
Overall, if Cambodia does not receive trade preferences from the European Union now or in the future, Cambodia will not die, the Cambodian economy will continue to move forward based on a number of key factors, such as:
1. Cambodia's labor costs are lower than other countries if we are productive and have a lot of potential. In economics, productivity is measured or divided by wages, which means that if investors spend $ 1 in our country, how much productivity do they get back, and if it costs the same $ 1 in other developed countries? How much productivity?
For example, Burma, which has lower wages than us, is not sure of having a higher productivity to lower wages than us, because we have higher productivity, in this sense, we may have more opportunities to attract investors than Burma.
2. Cambodia is completely peaceful. Now there are no riots and demonstrations because the Royal Government has taken great care to solve and provide a lot of benefits to workers, especially the former CNRP, which is the instigator of lies, innocent workers have disappeared, so now workers and Factory owners as well as investors operate in peace. This case is a good factor that makes more investors come to Cambodia.
3. The Royal Government has promoted trade facilitation by implementing single entry and exit, simplifying and automating customs procedures on both pricing and release of goods, and reducing both formal and informal fees. And adjust institutions at international gateways and international ports to facilitate and expedite exports and imports.
4. On software connectivity, the Royal Government is preparing a master plan for the logistics sector and has increased investment in physical infrastructure by expanding all national roads into four lanes, especially national roads connecting to neighboring countries. Build a deep-sea port up to 14 meters deep and build an expressway from Phnom Penh to the international port. These constructions will be completed soon.
5: Regarding the price of electricity, the Royal Government has decided that the price of electricity will be gradually reduced from 2019 onwards, as well as improve the stability of supply to improve the attractiveness of investment in the manufacturing industry. High added value, industry using modern machinery and integration with local value chains.
6. Cambodia is strategically located in the ASEAN region, which has been becoming the "factory of Asia" and on the other hand, Cambodia is in the middle of the Mekong region, the region with the highest economic growth and connectivity. .
7. Cambodia has opened its economy to all investors without discrimination between Cambodian and foreign investors.
8. Cambodian-made goods are not only supplied for the Cambodian market of more than 15 million people, but can also be supplied to the Mekong Sub-region market with about 250 million customers, the ASEAN market with approximately 630 million, and the regional market of the Comprehensive Economic Partnership Agreement, the region with about 3 billion customers, as well as access to other major markets in the world.
In conclusion, if Cambodia does not have preferential tariffs to the European Union, only the export of goods to the European Union, Cambodia is obliged to pay taxes.
At the same time, the Royal Government firmly adheres to the absolute will of the overwhelming majority of the Cambodian people, who have shown responsibility for the fate of the nation itself through universal suffrage. Last July 2018 (83.02% of voters went to the polls). This is a testament to the right decision in response to the independence and sovereignty of a sovereign nation.
We, the Cambodian people, are very proud that the Royal Government has led Cambodia through great difficulties and obstacles from 1979 to the present, under the gentle and firm guide of Samdech Akka Moha Sena Padei Techo Hun Sen, Cambodia has achieved results. Positive is the manifestation of the foundation of unity, solidarity and peace in the direction of independence and sovereignty.
Please be informed that the EBA context process is only in the transition phase of development, although it may have some impact on our Cambodian economy. But we must also remember that "we have our sovereignty, so we need to gather intelligence, gather strength to maintain strong unity."
We believe in the positive and sustainable benefits of another new page in the history of Cambodia and the Royal Government of Cambodia, which has the opportunity to defend its independence, sovereignty and true freedom from interference and disturbance by close friends.
Finally, as a Cambodian citizen who has been victims of foreign interference in Cambodia's internal affairs, I would like to urge you to go abroad if you want to remove the preferential tariff system from Cambodia. War because you all left Cambodia first.
