Ms. Kim Pisey, the mother of the victim girl, described with tears in her eyes that her daughter, Teav Vatey, 11 years old, and her husband, Teav Bora, 33 years old, lived in Thlok village, Chrakmtes commune, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province. In early December 2018, her daughter was bitten by a domestic cat on her left leg and was given an injection by a village doctor, but for a month, her daughter was unable to speak. Strange.
The mother of the girl said that when she returned home, they were not tired at noon and sent her to Calmette Hospital (Pasteur) in Phnom Penh. Her child also told the family to send her back home, because it looks like this girl is very serious, can not be treated because it is the last stage.
Hearing this, the girl's family decided to send her home with despair and pity that no doctor could save her life.
The mother said that they took a taxi to return home while traveling on the road, her child was very distressed, the taxi owner saw the girl's serious condition, he did not dare to take her back home. Near Neak Leung, her family asked the car owner to find a nearby hospital to find an ambulance to take her child home.
After traveling in an ambulance for a while, her son was so distressed that she died in the ambulance at 5:40 pm on February 12, 2019, causing the family to suffer. Very sad and crying over the loss of this lovely daughter.
With the tragic loss of her daughter, Kim Pisey recalled that the cat that had bitten her daughter for two months had been chased away by her husband and never returned home. When she was very sick, her daughter said that she was with her parents and that she was not going anywhere. She had to overcome the cat.
