European Chamber of Commerce issues statement of regret to European Commission for Proceeding to Suspend EBA (Video Inside) (Phnom Penh): The European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia represents more than 350 companies in the country. Issuing a statement expressing regret over the decision of the European Commission announcing the process leading to the possibility of suspending the EBA from Cambodia.
Through a statement obtained by Fresh News on the afternoon of February 14, 2019, the European Chamber of Commerce in Cambodia is committed to continuing its partnership and close relationship with the Royal Government of Cambodia to promote business and development.
The European Chamber of Commerce claims that the launch of an investigation by the European Commission to remove the "All But Arms" (EBA) has had a negative impact on Cambodia's socio-economic development.
Ministry of Social Affairs: Specific data on the number of people with disabilities is very important, especially for children with intellectual disabilities
(Phnom Penh): Secretary of State for the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, Mr. Nhek Vannara, Representative of Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation, stated that because Cambodia is a member of ASEAN, each state must regulate its disability sector. How many people have a disability, what kind of disability, how much disability and how much care do we have for our people with disabilities?
Mr. Nhek Vannara said, "Due to the attention from all national and international stakeholders, in recent years, the disability sector in Cambodia has improved steadily and now stakeholders "Begin to pay more attention, especially to children with intellectual disabilities, which is another significant step forward for the disability sector in Cambodia."
Mr. Nhek Vannara said this on the occasion of chairing a meeting on data collection of children with intellectual disabilities at the Ministry of Social Affairs recently, with representatives from relevant ministries, national and international institutions that have been working in the field. Disabilities in Cambodia participate.
Mr. Yeap Malino, Director of the Disability Welfare Department of the Ministry of Social Affairs, said that the actual data that will come from this technical collection is very important, it will be the basis for policy stakeholders such as education, economy, health. And other support services that are essential for children with intellectual disabilities to improve their living conditions and quality.
Cambodia has a total of more than 500,000 people with all kinds of disabilities, and every year about 28,000 people with disabilities receive free physical rehabilitation services that can meet the needs of the people. There are disabilities in Cambodia in both quantity and quality. CPP Team Distributes Donations to 5 Sick and Poor Families in Sangkat Prek Preah Sdach, Battambang Province
