Prey Veng CamControl Branch Found Nearly 20 Kilos of Expired Goods at Prey Veng Market
(Prey Veng): Camcontrol Branch Officer of Prey Veng Province, led by Mr. Uth Sopheap, Branch Manager, this morning, February 14, 2019, in cooperation with officials of the Department of Commerce, local authorities and the market commission, inspected the goods on display at Prey Veng City Market is located in Village 03, Kampong Leav Commune, Kampong Leav District, Prey Veng Province.
Mr. Uth Sopheap confirmed that during the inspection, the expert officers made a preliminary analysis on 12 products equal to 16 samples, such as: Noodles, dried fish, Samyong, Cabbage, Ginger, Banana tree, Hanlot Svith, Dumplings, Beef Fish, squid, pine, fresh shrimp and Yihi to find banned chemicals that can affect people's health. At the same time, professional officers inspected for non-compliance on the packaging of food products.
As a result, officials did not find the presence of banned chemicals, but found some defective goods beyond the expiration date, such as: 19 glasses of tomato juice equal to 13.3 kg, 6 bottles of sauce equal to 3 kg, canned fish 2 cans equal to 0.5 kg, 1 can of kulen equal to 0.6 kg, 10 packets of dumplings equal to 1.5 kg, a total of 18.9 kg of defective goods confiscated by professional officers.
CamControl officers then instructed the vendors to sign a contract to stop the sale of expired products and to record the confiscation of the goods and destroy them.
