The Ministry of Social Affairs and the National Welfare Council of Bangladesh meet to exchange experiences to promote the development of the social protection system and the welfare of the people in Cambodia
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and the Bangladesh National Welfare Council met for the purpose of exchanging experiences and promoting the development of the social protection system and the welfare of the people in Cambodia.
The meeting was held between Mr. Touch Channy, Director General of the General Department of Technical Affairs, Mr. Vong Soth, Minister of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation and officials of the Ministry of Social Affairs, and Mr. ATM Nashir Mia, Executive Director of the Secretariat of the Welfare Council of Bangladesh. Led a delegation from the National Welfare Council of Bangladesh while visiting the Ministry of Social Affairs on February 14, 2019.
On that occasion, Mr. TOCH Channy stated that the Royal Government has set a long-term vision for the development of the social protection system, which is to build a social protection system that is environmentally effective and financially sustainable as a tool to reduce and prevent Poverty, vulnerability and inequality contribute to the development and protection of human resources and promote national economic growth.
He added that based on this vision, the Royal Government has set out a comprehensive national social protection policy framework 2016-2025, focusing on two pillars: the social assistance system and the social security system.
On behalf of Minister Vong Soth, Mr. Touch Channy stated that in order to contribute to the achievement of the above aspirations and visions, the Ministry of Social Affairs, Veterans and Youth Rehabilitation has prepared a strategic plan 2019-2023 for the development of the social sector, veterans and youth rehabilitation.
He said that the purpose of preparing this document is to determine the strategy of the Ministry to ensure harmonious social welfare, reduce the vulnerability and vulnerability of the people to meet the needs of people at all levels to promote. Livelihoods of the people, especially the poor, vulnerable, the disabled, orphans, minors, victims of drug use, veterans, former civil servants and the elderly.
At the same time, ATM Nashir Mia, Executive Director of the Secretariat of the Welfare Council of Bangladesh, welcomed the current visit to the Ministry of Social Affairs. He said the current visit has further strengthened the ties between the Ministry and the Welfare Council of Bangladesh.
(Phnom Penh): Following the conclusion of the 14th Cambodia-Thailand General Boundary Commission (GBC) Meeting chaired by Co-Chairman Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Cambodia, and General Prawit Vong Sovann, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of Defense. Thailand On the morning of February 14, 2019, the two sides issued a joint statement on border issues between the two countries.
The meeting was held in accordance with the agreement on the establishment of border cooperation between Cambodia and Thailand, with the aim of enhancing cooperation for peace and security in the border areas, as well as further strengthening the relationship between the army and the security forces. Other stakeholders of Cambodia and Thailand.
The meeting stressed the importance of the 14th General Boundary Committee (GBC) meeting, which provided guidance and direction to promote existing good relations and important cooperation between the two armies at all levels. All the better for promoting peace, stability and security along the border. The meeting welcomed the progress of cooperation along the border.
The meeting agreed to urge the two sides to continue their duty to maintain peace and stability along the two countries' borders in accordance with the principles and measures set out in the minutes of the 14th meeting on all aspects.
