(Svay Rieng): A girl who was bitten by a cat for more than three months has lost her life, leaving the cries of her parents and relatives to mourn her body. . The girl died at 6:10 am on February 13, 2019 in Thlok village, Chrakmtes commune, Bavet city, Svay Rieng province, while being sent back to her hometown.
According to the girl's mother, her daughter was seriously ill and was taken to a hospital in Phnom Penh for treatment of rabies, but unfortunately doctors said there was no cure. Home to celebrate tradition. After the doctor told this, suddenly at night, his child lost his life, leaving his parents, making him not tired at all, he should not have died at such a young age.
His daughter has been bitten by a cat since early December 2018, but they were not vaccinated at the Pasteur Hospital, but in the village. With the symptoms getting worse, he was taken to Vietnam, but the Vietnamese doctor also said that it was not possible to come to the hospital in Phnom Penh, but unfortunately could not save his life.
The dead girl was named Teav Vatey, 11 years old, her father was named Teav Bora, 33 years old, a farmer, and his wife was named Kim Pisey, 33 years old.
Regarding the case of a girl who was bitten by a cat, Svay Rieng provincial health officials called on all parents and guardians to be careful with their children because a 10-year-old girl was bitten by a cat and contracted rabies. What are the symptoms of seizures that cause loss of life.
If you are bitten by a dog or cat, please bring the victim to the hospital as soon as possible so that the medical team can get vaccinated against rabies in time. Very cruel.
Trapping fish in the water, dragging human corpses in Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province
(Svay Rieng): A man took a net and dragged a fish into the canal while dragging it. This shocking case happened on the afternoon of February 13, 2019 at a canal in Chambok Kong village, Ta Suos commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province.
Mr. Som Sary, 35 years old, said that at around 1 pm on February 13, he was dragged in a ditch when he was caught with heavy objects and tried to pull him ashore, thinking only of big fish. From the water turned out to be the body of a man, he immediately reported to the police and the police came to search and identified the body as Chhuon Pros, male, 31 years old, living in Naraten village, Chheu Teal commune, Svay Chrum district, Svay Rieng province.
After the forensic examination, the authorities handed over the body to the parents for the traditional ceremony.
