Thai Defense Minister informs Hun Sen that there is no problem on the Cambodian-Thai border
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Prawit Vongsovan, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense of Thailand, informed Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, that there are no problems on the Cambodian-Thai border.
The confirmation of the Minister of Defense of Thailand was made on the occasion that Samdech Techo Hun Sen allowed him to pay a courtesy call on the morning of February 14, 2019 at the Peace Palace.
Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's Assistant, said that during this meeting, Mr. Prawit informed Samdech Techo about his meeting with Samdech Tea Banh, a discussion that focused on border issues, security issues and Other issues. Mr. Prawit concluded that the talks went smoothly and that there were no security or other issues along the border.
At the same time, Mr. Prawit also reported to Samdech Techo Prime Minister about his visit to the Victory Monument, expressing his congratulations that the Samdech's national liberation mission at that time started from 5 to receive. Success. At the same time, it also reflects Cambodia's historical journey to find peace for the whole of Cambodia.
On that occasion, Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked Mr. Prawit and also informed Mr. Prawit that the Victory Monument is a place to keep historical documents of each stage in the process of liberating Cambodia from the Khmer Rouge regime. And in that, it also reflects the characters who participated in the process.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen welcomed the talks between Mr. Prawit and Prince Tea Banh and said that the commission has a very important role to play in promoting peace and stability along the border, which is a factor for the sector. Tourism trade between the two countries. In particular, the relationship between people and people.
