Samdech Techo Hun Sen's urging was made during a working meeting with Ms. Panh Maharani, Minister of Coordination of Human Development and Cultural Affairs of Indonesia, this morning, February 14, at the Peace Palace.
According to Mr. Eang Sophalleth, Samdech Techo's personal assistant, during the meeting, Ms. Panh Moharani informed Samdech Techo of her intention to come to Cambodia. She said she was traveling to Cambodia now to attend the 60th anniversary of diplomatic relations between Cambodia and Indonesia, which were left to future generations by both King Norodom Sihanouk and former President Sukarno.
She was deeply grateful for the generous participation of the Cambodian leadership in the anniversary of the establishment of diplomatic relations. She also informed Samdech Techo that the selection of February 13, 2019 to celebrate the 60th anniversary of the relationship between the two countries because 60 years ago (February 13, 1959), Indonesia and Cambodia has signed a memorandum of understanding.
In response, Samdech Techo thanked her for coming to the event and brought the artists to the event, making the diplomatic relations program between the two countries more solemn and memorable. Samdech Techo also said that the previous generation of leaders left this relationship to the next generation, and after 60 years, Cambodia-Indonesia relations have grown and strengthened steadily.
In addition, Indonesia has played an important role over the past 60 years, both regionally and globally. In particular, for Cambodia, Indonesia has played an important role in contributing to the search for peace for Cambodia by participating as co-chair of the negotiations and in the Paris Agreement.
In addition, Indonesia has contributed to the deployment of peacekeepers in pursuit of peace in Cambodia, as well as expanding cooperation, including training and human resource development.
He said that Cambodia and Indonesia should further strengthen and expand this relationship through economic, trade, investment, tourism and culture. In particular, the exchange of experiences, relations, visits between the people and leaders of the two countries.
