Netanyahu admits Israeli army shelled Syrian territory earlier this week
Earlier this week, the Syrian state news agency SANA reported that Israeli tanks had hit a destroyed hospital and a checkpoint in the southern Syrian province of Quneitra near the border with Israel, but no one was killed. No victims of this attack.
On Tuesday, Netanyahu acknowledged that Israeli military forces (IDF) had shelled Syrian territory. "The Israeli army operates every day, including yesterday, against Iran itself and Tehran's efforts to strengthen its influence in the region," he said.
According to Benjamin Netanyahu, the Israeli military is committed to doing what is necessary as it operates on a regular basis, in line with Israel's assessment and the need to prevent Iran and Tehran from forming an alliance. The base is near the northern border of Israel.
In recent years, Israel has carried out several airstrikes on Syrian territory under the pretext that it was targeting forces as well as Iranian and Hezbollah bases, which Israel considers a threat. Iran is stepping up its influence in the region as Tehran insists it has sent only military advisers to Syria at the request of the Syrian government.
University of Human Resources submitted 11 strategic plans for the implementation of the work direction in 2019
(Phnom Penh): The University of Human Resources organized a meeting to review the work results in 2018 and work direction in 2019 on the morning of February 11, 2019. The ceremony was presided over by Prof. Dr. Seng Phally, Chairman of the Board of the University of Human Resources, along with 270 members of the Conference at the University of Human Resources.
Prof. Dr. Seng Phally said that through the experience of more than 21 years of training, it has been shown that the quality of education and training is based on the ability of ethical leadership, professionalism, teaching and learning skills. And the development of technical work in standardized training.
He also said that the new work direction of the university for 2019, which was raised with clear thinking, strategic and provided solutions to some of the challenges and inactions, as well as provided key recommendations. Such as:
* First, to strengthen the existing quality culture, all stakeholders in the conference must contribute to the belief, participate in values, participate in commitment and take responsibility for creating quality at the University of Human Resources.
* Second: to adopt new cultures and mindsets to develop innovative work attitudes to develop individuals, organizations and universities.
* Third: To strengthen the existing internal quality assurance mechanism to improve the quality of training at all levels.
* Fourth: Strengthen the management, leadership, staff at all levels and professors to work towards the vision, goals and objectives set in the five-year strategic plan.
* Fifth: Develop human resources, leaders, staff at all levels and professors must develop and update their professional skills in all forms, including internal training and attend training courses.
* Sixth: Continue to develop infrastructure and equipment for teaching, learning and research.
* 7th: Continue to strengthen the discipline of study discipline, examination discipline and work discipline, which is the culture of ensuring the quality of education, cultivating the spirit of respecting the law, and respecting professional ethics.
* Eighth: Strengthen research capacity Research is the basis of development in all fields, especially professors need to increase research activities to develop their teaching careers.
* 9th: Strengthen the English language training capacity to increase the capacity and quality of students' research.
* 10th: Increase the activities of discussion forums, increase research capacity and advocacy of students.
* 11th: Increase job search activities for students by promoting training activities, sharing experiences on preparing for work and finding jobs for students widely.
