(Battambang): Food vendors at Thmor Koul Market 47 stalls equal to 113 people were happy after Mr. Nguon Rattanak, Governor of Battambang Province, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, announced that food vendors at Thmor Koul Market for resale More.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen's announcement came after an explosion between Thmar Koul Market, with Heng Chhat, the company's president, seeking to reclaim the food on the market side. This announcement was made on the afternoon of February 12, 2019 at the Thmor Koul District Hall, with the participation of the Deputy Provincial Governor, Thmor Koul District Governor, forces and market traders.
According to Mr. Kim Vannak, Governor of Thmor Koul District, Thmor Koul Market has been open to traders for 11 years, and until February 28, 2018, there was an explosion between the market companies. Mr. Heng Chat, the chairman, told the food vendors on the side of the market to use this land as an apartment for sale.
Mr. Kim Vannak continued that immediately, the traders' complaints were complained to the district administration for help, and the district authorities had resolved them many times, but had not yet received any results, so the Battambang provincial governor visited. Come solve.
Immediately after the complaints between food vendors through the fence outside the market complained to the President of the Market Company several times, the representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, including Mr. Nguon Rattanak, came down to solve and announce to the food vendors All must be sold as original.
Mr. Nguon Rattanak stated that seeing the difficulties of the people, the 113 food vendors at Thmor Koul Market, equal to 47 stalls, also faced difficulties and with the direct guidance and recommendation of Samdech Techo, he came down Resolved immediately and announced the good news of Samdech, which allowed them to resume business from the date of this announcement.
