83-hectare sugarcane plantation in Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province was destroyed by fire, damaging tens of thousands of dollars
(Svay Rieng): At least 83 hectares of sugarcane plantations of two companies in Koki Som commune, Svay Teap district, Svay Rieng province were destroyed by fire almost to ashes. The case of the sugarcane plantation fire occurred on February 12, 2019.
Koy Saren, the owner of the sugarcane plantation, said that before the fire, workers were seen cutting sugarcane and harvesters were also harvesting. Very.
He added that while the fire was burning, workers rushed to the site to get a tractor to plow the sugarcane fields and spray water, but were not successful due to the wind blowing the burning sugarcane leaves in front of the tractor. The fire was so fast that the workers could not run. This incident burned 57 hectares of his plantation and 26 hectares of Sophat Samnang Company.
He added that the fire was extinguished at 2:20 pm the same day and the cause of the fire is not clear whether it was a natural fire or someone stole or burned cigarette butts. Authorities are currently conducting a search.
It should be noted that the sugarcane plantations have been on fire many times until the dry season arrives, which causes the sugarcane growers to lose tens of thousands of dollars.
