Minister of Tourism encourages like-minded projects to promote Cambodia's tourism sector
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Thong Khon, Minister of Tourism, encouraged the youths of the One Mind Project to continue to promote Cambodia's tourism sector as Cambodia has many potential tourist destinations such as cultural tourism and ecotourism. Clean and green.
This encouragement was made on the occasion of the Minister allowing Ms. Nguon Sony, the director of the One Heart Project, to pay a courtesy call at the Ministry of Tourism on February 12, 2019.
Ms. Nguon Sony said that the same project was established in 2016 by the Youth Volunteers of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia in collaboration with UNI and Google Cambodia. In its first year, the same mindset project launched a charity run organized in Koh Pich, with more than 2,000 participants raising funds to help Drama and Children's Kitchen.
She said that after the success of the first program, the same mental project organized another program, "For our society can do", which provides opportunities for high school students to compete in projects that they create. And the program was also a success.
Ms. Nguon Sony stated that the third program "Run for Teachers" to raise funds to help the Khmer Academic Staff Association, which is composed of retired teachers, as well as other teachers who are working in the field of education.
She also said that for the fourth project, "For a society we can do" season 2, which will be held in the future. Therefore, the youth group of the same mind project requested to pay a courtesy call and accept the advice and recommendations of the Minister of Tourism, because all programs organized by the same mind project focus on tourism and receive support and Participate from the Cambodian youth.
Mr. Thong Khon expressed his support for all the ongoing programs of the One Mind Project of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, most of which focused on tourism, and encouraged the One Mind Project Youth Group to continue their work, especially Participate more actively in promoting tourism development.
The Minister said that Cambodia has many tourist sites and is full of potential, especially cultural and nature tourism or ecotourism, which is trying to transform and make those areas a clean and green tourist area.
At the same time, the Minister also introduced the project to pay more attention to smart tourism and smart city, and now in addition to cultural tourism destinations, Cambodia is also trying to promote ecotourism.
He reminded that currently in the world, more than 50% of tourists like cultural tourism sites, while more than 30% prefer eco-tourism or ecotourism, while Cambodia also has great potential for ecotourism.
At the same time, Cambodia is developing many tourist destinations to turn the area into the most important and attractive tourist destinations, such as tourist destinations in the Northeast, Southwest and North of the country, which are all areas with high potential in the field. Tourism.
In this statement, the Ministry of Foreign Affairs stated that the Royal Government of Cambodia strongly regrets the decision of the European Commission on 11 February 2019 to launch a formal procedure for the temporary withdrawal of the preferential tariff system. "All goods except arms (EBA)" from Cambodia.
The European Commission did not consider a constructive partnership between the Royal Government and civil society organizations. In contrast, the European Commission has expressed dishonesty, relying solely on biased systematic criticism organized by a small number of local and international NGOs, and not recognizing the full rights and freedoms of the two associations. 286 3,221 local NGOs and 397 foreign NGOs are implementing and receiving.
The values of the Principles are the basis on which the EU implements its policies under all circumstances, regardless of the terms of its unilateral or bilateral implementation, even in the event that the EU unilaterally provides a preferential framework for Cambodia. Or when the EU signs free trade agreements with other countries.
However, the Royal Government of Cambodia is committed to continuing to work honestly with those countries to promote mutually beneficial cooperation and partnership.
