More South Koreans begin to see North Korea in an unprecedented way
SEOUL: Most schoolchildren in South Korea see North Korea in a more positive light at a time when the situation on the Korean Peninsula is calm. This is according to a survey released on Tuesday, quoted by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on the evening of February 12, 2019.
According to a joint survey by South Korea's Ministry of National Unification and the Ministry of Education released on Tuesday, nearly 51 percent of schoolchildren expressed their view that North Korea is a partner of South Korea. Should cooperate with, as the rate rose from 41.3 percent in the previous survey.
On the other hand, the number of students who consider North Korea as an enemy of South Korea also decreased significantly, to 5.2 percent in 2018 from 41 percent in 2017, while students who understand That North Korea as a country in need of assistance from South Korea increased from 10.8 percent in 2017 to 12.1 percent in 2018.
A more positive image of North Korea has emerged in the face of the escalation of the peaceful atmosphere on the Korean Peninsula, which was created through a series of inter-Korean summits, combined with the first summit in inter-Korean history. North and the United States last year.
