Details are as follows: Wing surprises customers with live radio!
(Phnom Penh): In addition to offering innovative products and services that help improve the daily lives of Cambodians, Wing has brought another surprise and excitement by providing Give your customers lots of rewards through the new radio program "Wing Wins Out".
With five radio programs covering almost everywhere in Cambodia, this new one-hour radio program will provide information on Wing's many promotions. What is even more special and interesting in this program is the episode where the radio host calls 5 Wing customers and surprises them by transferring 100,000 Riels to their Wing account He.
The total prize money that Wing will distribute to customers through this radio program is a total of 500 million Riels. All Wing customers are eligible for this reward by simply topping up their mobile phone through the Wing smartphone app. From Monday to Friday, 25 winning customers (5 of them are Wing agents) will be selected to call them and transfer the prize money immediately to their WING account.
Jojo Malolos, CEO of Wing Specialized Bank, stated that the new radio program aims to create a platform where customers can participate in making suggestions or comments related to Wing services, as well as rewarding customers who have high confidence in our services. Wing to top up their phone for their daily communication.
"We believe this radio program will bring Wing closer to our customers," added Malolos. "Through all these discussions, we hope that our customers will have a better understanding of Wing's products and services, give them any suggestions they would like Wing to make adjustments and participate in fun activities."
The CEO of Wing Specialized Bank stated that the new radio program is expected to make a significant contribution to educating Cambodians on how mobile financial services can improve their daily lives. .
Wing customers can also join the program as some radio broadcasts will be broadcast live on the official Facebook page of Wing Specialized Bank. In addition, there will be several tests related to radio programs on the Facebook page for customers to receive other gifts as well. Close again! Mercedes-Benz and the 4th Secret Treasure Will Go to Koh Kong Tourism Treasure Hunt
(Phnom Penh): The Government of Japan has provided a total grant of US $ 529,069 to a volunteer security organization under a grant scheme for a Japanese NGO project.
The signing ceremony for the grant took place on February 12, 2019 at the Embassy of Japan, in which the Japanese side was represented by Mr. Horino Uchihi Hidehisa, Ambassador of Japan to Cambodia, and the Japanese NGO side was represented by Mr. Tase Takashi, Director of the Volunteer Organization for Human Resource-Based Kindergarten Project, focuses on libraries in Battambang.
On this occasion, Mr. Horinouchi Hidehisa said that the Japanese government provides a lot of money to the peacekeeping organization. The organization will establish a model kindergarten equipped with a library to promote reading in early childhood education and increase the capacity of kindergarten teachers in Battambang to improve the quality of early childhood education and better development for young children.
At the same time, through this project, it is hoped that the activities of the library will grow throughout the province and young children in Battambang will develop more.
In this project, the volunteer organization aims to improve the quality of early childhood education by establishing a model kindergarten equipped with a library and increasing the capacity of kindergarten teachers and librarians in Battambang city.
Through this project, in particular, about 450 children at the Battambang Resource Kindergarten will be able to get a better environment for early childhood education, and about 10,000 children in Battambang are expected to receive an education. Better yet.
