By: Chao Chak Smok, Kamchay Mear District, On February 12, 2019, the Ministry of Public Works issued a directive to promote traffic safety.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works and Transport (MPWT) has issued a guideline to promote traffic safety education to civil servants and employees of the General Department of Public Enterprises, Departments and Units under this Ministry. This is according to the instructions received by Fresh News on the afternoon of February 12, 2019.
The Ministry of Public Works issued the instruction based on the situation of traffic accidents that continue to occur, causing deaths and injuries, disabilities, damage to public and private property on a daily basis.
The Ministry would like to recommend to all General Departments of Public Enterprises, Departments and Units as follows:
* Organize separate programs to educate and disseminate the contents of the road traffic law and related standards at least quarterly to raise awareness and ensure traffic safety.
* Regularly report on educational activities, disseminate or include in the unit's monthly work report to the National Road Safety Committee through the General Secretariat of the NCC, located at the Ministry of Public Works and Transport. .
