The draft law on the right to information, 9 chapters and 38 articles has been drafted and is scheduled to be sent to the National Assembly soon.
(Phnom Penh): The draft law on the right to information has been finalized by the Ministry of Information, which has 9 chapters and 38 articles and is designed to ensure the public's right to freedom of information. This is according to the announcement of the Ministry of Information, which was received by Fresh News on February 12, 2019.
The letter from the Ministry of Information is in response to the 19 civil society organizations that wrote a letter to the Ministry of Information on January 30, 2019, expressing support for the Ministry of Information in leading the process of reviewing the draft law. On the right to information and inclusion in the five-year strategic plan (2019-2023).
According to the Ministry of Information, the Ministry of Information has included the draft law on access to information in the program requirements of the draft law and legal documents for the Royal Government of the 6th legislature of the National Assembly for 5 years (2018- 2023) is ready, including the draft law on audio-visual, the amendment of the law on the media and the draft sub-decree on advertising management.
According to the announcement of the Ministry of Information, on behalf of the Ministry of Information as well as the Royal Government is willing to expedite and promote the review of the draft law on the right to information with other relevant ministries and institutions and believe that this draft law will be Sent for approval from the legislature in the near future.
