Preah Vihear and achievements at Wat Chamnom in Takeo province worth more than 200,000 USD inaugurated, General Hing Bun Heang tells people to join Samdech Techo against illegal overthrow
(Takeo): The temples and achievements of Wat Chamnom in Kampeng commune, Prey Kabbas district, Takeo province were inaugurated on February 12, 2019 under the presidency of Honorary General Dr. Hing Bun Heang. Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, representing Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Kittiprittbandit.
Wat Chamnom was built on a hill in the east of Chhum village, Chamnom village, Kampeng commune, Prey Kabas district, and began to be built during the reign of King Utay, called Preah Ang Chantna in 1801 AD. This pagoda was devastated and was a killing field during the Democratic Kampuchea era. After the liberation on January 7, 1979, the government and the people jointly rebuilt it into a place of worship for Buddhism.
General Hing Bun Heang confirmed that "this is another new achievement that comes from the value of the shadow of peace, the politics of victory under the wise leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia."
The General emphasized that due to the victorious policy of Samdech Techo, the country was peaceful and developed in all fields to this day, both in the field of Buddhism and empire.
Dr. also instructed the civil servants of the Armed Forces as well as the people of Prey Kabbas district, Takeo province to continue to strictly implement the recommendations of Samdech Techo Hun Sen to serve the people and maintain social stability, achieve peace and stability in Cambodia and Absolutely oppose any attempt to undermine the security of the people and peace in Cambodia.
