Meanwhile, Mr. So Sokhon, Director of Pailin Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, said that the systematic land registration procedure has five stages:
* First, the preparation is to determine the judicial area, the establishment of the administrative committee, the notification of the meeting, the dissemination and the process of disseminating the land registration system in a systematic manner.
* Second: Technical operations are demarcation, measurement and judgment to build cadastral plans and list of landowners.
* Third: Publicly post the judgment documents (cadastral plan and list of landowners) for 15 days to allow the landowners and stakeholders to verify their names, family status and plots and to protest in The case is wrong.
* Fourth: Pepper on the judicial documents, report on the results of the public posting of the judicial documents of the Administrative Commission to the provincial governor to review and decide on the granting of rights to any plot that is not in dispute or related. State land.
