Minister of Information Visits Patients and Examines the Work of Volunteer Doctors from the United States at the Baray-Santuk District Referral Hospital in Kampong Thom Province
(Kampong Thom): Mr. Khieu Kanharith, Minister of Information and his team visited patients and examined the work of a group of volunteer doctors of the Cambodian Health Association in the United States, who came to help examine and treat people at Baray District Referral Hospital. Santuk, Kampong Thom province, on the afternoon of February 11, 2019.
According to the chairman of the working group of the Cambodian Health Association in the United States, as of 2019, this is the ninth year that the volunteer team of the association has visited and treated the people of Cambodia on a mobile basis. In different capitals and provinces, about 4-5 thousand Cambodians are examined and treated each year. Therefore, in all 9 years, a total of more than 40,000 Cambodians were examined and treated.
The 9th Medical Examination was held at Baray-Santuk District Referral Hospital, Kampong Thom Province from 11 to 16 February 2019, with a total of 35 volunteer doctors from the United States, including doctors. More than 90 Cambodian volunteers have also joined the team of doctors at Baray-Santuk District Referral Hospital.
The Minister also thanked the volunteer doctors who donated personal funds to help people in Kampong Thom, as well as people across Cambodia.
Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia Leads Artists to Perform 5 Performances at the 2019 "Qingge" Multi-Ethnic Parade in Singapore
The "Qinghai" Parade is one of the largest performing arts parades in Asia, organized annually by the People's Association of the Republic of Singapore. The program was initiated by former Prime Minister Lee Kuan Yew with the aim of showcasing the magnificence, beauty and diversity of multiculturalism.
The march was performed by about 150 national art groups and brought together a total of nearly 10,000 artists from around the world to showcase the cultural art of their respective nations.
Speaking to the media this morning, February 12, 2019, Mr. Sok Sabayna, Permanent Member of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, said that the artists who went out to perform these five forms led by Mr. Hun Many, President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia and There is coordination from other relevant institutions as well.
