Chronic dispute between traders and investors in Prey Sandek market in Takeo province is resolved under a win-win policy
(Takeo): Finally! The long-running dispute between the old traders of Prey Sandek Market in Traing District and the market investors has been completely closed under the mediation of Mr. Ouch Phea, Governor of Takeo Province on the morning of February 11, 2019.
During the visit to Prey Sandek Market between the old traders and investors, the Governor of Takeo Province, together with the relevant departments and units, spent about 2 hours to coordinate a fruitful settlement.
The settlement was accepted by both parties, with more than 30 traders who did not yet have stalls, they were able to get their stalls back to normal and the remaining minor issues will be resolved later.
Mr. Ouch Phea said that this successful solution is in line with the win-win strategy of the head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, that is, this solution is successful for all business people and market investors. Ministry of Industry and GIZ sign and announce the opening of "Small and Medium Enterprise Development"
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Industry and Handicrafts and GIZ, supported by the German government, this morning, February 11, 2019, signed and officially announced the development of micro and small and medium enterprises in Cambodia.
On that occasion, Mr. Son Seng Huot said that the signing ceremony and opening ceremony of the SME Development Program is one of the most important platforms to provide information updates as well as new policies that are the basis for Continue to work to encourage the micro and small enterprise sector in Cambodia.
He added that the forum also heard about the results of the SME development program in Cambodia, as well as providing input from all stakeholders, especially GIZ, about the challenges of small and medium enterprises in Cambodia to As a basis for setting new indicators in order to facilitate micro, small and medium enterprises to be able to develop, improve their production lines and expand their business.
A senior official of the Ministry of Industry stated that in addition to receiving incentives for small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) in the field of taxation and financing, the Ministry is also involved in addressing and finding other solutions to challenges related to Other areas such as product quality issues, standards, human resource training and so on.
In addition, Mr. Son Seng Huot suggested that micro and small enterprises themselves should make efforts to strengthen and further develop themselves, as well as try to find modern technology and machinery in production to increase productivity and win competition. Body in domestic and foreign markets.
Lam Kim Leng, Director General of Small and Medium Enterprises and Handicrafts, also thanked the German government and people for devoting resources to the development of this project to help develop micro and small and medium enterprises in Cambodia. He said that this project focuses on strengthening the management capacity of good production techniques, good hygiene to increase productivity, efficiency in the production chain.
Separately, Mr. Chhea Lay Hy, Director of the Department of Small and Medium Enterprises and Project Director, is committed to continue working with GIZ to develop a detailed action plan in order to achieve the plan of this project to be more successful.
