Paragon Brings Technology and Partnership with Canadian Polytechnic Institute
Paragon Educational Institution is committed to keeping young Cambodians moving forward in technology through a partnership with Canada's leading polytechnic institute. SAIT is a Canadian Polytechnic Institute that trains its students to acquire knowledge, skills and abilities in line with the needs of today's technology world.
The institute was established in 1916 and offers more than 100 programs offering high-quality diplomas and certifications. The institute helps students prepare for careers in related fields, especially technical jobs, while Canada is recognized as one of the world's leading countries in the field of technological innovation.
A cocktail party to celebrate the signing of a memorandum of understanding between the two educational institutions took place at Paragon International University in Toul Kork district, Phnom Penh on February 10.
Computer science and information technology, along with engineering and business management, are at the core of Paragon University education, while students from all Paragon International School campuses are introduced to the basics. Come on.
The new partnership with the Canadian institution will expand the scope and increase opportunities for students as well as provide them with better knowledge in areas that are shaping the future of the world.
