(Kampong Speu): Mr. HUN Many, Member of Parliament for Kampong Speu Constituency and President of the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia, this morning, February 11, 2019, attended the award ceremony of the Under-18 Youth Football Tournament in Kampong Speu. .
The tournament is part of the Kampong Speu Provincial Football Development Program, a two-year initiative of NagaWorld with a generous heart in collaboration with the Football Federation of Cambodia, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports and the Union of Youth Federations of Cambodia to help train players. The next generation of football players in the community.
In November last year, 120 coaches from 94 secondary and high schools in Kampong Speu province received professional football training provided by NagaWorld Football Club, the 2018 Metfone Cambodian League champions.
After two months of training, a total of 28 teams (19 boys and 9 girls) participated in the U18 mini-football tournament held at the venue of Kampong Speu Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports. From January 28 to 31, 2019.
On that occasion, Mr. Hun Many said that the government is committed to developing athletes and raising the standard of sports coaching in schools, which will be able to produce outstanding players for local clubs as well as national teams.
Separately, the Governor of Kampong Speu said, "We are pleased that NagaWorld and related agencies organized this good program in our province, which will benefit about 18,500 students aged 14 to 18 years."
Please note that in order to support the development of football in Cambodia, NagaWorld has long cooperated with the National Olympic Committee of Cambodia and will continue to reward Cambodian athletes who have won major international sports events such as continental sports. Asia and Southeast Asian sports.
