(Sihanoukville): A dump truck collided with a train traveling from Sihanoukville in Phnom Penh, causing the locomotive to fall off the tracks and the vehicle to be severely damaged.
The accident between the car and the train happened on the morning of February 11, 2019 in Prek Tol village, Teuk Thla commune, Prey Nob district, Sihanoukville province. This is according to Mr. Hou Yay, Prey Nup District Police Inspector.
Prey Nup District Inspector confirmed that the accident did not cause any casualties, but the train and the car fell on both the railway and the rubber road, and also suffered serious damage, respectively. .
After the incident, the competent experts went down to the scene to deal with the procedure later.
At the same time, the Prey Nup District Police Inspector also called on drivers or road users to be careful at the point where the railway crosses National Road 3 and National Road 4 in Sihanoukville, as it often causes traffic accidents. He also reminded drivers of all types of vehicles to respect all road traffic laws, no matter how close or far the distance, in order to contribute to reducing the rate of traffic accidents.
