Phnom Penh Capital Administration Builds an Groundwater Reservoir to Divert Wastewater from Tonle Bassac Toch to Boeung Choeung Ek Wastewater Treatment Plant
(Phnom Penh): The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has issued a notification on the implementation of the project to build an underground water reservoir, a pumping station and dig a drainage system to divert wastewater from Tonle Bassac Toch to Boeung Choeung Ek wastewater treatment station. This is according to the announcement of Phnom Penh Capital Administration, which was received by Fresh News on February 10, 2019.
The Phnom Penh Capital Administration has confirmed that the implementation of the above project starts from February 2019 and is scheduled to end by the end of November 2020, including:
1. Dig a sewer system to divert dirty water from the small Bassac River with a diameter of 1.2 meters and 1.5 meters, a length of 2,660 meters along Sabit Blvd., Samdech Sothearos Blvd. and Mao Tse Toung Blvd in Tonle Bassac Sangkat and Sangkat Boeung Keng Kang I, Khan Chamkar Morn.
2: Construction of an underground water reservoir with a capacity of 3,000 cubic meters and a pumping station with a pumping capacity of 4.5 cubic meters per second at the Neak Phlos Bridge Park in Chaktomuk Sangkat, Daun Penh District.
3: Construction of a 100 cubic meter underground water reservoir and equipped with an automatic motor with a pumping capacity of 500 cubic meters / hour at the corner of the east fence of the Russian Embassy in Tonle Bassac, Chamkarmon district.
To start the implementation of this project, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration will open a test excavation site to find the underground network at some points on Seth Blvd., Samdech Sothearos Blvd. and Mao Tse Tung Blvd. to avoid maximum impact.
