(Phnom Penh): Pharmacist Ang Hok Srun, Director of the Food Safety Bureau, Department of Food, Drug, Medical Equipment and Cosmetics of the Ministry of Health, said that in 2018, there were 13 cases of food poisoning in Cambodia, 203 patients were hospitalized, 196 people were hospitalized and 12 died. People.
On that occasion, pharmacists called on people to follow five tips for food safety, including: 1: Keep clean (wash hands with soap before cooking and after defecation, stove, dishwasher, dishes clean and dry , Protect the kitchen and food from animals such as rats, cockroaches, flies and other insects)
2: Store raw and cooked food separately.
3: Cook food well
4: Store food at a safe temperature (Store cooked food at room temperature for no more than two hours, put perishable or perishable food and cooked food in the refrigerator or freezer immediately at low temperature. Above five degrees Celsius, keep cooked food hot at temperatures above 60 degrees Celsius, do not store food for too long, even in the refrigerator)
At the same time, he called on national and international guests to check the A, B, C signs or hygiene certificates from the Ministry of Health given to restaurants that have been trained and implemented in accordance with the regulations of the Ministry to provide Food safety for Cambodians and for international guests.
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Foreign Affairs and International Cooperation on February 9, 2019 issued a statement strongly condemning the actions of Sam Rainsy, who called for the army not to obey orders and for the uprising and Poisonous statement of this person.
