This week, Fresh News Legal Awareness Program, in collaboration with the Cambodian Lawyers for International Cooperation, would like to share the following topics on "Fraud of Public Documents" with citizens and students:
Forgery of public documents is a criminal offense under Article 629 of the Penal Code, defined as "fraud committed in authenticity or forgery in documents issued by a public official to work. "Note the right to identity or status or to agree to grant permission is punishable by imprisonment from 5 (five) to 10 (ten) years."
In short, forgery of public documents is illegal and seriously harms Cambodian society, and those who falsify public documents will be punished according to Article 629 of the Penal Code of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
