Russia plans to send people to the moon in 2031 to research and build the first base
While China and the United States are most active in exploring the moon, Russia also has plans, but it is not until 2031 that Russia can send astronauts to orbit the moon and work. Scientific research. This is according to the press release from Sputnik on Saturday evening, February 9, 2019.
The mission, led by Russia's Central Institute of Machinery Production and Research TsNIIMash, said: "The purpose of the mission is to bring humans to the moon, which will begin in 2031, and all astronauts will be trained to perform related missions. What they have to do on the moon ... ".
Russia plans to send people to the moon in 2031 and again in 2032 to test vehicles equipped there. Then, in 2033, astronauts will travel to the moon for a long time to conduct research and test research robots on it. The construction of the first Russian base on the moon will begin in 2034 until 2035.
