Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, February 08: 817 Illegal Vehicles Found and 423 Fineed
(Phnom Penh): The nationwide traffic law enforcement campaign for February 08, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 5,333 vehicles, found 817 vehicles violated the law (78% motorcycles), 394 education vehicles and 423 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 2,898 helmets and goggles were inspected on February 8, 286 education helmets and 349 helmets were fined.
For the results of the eight-day inspection from February 1 to 8, 2019, the police force inspected 33,439 vehicles and found 5,014 vehicles, including 2,090 education vehicles and parks. 2,924 units were fined. Slogan "Preventing Genocide" and Memorial Garden at Mesang High School, Prey Veng Province Inaugurated
The inauguration ceremony, held on February 6, 2019, also distributed 1,500 books on the history of Democratic Kampuchea, genocide and Cham identity from the Khmer Rouge regime to the Hambali incident to students and participants. .
Both slogans are entitled "Learning the history of Democratic Kampuchea is learning to prevent genocide" and "Speaking of living during the Khmer Rouge era is about reconciliation, educating children to be tolerant". Exhibit a photo gallery of research data and a brief history of the top leaders of the Khmer Rouge regime in the newly built park.
The construction of this park and the display of these posters to show to the public is to honor and dedicate to the souls of the victims who died and were buried on the campus of Mesang High School, where the staff of the Documentation Center came to do research. Since 1997.
In 2018, the Documentation Center of Cambodia, in collaboration with the US company Sparrow Hawks, updated the existing data and conducted scientific research on the graves at Mesang High School using the RD 1500, which can not only measure The depth, height, length and width of each pit, but can also show the bones of victims buried in the pit during the Khmer Rouge era.
Preliminary information obtained from the inspection of the RD1500 engine showed that there were indeed corpses in the pit depth of one and a half to eight meters. The new park is named "Memorial Garden or Garden of Remembrance".
Ms. Tun Saim, Undersecretary of State at the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports, said that the gardening and construction of the slogan on the grave was to preserve the historical site and to serve the memory of the younger generation. In addition, she also praised Mesang High School for its well-disciplined and warm-hearted students.
"The younger generation must work hard to learn and understand history clearly," she added. Speaking of genocide is for tolerance, reconciliation and tolerance. We need to develop our country to grow together with rich human resources with the Royal Government, because the next day you will become a leader, do not lead the country to destruction like the Khmer Rouge.
Mr. Chhun Sophal, Director of Prey Veng Provincial Department of Education, Youth and Sports, emphasized the importance of preventing the recurrence of the genocidal regime. He also praised the academic results and the number of outstanding national students that Mesang High School has achieved so far.
"These slogans and research findings are a living document, especially for students, as well as teachers, to remind the memory of the past for the common good of the future. Let the genocidal regime be born in Cambodia again. ”
Rith Sereymak, a 12th grader, said: "Applying a slogan at a school like this makes the next generation of students like me aware of what has happened at this location. This evidence will make the next generation of children aware that this is a place with many bones and corpses and can even show me and other students more convincingly the story of the massacre during the Khmer Rouge regime. When the past really happened. ”
"The slogans, along with data on the bodies of victims of the Khmer Rouge era, give us insight into the atrocities of the time, and we need to learn about the different causes of the regime to prevent it," Han Sokun said. Born again. So we have to learn clearly and remember together.
It should be recalled that the Khmer Rouge regime, officially known as the Democratic Kampuchea regime led by Pol Pot, between April 17, 1975 and January 7, 1979, caused an estimated 2 million deaths due to Overwork, killing and starvation. The Khmer Rouge transformed schools and pagodas into security departments, cattle barns, handicrafts, rice barns, and slaughterhouses.
Comment: Political clown Sam Rainsy performed this story ... completely crazy
Falling into a state of loss of control and despair, Sam Rainsy dared to do anything. But doing this not only shows that Sam Rainsy is going crazy, but it goes hundreds of times crazy. What is the weight? What is the evidence? What is the argument? And how much hope is there to dare to fake documents and post slanders in an attempt to divide the CPP.
