Ministry of Education launches measures to prevent irregular activities on Valentine's Day (February 14) in public and private schools
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports has issued a guideline setting out measures to prevent irregular activities on Valentine's Day in public and private educational institutions.
The Ministry states that this day is not a traditional festival of our Cambodian people, and in recent years, Valentine's Day has become more and more influential, making young people forget their studies, lose their dignity and family. Leaving the beautiful culture and national traditions of Cambodia.
To strengthen the implementation of internal regulations for public institutions, the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports would like to introduce the following measures to prevent irregular activities on Valentine's Day in public and private schools:
1. Disseminate to students by all means, such as through meetings when saluting the flag, so as not to misunderstand the meaning of Valentine's Day.
2. To strictly enforce the internal regulations of public educational institutions, especially on the management of ethics and discipline by monitoring the absence of students on a regular basis.
3: To promote the process of the Youth Council, the Children's Council of the school by implementing the activities of "peer educator".
4. To have close contact with parents, guardians, students of the community to provide and receive information related to irregular activities committed by students in order to cooperate in educating and guiding students in a timely manner.
