(Kampong Thom): In the next two weeks, people living in Stong district, Kampong Thom province, especially those who used to rely on the use of Stung Stong water, may face a shortage of water for daily consumption due to the current situation of Stung Stong broken. Already gone. This was confirmed by a senior official of the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology told Fresh News on the afternoon of February 8, 2019.
In order to solve this natural disaster for the people in the area, the Minister of Water Resources and Meteorology, Mr. Lim Kean Hor, this afternoon, accompanied by Secretary of State Bun Hean, who is in charge of monitoring water issues in Kampong Thom and Siem Reap, and his colleagues. Some technicians have been inspecting for practical and long-term measures.
A senior official of the Ministry of Water Resources stated, "What is a concern in the next two weeks, as the current situation in Stung Stoung has already broken into pieces, is the need for water for daily consumption of the people can really There is a problem. In this situation, the Minister has decided to use some of the excavators already located in the Kampong Thom diocese to build wells along the Stung Stong.
As a matter of fact, to this day, the Department of Water Resources and Meteorology of Kampong Thom Province has completed the implementation of dry season rice cultivation after the intervention measures to remove water from the reservoir on September 30 and continue pumping rice to the rice fields, which is currently waiting for Harvest only. The next step is to build a dam at Msar Krang commune and a water distribution bridge nearby.
The Royal Government has called on the authorities and the people to take measures to conserve water for use. This is according to the circular on water conservation measures against drought, released on January 17, 2019. Tourists visit Preah Vihear Province decreased by 14% due to weather factors during Chinese New Year
