Murder of Journalist in Snuol District, Kratie Province
(Kratie): A suspect was arrested by Kratie Provincial Police under the direct command of the Provincial Police Commissioner, Major General Lon Sophat, and was arrested in connection with the murder of a journalist on the night of February 3, 2019 in Kratie Province. Road junction 88, 2 Thnou commune, Snoul district, Kratie province. The suspect was arrested on February 7, 2019 at Cheung Khle village, 2 Thnou commune, Snoul district, Kratie province.
* First: Lim Sok Kong, 21 years old, living in Dangkor village, Treak commune, Memot district, Tbong Khmum province, escaped * Third: Ratha, about 17 years old.
The suspect replied that before the incident, he was riding a motorcycle, three people together to ambush the victim. At that time, Rith Seiha and Lim Sok Kong threw stones at the victim, causing him to fall off the motorcycle.
After the operation, he contacted Ratha, about 17 years old, and a taxi driver named Rith Seiha, while he was riding a motorbike with Lim Sok Kong when he returned home only to find out that the victim, Sorn Sithy, was dead. According to police, the killing of the victim may have been motivated by resentment.
Please be informed that at 22: 3 pm on February 3, 2019, the victim, Sorn Sithy, living in Kbal Snuol village, Snuol commune, Snuol district, Kratie province, working as a journalist working in the Battambang Post unit, was stopped by the suspect. Thrown at the intersection of 88 Road, Cheung Khle Village, 2 Thnou Commune, Snoul District, causing a motorcycle to fall and die at the scene.
