APSARA Authority is pumping water into Angkor Wat temple pond
(Siem Reap): The pond at Angkor Wat is an important part for tourists who like to capture the top of Angkor Wat with water. The scorching heat of the dry season caused the water in the pond to recede rapidly and partially lose its beauty. To solve the above problem in time, APSARA Authority has been pumping water into this pond.
Deputy Director of the Water Management Department of the APSARA Authority, Mr. Phoeun Sokhim, said that the team of the Department of Water Management is pumping water from the Angkor Wat temple into the South Pond or Srah Pros, which began on February 3. At present, the water supply has reached about 30%, equivalent to 1,500 cubic meters.
According to Mr. Phoeun Sokhim, the pond of Angkor Wat is 50x80 meters and can hold 5,000 cubic meters of water, and this work will take another week to add enough water.
According to Mr. Phoeun Sokhim, the water supply is only for Pras Pros, while the North Pond or Srah Srey, which is also a tourist attraction, was not included by the APSARA Authority, leaving the Department of Temple Conservation in the park And preventive archeology from further excavations in the restoration project of this pond structure.
It should be noted that the pond of Angkor Wat is an important part that tourists visit with the top image of Angkor Wat reflected in the water. Tourists visit these places every sunrise and sunset. Fire engulfs 4 houses in Memot district, Tbong Khmum province on Chinese New Year
