(Preah Vihear): Mr. Un Chanda, Governor of Preah Vihear Province, this morning, February 6, 2019, chaired a meeting to resolve the land issue of the Agriculture-Industry Friendship Company, which was occupied by villagers. The ceremony was attended by the Deputy Governor, the Prosecutor of the Provincial Court, relevant departments, units, representatives of Adhoc.
During the ceremony, Mr. Un Chanda, Provincial Governor, introduced 5 tips that will be followed. The five tasks include:
1. The provincial administration will establish a working group to resolve land disputes between agri-industrial friendship companies and the people in the area.
2. The land registration team must urgently study to determine and demarcate the border and identify the people there clearly.
3. The company must continue to cooperate with the provincial and district authorities, especially the dispute resolution team and the land registration team, which will visit the actual location soon.
4. Request the district, commune, and village authorities to instruct all the people who have been abducted to maintain their original status to avoid harassment and other activities, obstacles for the provincial working group to solve in the near future.
5: Request the Provincial Court to stop issuing arrest warrants to other people who illegally encroach on the company's land to wait for the provincial working group to resolve first.
It should be noted that Metro-Industrial Friendship Company received Sub-Decree No. 92 dated June 12, 2012 to develop 8,520 hectares of rubber plantations, agro-industrial crops and animal husbandry covering Choam Ksan and Kulen districts. About 559 families, including 339 families from other provinces.
