Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign, February 05: 284 illegal vehicles found and 182 fines
(Phnom Penh): Nationwide Traffic Law Enforcement Campaign For February 05, 2019, the traffic police force inspected 1,412 vehicles and found 284 vehicles violating the law (36% motorcycles), 102 education vehicles and 182 fines. This is according to the official report of the Traffic Police and Public Order Department of the General Commission of the National Police.
According to the report, 563 helmets and goggles were inspected on February 5, 68 education helmets and 99 helmets were fined.
For the results of the five-day inspection from February 1 to 5, 2019, the police force inspected 18,739 vehicles and found 2,812 offending vehicles, including 1048 education vehicles and 1 fine. , 764 units. Locals in the land of Angkor organize the festival of ascension or ascension by catching fish in the lake, a tradition from the ancestors
(Siem Reap): Angkor Resort is a living heritage site rich in intangible heritage and has been consistently operated by Angkor residents to this day.
The Ascension Ceremony is also one of the many intangible heritage practices practiced by the people of Angkor.
In fact, on the morning of the 5th, which is the 1st day of the month of Meak, the villagers in Bangkong village organized a fish-finding ceremony in the conservation lake to prepare to ascend to Meak or Neak Ta, as every year. The ceremony takes place in a lake that the villagers have always preserved, not allowed to fish freely from June to save the fish for the celebration of ascension or ascension.
Bangkong village chief Pich Khin said that the fishing ceremony is held once a year, once a month, after the approval of the village elders, and announced a fishing day to take the fish to make water, noodles and food together. Ascension ceremony or ascension according to tradition.
He said that in the whole lake, there are two places where the fish caught in the area can be used for family cooking, while the fish caught in the pond are kept together to make noodles.
Mr. Pich Khin stated that after the fishing announcement, the villagers had prepared traditional fishing gear with nets to wait for the crowd at the lake, and some people came from 12 o'clock at night, some got up from 3 o'clock at 4 o'clock. Yes.
This year, the fishing program begins at 7 a.m., with the committee announcing the microphone and shooting the arrow. He added that all the villagers who come to fish not only focus on fishing, but also to have fun and have a closer solidarity between the villagers.
Ms. Bang Tet, a villager in Bang Kong, said that her family, like other people, came to fish and used some of the fish they found to make noodles to prepare for the sky or the sky, and some for cooking.
