(Phnom Penh): A man who was driving a PassApp tricycle was arrested by the police force of the Ministry of Interior in connection with the case of leaking nude photos and threatening to kill a woman. This is according to the report of the Department of Technology Crimes of the Ministry of Interior, which was presented on February 5, 2019.
According to the report, under the direction of the plaintiff and in cooperation with Mr. Riel Sophin, Deputy Prosecutor of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court, the Department of Technology Crimes arrested a 29-year-old suspect, PassApp tricycle rider, on the 30th. January 2019 Related to the threat to kill a woman after dating her failed.
According to the victim, she knew the suspect by calling PassApp frequently and was comforted by the suspect in order to have sex with him and steal nude photos. The suspect then contacted the victim to have sex again, but the victim refused. The suspect then sent a nude photo to a friend and threatened to kill him if he met again.
The suspect is currently being held in legal custody on charges of threatening to kill and threatening to defame.
The Department of Technology Crime Prevention calls for and considers it a message to educate all to know that this is a technological age that requires us to be highly considerate, do not believe in the comfort of some crooks who may cause us to suffer Accidents in the future.
