The report of the Kandal Provincial Gendarmerie confirmed that on February 2, 2019, the Khsach Kandal District Gendarmerie and provincial experts, led by Lieutenant Colonel Pin Chantara, Deputy Commander, received drug work with the permission of Mr. Leav Sreng. Prosecutors from Kandal Provincial Court cracked down on drug trafficking cases in Prey Thom village, Sanlong commune, Khsach Kandal district.
During this operation, the specialized force arrested 2 suspects: 1: Neng Phanit, 18 years old, false occupation, residing in Prey Thom Keut village, Sanlong commune, Khsach Kandal district, and 2: Mak Sovanrath, 37 years old, false occupation. Address: Vihear Sour Tbong Village, Vihear Sour Commune, Khsach Kandal District. The seized items include 66 packs of drugs (ice cubes), 2 mobile phones, 3 motorbikes, 4 metal swords, packaging materials and some other items.
Separately, on January 26, 2019, the Khsach Kandal District Gendarmerie and provincial experts, led by Mr. Vato Pin Chantara, cracked down on drug trafficking cases in Anlong Village, Prek Ta Mak Commune, Khsach Kandal District. Detained a suspect named Heng Dina, 36 years old, tuk tuk driver, living in a rented house in Russey Village, Sangkat Stung Meanchey, Khan Meanchey. The seized items include 46 packs of drugs (ice cubes) and a mobile phone.
On January 28, 2019, the Takhmao Provincial and Municipal Gendarmerie, led by Lieutenant Colonel Pin Chandara, Deputy Commander of the Narcotics Task Force, under the coordination of the Prosecutor, arrived at the scene around Krapeu Ha Village, Takhmao Commune. Takhmao also found Chheng Sothy running a tricycle with suspicion, called for questioning and searched and found a large package of drugs (ice cubes) weighing about 1,200 dollars.
Currently, the specialized military force has built a case to be sent to proceed with the procedure and search to arrest the fugitive mastermind.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen Calls on Compatriots to Support and Participate in the Cambodian General Census Starting March 3-13
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, has issued a message calling on his compatriots to support and participate in the Cambodian census, which will start from March 3 to 13, 2019. Adequate, accurate and honest information from the interview questions to the census officer.
The message received by Fresh News on February 5, 2019, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that the census will allow us to get real demographic data of the country and help the government to prepare. Properly formulate policies and implement programs to achieve a balanced development for people across the country.
According to Samdech Techo Prime Minister, the census is the only source that can provide complete data on the population and characteristics of the population in the country. The census is conducted nationwide, providing information on the local population to the lowest levels, which is an irreplaceable need for data sources.
He stressed that the census data will provide indicators to monitor the implementation of the National Strategic Development Plan and the Sustainable Development Goals of the 2016-2030 Agenda without leaving anyone behind.
Please be informed that the General Census of Cambodia, which will start from March 3 to 13, 2019, is the first census using the national budget after Cambodia became a low middle income country. This is the third census of Cambodia after the second census in 2008, only eleven years in accordance with the Law on Statistics, which defines the obligations of each citizen to participate in the census.
