Royal Government Decides to Divide Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary Management Area in Mondulkiri Province into 4 Areas
(Phnom Penh): The Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to divide the management area of Sre Pok Wildlife Sanctuary into 4 areas: core area, conservation area, sustainable use area and community area to serve the management, conservation, conservation and sustainable socio-economic development. Srek Pok Wildlife Sanctuary Management Area is geographically located in Mondulkiri Province with a total area of nearly 400,000 hectares.
He said that after the division of the management area, the Ministry of Environment believes that it will make the protection and conservation of natural resources in the area more effective and will greatly reduce natural resource crime and illegal wildlife hunting by the group. Corrupt people.
1: There are 2 core areas with a total area of 187,631 hectares, including the first core area, located in Or Buon Leu commune, Nang Khilek commune, Sre Huy commune, Sre Sangkom commune, Koh Nhek district, and in Krang Te commune, Pu Chrey district. Pichreda and the second core area are geographically located in Soksan and Pou Chrey communes and are covered by dense forest, semi-dense forest, mixed forest, which is defined in Annex 2.
3: There are 8 sustainable use areas with a total area of 65,717 hectares, including the first and second sustainable use areas are located in Or Buon Leu and Nang Khileuk communes, the third sustainable use area is geographical. Located in Sre Huy Commune, Sre Sangkom Commune and Sok San Commune, the 4th, 5th and 6th Sustainable Use Areas are located in Pu Chrey Commune and the 7th and 8th Sustainable Areas are located in Krang Teis Commune. Annex 2.
