Mobile app "Memory" easy to study the history of the Khmer Rouge regime has been officially launched!
The mobile app and the "Memory" website make it easy for the public, students, scholars and tourists to locate historical sites during the Khmer Rouge regime. The site also features videos from the past that relate to the daily activities of the people during the Khmer Rouge regime by survivors.
The "Memories" mobile app and website not only reveal the history of the Khmer Rouge regime, but also promote dialogue and reconciliation in intergenerational generations (people who went through the Khmer Rouge regime and people who were born later). The Khmer Rouge regime) through the use of information technology.
According to Ung Bun E, Acting Director of the Department of Media and Communication, the students' efforts to develop mobile applications and the "Memory" website of the Department of Media and Communication for the public will make it easier to read. Study, research and encourage the younger generation to become more interested in studying the history of the Khmer Rouge regime.
Topics on the Khmer Rouge regime have been carefully produced and presented in a multi-media format that can be used in two platforms: mobile applications and websites. Khmer Rouge history is a recurring theme for our students during their studies. The Department of Media and Communications considers it important to continue the conversation about Khmer Rouge history.
He said that many problems in Cambodian society today are rooted in the tragedy that occurred during the Khmer Rouge regime. The younger generation must learn from Cambodia's past to understand that the past has influenced their lives and society today. Conversation is an important tool for public learning and reconciling the past with the present.
