Ministry of Environment: Air quality in Cambodia is good, not affected by the effects of neighboring countries
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Environment claims that the air quality in Phnom Penh as well as throughout Cambodia is good, there is no bad air impact from neighboring countries.
The Ministry of Environment also called on the Cambodian people not to worry, and the Ministry will provide regular information if there are any significant issues related to air quality.
The Ministry of Environment's statement confirming the wind condition came after a Facebook message was leaked, claiming that Cambodia was being affected by bad weather from Thailand.
It should be noted that in the last few months, Bangkok and four provinces of Thailand, namely Samut Prakan, Samut Sakhon, Nonthaburi and Nakhon Pathom have experienced air pollution, affecting the lives of people, especially roads. Breathing until the authorities announced that some schools and educational institutions are temporarily closed to protect the safety and health of children and students.
